371
00:35:08,293 --> 00:35:12,579
So I'm just going to go heel to hip and I'm just going to get up nice and tall.

372
00:35:12,859 --> 00:35:19,669
I'm going to raise my opposite hand and I'm just going to hold for 15 seconds and then I'm going to switch over to the other side.

373
00:35:19,969 --> 00:35:23,454
If you need to hold on to something for balance, that's OK.

374
00:35:23,734 --> 00:35:31,245
We're not going to get the same arm raise, but you can hold on and just make sure that we're nice and tall and that heel is touching the hip the whole time.

375
00:35:31,225 --> 00:35:35,577
For the elevated hamstring stretch, I'm just gonna use a bench, a box, a chair.

376
00:35:35,998 --> 00:35:37,983
I'm just gonna get my heel on there.

377
00:35:38,003 --> 00:35:40,510
That toe is pointed up towards the ceiling.

378
00:35:40,790 --> 00:35:42,856
And then I'm just gonna hinge from the hips.

379
00:35:43,137 --> 00:35:45,363
So I don't wanna lean forward and round my back.

380
00:35:45,643 --> 00:35:47,428
I'm just gonna lean forward.

381
00:35:47,408 --> 00:35:50,133
from the hips, keeping my back nice and straight.

382
00:35:50,454 --> 00:35:57,607
If you wanna reach down and touch your ankle or touch your toe, you can, but don't reach down and start to bend over from the back.

383
00:35:57,627 --> 00:36:02,717
So I like to just keep my hands here to make sure that I'm not rounding the upper back.

384
00:36:03,625 --> 00:36:07,494
and I'm just gonna hold 15 seconds, and then I'm gonna switch over to the other side.

385
00:36:07,515 --> 00:36:10,382
15 seconds on the other side as well.

386
00:36:10,522 --> 00:36:12,647
We should feel this stretch all in the hamstrings.

387
00:36:12,848 --> 00:36:14,271
So that is the back of the thigh.

388
00:36:14,512 --> 00:36:18,782
We'll feel it a little bit down into the calves, but we should feel it mostly hamstrings.

389
00:36:18,762 --> 00:36:22,489
For our adductor stretch, I'm just gonna go one leg out.

390
00:36:22,649 --> 00:36:25,054
I need to lock out this knee so I'm nice and straight.

391
00:36:25,414 --> 00:36:27,719
I'm gonna sit back onto my heel.

392
00:36:28,099 --> 00:36:29,662
So now look at this back foot.

393
00:36:29,682 --> 00:36:31,085
I'm not curling the toe under.

394
00:36:31,485 --> 00:36:35,573
I'm putting it down like this so the top of my foot is flat to the floor.

395
00:36:35,553 --> 00:36:38,996
and I'm gonna sit my hips back to that heel.

396
00:36:39,416 --> 00:36:44,781
Now from there, I can already feel a little bit of a stretch in the adductor.

397
00:36:45,082 --> 00:36:58,193
Now if you don't really try to square your chest towards the floor, now from there, if you don't feel a big stretch already, we're gonna come down to the elbows and we're just gonna hang out in this position for 15 seconds.

398
00:36:58,554 --> 00:37:03,298
All right, so I should feel that stretch all through the adductors, that's the inside of the leg.

399
00:37:03,278 --> 00:37:06,843
After 15 seconds, I'm going to switch over to that other side.

400
00:37:07,424 --> 00:37:08,125
Same thing.

401
00:37:08,446 --> 00:37:11,330
For my glute stretch, I'm going to pull this knee back.

402
00:37:11,631 --> 00:37:14,775
Now make sure that this other leg stays down on the floor.

403
00:37:15,056 --> 00:37:18,942
So I need my right knee and my right heel down through the ground.

404
00:37:19,242 --> 00:37:23,869
I'm not going to lift off and I'm just going to lay my head back and just pull

405
00:37:23,849 --> 00:37:51,477
this knee as far towards the chest as i can now a lot of you as you pull the tendency is to rise here because we're tight in the hip flexors if that's the case try to have somebody hold that leg down or strap it down with a band or just realize that you don't have that range of motion yet and you can only pull to right here but this is a glute stretch for this left leg but at the same time for a lot of you this will be a hip flexor stretch on that right side

406
00:37:51,457 --> 00:37:54,522
So I'm just going to pull back, hold for 15 seconds.

407
00:37:54,963 --> 00:38:01,074
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side, trying to get full range of motion with that other leg.

408
00:38:01,094 --> 00:38:04,119
So for our hip flexor stretch, make sure that we have something soft.

409
00:38:04,139 --> 00:38:06,303
I don't want you guys putting your knee on a hardwood.

410
00:38:06,543 --> 00:38:10,410
Make sure you have a pad or a soft floor to do this stretch on.

411
00:38:10,390 --> 00:38:12,192
So I'm just going to go on one knee.

412
00:38:12,253 --> 00:38:15,136
This knee is going to go 90 degrees.

413
00:38:15,217 --> 00:38:16,118
So I'm 90 there.

414
00:38:16,478 --> 00:38:19,262
My ankle is directly underneath that knee.

415
00:38:19,623 --> 00:38:21,926
Now from here, I just got to get up nice and tall.

416
00:38:22,286 --> 00:38:26,953
Some of you are already going to feel a stretch in the hip flexor because we're extra tight.

417
00:38:27,333 --> 00:38:30,317
Now from there, I'm just going to lean forward.

418
00:38:30,578 --> 00:38:33,361
So I should have this knee back behind the hip.

419
00:38:33,762 --> 00:38:38,929
And now from there, I'm just raising straight up and I'm going to hold.

420
00:38:39,533 --> 00:38:45,839
All right, so I feel a big stretch from here all the way down through the bottom of that hip flexor.

421
00:38:46,600 --> 00:38:50,344
After 15 seconds, I'm gonna switch over to that other side and do the same thing.

422
00:38:50,464 --> 00:38:55,769
For my calf stretch, I'm basically gonna do what they would call a downward dog in yoga.

423
00:38:56,130 --> 00:39:02,636
So I'm here, I'm gonna push back like this, I'm gonna straighten out my arms, and now I'm just gonna cross over.

424
00:39:03,037 --> 00:39:09,203
So I'm gonna put my left foot over that right foot, and I'm gonna try to get that right heel

425
00:39:09,183 --> 00:39:12,629
down towards the floor or as close as I can.

426
00:39:13,110 --> 00:39:19,542
So I do have a straight knee, so we're stretching out what's called the gastrocnemius, that's the outside calf muscle.

427
00:39:19,802 --> 00:39:25,993
So I shouldn't feel the stretch as much down in the ankle and the Achilles as we would on some of our hip mobility drills.

428
00:39:26,374 --> 00:39:30,702
We should feel it on the outside of that calf muscle.

429
00:39:31,508 --> 00:39:34,619
A lot of us aren't going to be able to get our heel all the way to the floor.

430
00:39:34,680 --> 00:39:35,402
That's okay.

431
00:39:35,764 --> 00:39:38,955
Just work on getting it down as low as we can.

432
00:39:39,437 --> 00:39:42,970
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side.

433
00:39:45,700 --> 00:39:47,283
So we're going to get through a foam roller circuit.

434
00:39:47,443 --> 00:39:49,127
I have a long roller from Skills.

435
00:39:49,387 --> 00:39:56,260
You can do long or you can do one of the shorter rollers that you can get from Skills online, or you can just get it from Walmart or Target.

436
00:39:56,621 --> 00:40:01,971
So the first muscle that we're going to focus on is the glutes, one of the most important muscles for us to foam roll.

437
00:40:01,951 --> 00:40:05,115
So you can either go this way or you can go vertical.

438
00:40:05,475 --> 00:40:14,607
So if you go this way, we're just going to lean over to one side and then I'm just going to roll from the bottom of my glute all the way up to the top of my glute.

439
00:40:14,627 --> 00:40:21,075
Now, always, if we want more pressure, we could cross over here and add a little more pressure to make it a little tougher.

440
00:40:21,776 --> 00:40:28,144
Or we could go vertical here and then we could lean over and get the glute horizontally as well.

441
00:40:28,124 --> 00:40:30,448
So the next one, we're going to move down the posterior chain.

442
00:40:30,468 --> 00:40:31,890
We're going to focus on the hamstrings.

443
00:40:32,230 --> 00:40:40,603
So I'm just going to sit on the roller, and I'm going to cross over this foot, and I'm just going to roll from the bottom of my glute all the way to the top of my knee.

444
00:40:41,004 --> 00:40:52,782
So I'm just going to start in the center, and then I'm gradually going to rock over a little bit so I can get the outside of my hamstrings, and then I'm going to rock to the inside so I can get the inside of my hamstrings.

445
00:40:53,015 --> 00:40:54,777
Now the next one we're going to do is the calves.

446
00:40:55,077 --> 00:40:58,502
So we're just going to cross over and I'm going to push myself up.

447
00:40:58,582 --> 00:41:06,792
So my hips are off the ground and I'm just going to roll basically from the bottom of the knee all the way up to the top of the ankle.

448
00:41:06,852 --> 00:41:10,596
So we're going over that calf and also over that Achilles.

449
00:41:11,037 --> 00:41:12,398
And our next one we're flipping over.

450
00:41:12,458 --> 00:41:15,602
We're going hip flexor all the way down to the quad.

451
00:41:15,662 --> 00:41:22,971
So I'm going to go on the side of the roller now and I'm just going to come down into a plank position and I'm going to roll

452
00:41:22,951 --> 00:41:29,261
from that hip flexor all the way down towards the top of my thigh.

453
00:41:29,982 --> 00:41:32,967
So I'm getting my whole quad in this one.

454
00:41:33,408 --> 00:41:38,657
And if you can't get down to the quad muscles around your knee, then start here and finish.

455
00:41:39,117 --> 00:41:45,668
And then you would scoot up and then just focus on those lower quad muscles down around the knee.

456
00:41:45,648 --> 00:41:48,553
Our next one's gonna be for the adductors, that's the inside of the leg.

457
00:41:48,734 --> 00:41:50,457
So a lot of different ways that we can do this.

458
00:41:50,777 --> 00:42:04,602
The way that I like to go is I like to just turn that roller here, come in a plank position, bring this foot up, and I'm just rolling from the inside, the top of the knee, all the way up through the groin area.

459
00:42:06,320 --> 00:42:13,154
So we could go bent leg there or we could go straight leg there for a little bit deeper of a roll.

460
00:42:13,354 --> 00:42:16,921
So after we're done with the foam rolling circuit, I like to get out a lacrosse ball.

461
00:42:17,202 --> 00:42:20,469
You could use a golf ball, a baseball, anything hard.

462
00:42:21,030 --> 00:42:23,715
And I'm just gonna really dig into that heel.

463
00:42:23,735 --> 00:42:25,419
So I'm gonna apply some pressure in there.

464
00:42:25,719 --> 00:42:27,062
I'm gonna go from the heel

465
00:42:27,042 --> 00:42:32,653
all the way down through the ball of the foot, and I'm going to really loosen up that fascia.

466
00:42:33,215 --> 00:42:40,991
A lot of times our fascia of the feet take a lot of excess stress because we're on our feet all day, we're moving, we're cutting, we're jumping.

467
00:42:41,311 --> 00:42:44,157
We got to really start to loosen that up.

468
00:42:45,503 --> 00:42:50,155
Now after that, it's optional if you want to go up and work on the smaller muscles of the hip.

469
00:42:50,416 --> 00:42:53,945
You can work on the smaller muscles of the shoulder up against a wall if you'd like to.

470
00:42:53,965 --> 00:42:59,138
I just want to make sure that we get that foam roll circuit and we get that lacrosse ball on the feet.

471
00:42:59,519 --> 00:43:01,183
Everything else is extra credit.

472
00:43:14,984 --> 00:43:18,050
So for our hamstring floss, we're just gonna go lying on our back.

473
00:43:18,411 --> 00:43:27,909
I wanna make sure that my left leg stays down, so I'm actively pushing this left knee through the ground, pushing my left heel down through the ground, and I'm just gonna pull back.

474
00:43:28,009 --> 00:43:35,524
So here in this position, I'm gonna feel a little bit of a stretch in my glute, a little bit of a stretch in that opposite hip flexor, and then I'm just

475
00:43:35,504 --> 00:43:39,234
Extending that knee and coming back into flexion.

476
00:43:39,254 --> 00:43:41,119
So it's extension, flexion.

477
00:43:41,240 --> 00:43:43,406
So we call this hamstring floss.

478
00:43:43,727 --> 00:43:47,898
We're gradually trying to get that range of motion bigger and bigger.

479
00:43:48,279 --> 00:43:51,488
In each rep, we're trying to extend that knee more and more.

480
00:44:05,423 --> 00:44:09,007
So for the supine kickover, supine means facing up.

481
00:44:09,187 --> 00:44:15,354
So we're laying on our back, and I'm just gonna kick over this way, so I'm basically swinging my leg across.

482
00:44:15,795 --> 00:44:22,302
I am trying to keep that knee as straight as I can, and I'm just gonna tap that toe as high as I can, okay?

483
00:44:22,322 --> 00:44:27,988
And then I'm gonna bring it back the other way, and I'm gonna tap my toe on this side as high as I can.

484
00:44:27,968 --> 00:44:31,715
Okay, so it's over the body and then open it up.

485
00:44:31,815 --> 00:44:33,759
And we're just getting a gradual swing.

486
00:44:34,240 --> 00:44:39,570
Each rep, try to loosen up more and more and really swing that foot as high as we can.

487
00:44:39,710 --> 00:44:48,407
You're going to feel a big stretch on the outside of the hips and I'm going to feel a big stretch on the inside of the legs when I'm opening up to that side.

488
00:45:00,959 --> 00:45:07,394
For our PNF v-sit, basically what I'm gonna do is I'm gonna go in a v-sit position.

489
00:45:07,634 --> 00:45:11,322
I can put my hands down on the floor and I'm gonna sit up as high as I can.

490
00:45:11,423 --> 00:45:16,875
So the first part of this drill is we're gonna actively push our legs as hard as I can.

491
00:45:16,855 --> 00:45:20,280
down into the ground, and you're gonna hold that for seven seconds.

492
00:45:20,340 --> 00:45:29,094
So it's push as hard as you can, you gotta really contract your hamstrings, contract your glutes, and push down into the ground like you're trying to lift your body off the ground.

493
00:45:29,775 --> 00:45:37,227
After seven seconds, get up nice and tall, take a deep breath, and we're just relaxing and stretching down the center.

494
00:45:37,207 --> 00:45:39,871
So I want to get as far forward as I can.

495
00:45:40,151 --> 00:45:42,275
I'm not going to have a big rounded back.

496
00:45:42,335 --> 00:45:46,441
I do want to keep my shoulder blades pinched together and my back nice and flat.

497
00:45:46,802 --> 00:45:49,085
And then I'm just reaching forward as far as I can.

498
00:45:49,105 --> 00:45:51,469
I'm going to hold for 10 seconds.

499
00:45:51,489 --> 00:45:53,311
Now that's one rep.

500
00:45:53,351 --> 00:45:55,535
To finish this set, we need three reps.

501
00:45:55,595 --> 00:45:56,616
So then I'm right back in.

502
00:45:57,117 --> 00:45:57,918
Nice and tall.

503
00:45:58,159 --> 00:45:59,681
Push down as hard as I can.

504
00:45:59,901 --> 00:46:00,402
Seven.

505
00:46:00,803 --> 00:46:01,364
Relax.

506
00:46:01,564 --> 00:46:03,226
Breathe nice and deep.

507
00:46:03,246 --> 00:46:04,328
And then stretch.

508
00:46:04,308 --> 00:46:05,089
down the middle.

509
00:46:05,369 --> 00:46:08,453
If you do want to go for your toes, you could do that as well.

510
00:46:08,493 --> 00:46:10,395
You're still going to be stretching the same muscles.

511
00:46:10,736 --> 00:46:18,425
So you could grab your ankles, pull yourself forward, or you could grab your toes and pull yourself forward as long as you're not rounding that back.

512
00:46:18,886 --> 00:46:24,132
So the contraction allows our muscles to then relax more afterwards.

513
00:46:24,352 --> 00:46:27,075
So that's any type of PNF stretching.

514
00:46:27,115 --> 00:46:34,264
You're going to get more range of motion because our muscles are contracting and always after a hard muscle contraction,

515
00:46:34,244 --> 00:46:37,236
The muscles are primed for that relaxation.

516
00:46:37,256 --> 00:46:42,718
So then when you take a big breath and we relax and stretch, we're going to get a little further than we normally would.

517
00:47:17,495 --> 00:47:21,243
For the 90-90 hip opener, I'm just gonna start in a 90-90 position.

518
00:47:21,343 --> 00:47:32,588
So that means I'm sitting here, I'm gonna roll over towards my left glute, and I'm gonna get in a 90 degree position with that knee, and then this back leg is also gonna be 90 degrees.

519
00:47:33,008 --> 00:47:37,478
So we have 90 here, we have 90 here, and we have 90 here.

520
00:47:37,745 --> 00:47:41,631
Okay, from there, I'm going to square my chest with this knee.

521
00:47:42,072 --> 00:47:43,494
So I'm nice and tall right here.

522
00:47:43,934 --> 00:47:46,378
Now from there, my left hand is back.

523
00:47:46,759 --> 00:47:49,202
I'm going to thread my right arm underneath.

524
00:47:49,803 --> 00:47:52,347
And the ultimate goal is to get the right shoulder down to the floor.

525
00:47:52,668 --> 00:47:56,413
A lot of you might not have that mobility yet, but just get as low as we can comfortably.

526
00:47:56,794 --> 00:47:58,016
So I'm going to thread through.

527
00:47:58,036 --> 00:48:01,902
One, two.

528
00:48:02,523 --> 00:48:04,085
And then I'm going to roll to the next side.

529
00:48:04,205 --> 00:48:05,507
So hand down.

530
00:48:06,061 --> 00:48:15,282
I get into this position, same thing, 90, 90, 90, and then I thread my left hand through, shoulder to the ground.

531
00:48:15,683 --> 00:48:22,078
I should feel that stretch sort of in the outside of the hip, and we're just going to flow straight through.

532
00:48:26,446 --> 00:48:32,273
Okay, so after the desired reps there, then I'm going back to my original position, 90-90.

533
00:48:32,633 --> 00:48:34,475
I'm gonna have both hands on the floor.

534
00:48:34,515 --> 00:48:36,598
I'm gonna keep this leg grounded.

535
00:48:36,638 --> 00:48:43,465
I cannot lift this knee or this ankle off the ground, and I'm just gonna raise as high as I can and back down.

536
00:48:43,826 --> 00:48:44,967
So now it's just an opener.

537
00:48:46,108 --> 00:48:49,212
A lot of you will go here, and the tendency is to open up here.

538
00:48:49,272 --> 00:48:50,514
We gotta stay grounded.

539
00:48:50,954 --> 00:48:55,339
My goal is to get the sole of that foot flat on the floor.

540
00:48:55,960 --> 00:49:00,206
So I want to get all the way flat if possible and back down.

541
00:49:01,168 --> 00:49:03,851
After the desired reps, I'm flowing straight through.

542
00:49:03,912 --> 00:49:07,697
Same thing, I'm down and open.

543
00:49:10,601 --> 00:49:13,425
We should feel that stretch on the opener in here.

544
00:49:13,646 --> 00:49:17,992
So inside of the leg that's grounded, inside of the leg that's moving as well.

545
00:49:19,114 --> 00:49:21,377
Really opening up those hips.

546
00:49:37,591 --> 00:49:41,017
For the hip flexor tilt, I'm just gonna use a box of bench or a chair.

547
00:49:41,718 --> 00:49:46,547
I'm gonna get my back foot up so the top of my foot is on the bench.

548
00:49:46,607 --> 00:49:48,190
I'm not gonna go with my toe on the bench.

549
00:49:48,590 --> 00:49:51,135
Top of the foot on the bench, I'm just gonna come down.

550
00:49:51,455 --> 00:49:55,903
Now I wanna get my heel touching my hips or as close as I can get to that.

551
00:49:55,883 --> 00:49:57,865
If you have a pad, that'd be better.

552
00:49:57,905 --> 00:49:59,207
I wouldn't do this on hardwood.

553
00:49:59,387 --> 00:50:01,069
Make sure you got a nice, soft surface.

554
00:50:01,569 --> 00:50:02,330
So I'm touching.

555
00:50:02,731 --> 00:50:06,595
I'm in a straight line from my knee all the way up through my shoulders.

556
00:50:07,136 --> 00:50:08,297
And I'm just going to sit here.

557
00:50:08,437 --> 00:50:09,999
First, I'm going to get in a good position.

558
00:50:10,499 --> 00:50:12,442
This ankle should be under that knee.

559
00:50:13,102 --> 00:50:16,907
I should already feel a little bit of a stretch in that hip flexor, a little bit in the quad as well.

560
00:50:17,327 --> 00:50:19,810
Now from here, I'm getting nice and wide.

561
00:50:19,850 --> 00:50:21,011
I'm not going to lean forward.

562
00:50:21,352 --> 00:50:23,494
And I'm going arms out.

563
00:50:23,474 --> 00:50:52,266
and together now at the top with straight elbows not bent elbows at the top I'm going to lean towards the lead leg so that's to my right as far as I can hold for five and then come right back okay and then we're hands down all the way up hands together nice and tall elongate through the spine and lean towards that lead leg three two one

564
00:50:52,313 --> 00:50:54,898
back down, and we're back through.

565
00:51:14,386 --> 00:51:18,816
For the kneeling adductor pulse, I'm gonna go half kneel position.

566
00:51:19,437 --> 00:51:22,083
I'm going to point the toe out so I'm not curled.

567
00:51:22,284 --> 00:51:23,286
I'm pointed like this.

568
00:51:23,326 --> 00:51:26,353
Top of the foot is down towards the floor.

569
00:51:27,683 --> 00:51:30,046
I'm gonna go straight out with this leg.

570
00:51:30,067 --> 00:51:32,009
This knee's gonna be nice and straight.

571
00:51:32,029 --> 00:51:34,413
Okay, from here, I'm gonna do some rocks.

572
00:51:34,433 --> 00:51:35,915
So I'm gonna rock straight back.

573
00:51:36,496 --> 00:51:40,682
I need my hips to touch my heels or as close as you can.

574
00:51:41,183 --> 00:51:46,010
And you're gonna really feel that stretch in the adductor and you'll feel a certain angle in that adductor.

575
00:51:46,070 --> 00:51:49,395
And now we're gonna switch that angle by rocking forward.

576
00:51:49,716 --> 00:51:54,062
So I'm gonna rock back one second and then I'm gonna creep the hands forward

