01:16:48,966 --> 01:16:51,330
I want the back leg parallel to the floor.

812
01:16:51,350 --> 01:16:53,995
I want my torso parallel to the floor.

813
01:16:54,536 --> 01:16:56,359
First, let's just hold in this position.

814
01:16:56,720 --> 01:16:59,565
And if this is hard for you, then just hold here and let's work on that.

815
01:17:00,005 --> 01:17:05,455
Now, if you can, we're gonna go arm straight and I'm gonna turn as high as I can.

816
01:17:05,435 --> 01:17:31,628
ideally getting my hand pointed up to the ceiling and then I'm coming back down and I'm going the other side this side is a lot harder for most people and we're back down switch to the other side and I'm just gonna rep out there now for a lot of you that's gonna be too difficult off the bat so if that's the case then let's just hold in this position and we'll just go for 25 seconds

817
01:17:32,317 --> 01:17:34,044
And just focus on getting that stability.

818
01:17:34,084 --> 01:17:38,561
Now, if that's too easy and the other version is too hard, then just go baby turns.

819
01:17:38,581 --> 01:17:41,432
So just start to work on turning the shoulders a little bit.

820
01:17:41,918 --> 01:17:45,144
We're adding a little bit of chaos to that single leg stability.

821
01:17:45,465 --> 01:17:49,573
And then gradually over time, day after day, we're going bigger and bigger.

822
01:17:49,994 --> 01:17:58,250
If we can stabilize in this position and add chaos to that single leg stability and start to get big turns, we're going to be very, very stable on one leg.

823
01:17:58,531 --> 01:18:02,779
And that's going to show up in our cuts, in our vertical jump, and in our speed.

824
01:18:05,392 --> 01:18:09,157
So the first thing we're gonna do for our dynamic warmup is stationary skips.

