2268
03:38:27,452 --> 03:38:34,963
We're not going to get the same arm raise, but you can hold on and just make sure that we're nice and tall and that heel is touching the hip the whole time.

2269
03:38:34,943 --> 03:38:39,294
For the elevated hamstring stretch, I'm just gonna use a bench, a box, a chair.

2270
03:38:39,715 --> 03:38:41,680
I'm just gonna get my heel on there.

2271
03:38:42,020 --> 03:38:44,226
That toe is pointed up towards the ceiling.

2272
03:38:44,507 --> 03:38:46,572
And then I'm just gonna hinge from the hips.

2273
03:38:46,852 --> 03:38:49,058
So I don't wanna lean forward and round my back.

2274
03:38:49,379 --> 03:38:51,163
I'm just gonna lean forward.

2275
03:38:51,143 --> 03:38:53,848
from the hips, keeping my back nice and straight.

2276
03:38:54,188 --> 03:39:01,181
If you wanna reach down and touch your ankle or touch your toe, you can, but don't reach down and start to bend over from the back.

2277
03:39:01,361 --> 03:39:06,170
So I like to just keep my hands here to make sure that I'm not rounding the upper back.

2278
03:39:07,492 --> 03:39:11,920
And I'm just gonna hold 15 seconds, and then I'm gonna switch over to the other side.

2279
03:39:12,237 --> 03:39:14,100
15 seconds on the other side as well.

2280
03:39:14,220 --> 03:39:16,363
We should feel this stretch all in the hamstrings.

2281
03:39:16,544 --> 03:39:17,986
So that is the back of the thigh.

2282
03:39:18,206 --> 03:39:22,413
We'll feel it a little bit down into the calves, but we should feel it mostly hamstrings.

2283
03:39:22,533 --> 03:39:26,218
For our adductor stretch, I'm just gonna go one leg out.

2284
03:39:26,379 --> 03:39:28,802
I need to lock out this knee so I'm nice and straight.

2285
03:39:29,163 --> 03:39:31,466
I'm gonna sit back onto my heel.

2286
03:39:31,827 --> 03:39:33,409
So now look at this back foot.

2287
03:39:33,430 --> 03:39:35,072
I'm not curling the toe under.

2288
03:39:35,052 --> 03:39:38,897
I'm putting it down like this so the top of my foot is flat to the floor.

2289
03:39:39,478 --> 03:39:42,722
And I'm going to sit my hips back to that heel.

2290
03:39:43,142 --> 03:39:48,509
Now from there, I can already feel a little bit of a stretch in the adductor.

2291
03:39:48,810 --> 03:40:02,207
Now if you don't really try to square your chest towards the floor, now from there, if you don't feel a big stretch already, we're going to come down to the elbows and we're just going to hang out in this position for 15 seconds.

2292
03:40:02,187 --> 03:40:05,353
Alright, so I should feel that stretch all through the adductors.

2293
03:40:05,373 --> 03:40:06,716
That's the inside of the leg.

2294
03:40:07,197 --> 03:40:10,564
After 15 seconds, I'm gonna switch over to that other side.

2295
03:40:11,165 --> 03:40:11,846
Same thing.

2296
03:40:12,187 --> 03:40:15,073
For my glute stretch, I'm gonna pull this knee back.

2297
03:40:15,373 --> 03:40:18,660
Now make sure that this other leg stays down on the floor.

2298
03:40:18,640 --> 03:40:22,627
So I need my right knee and my right heel down through the ground.

2299
03:40:22,948 --> 03:40:30,581
I'm not going to lift off and I'm just going to lay my head back and just pull this knee as far towards the chest as I can.

2300
03:40:30,961 --> 03:40:36,451
Now, a lot of you, as you pull, the tendency is to rise here because we're tight in the hip flexors.

2301
03:40:36,852 --> 03:40:42,201
If that's the case, try to have somebody hold that leg down or strap it down with a band.

2302
03:40:42,181 --> 03:40:46,887
or just realize that you don't have that range of motion yet and you can only pull to right here.

2303
03:40:47,307 --> 03:40:54,957
But this is a glute stretch for this left leg, but at the same time, for a lot of you, this will be a hip flexor stretch on that right side.

2304
03:40:55,458 --> 03:40:58,261
So I'm just gonna pull back, hold for 15 seconds.

2305
03:40:58,702 --> 03:41:04,729
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side, trying to get full range of motion with that other leg.

2306
03:41:04,709 --> 03:41:07,792
So for our hip flexor stretch, make sure that we have something soft.

2307
03:41:07,832 --> 03:41:10,014
I don't want you guys putting your knee on a hardwood.

2308
03:41:10,234 --> 03:41:13,897
Make sure you have a pad or a soft floor to do this stretch on.

2309
03:41:14,378 --> 03:41:15,919
So I'm just going to go on one knee.

2310
03:41:16,340 --> 03:41:18,862
This knee is going to go 90 degrees.

2311
03:41:18,942 --> 03:41:19,883
So I'm 90 there.

2312
03:41:20,203 --> 03:41:22,986
My ankle is directly underneath that knee.

2313
03:41:23,366 --> 03:41:25,628
Now from here, I just got to get up nice and tall.

2314
03:41:26,009 --> 03:41:30,693
Some of you are already going to feel a stretch in the hip flexor because we're extra tight.

2315
03:41:31,053 --> 03:41:34,176
Now from there, I'm just going to lean forward.

2316
03:41:34,156 --> 03:41:37,443
So I should have this knee back behind the hip.

2317
03:41:37,463 --> 03:41:42,232
And now from there, I'm just raising straight up and I'm going to hold.

2318
03:41:42,252 --> 03:41:43,675
All right.

2319
03:41:43,715 --> 03:41:49,607
So I feel a big stretch from here all the way down through the bottom of that hip flexor.

2320
03:41:50,348 --> 03:41:54,156
After 15 seconds, I'm going to switch over to that other side and do the same thing.

2321
03:41:54,136 --> 03:41:59,466
For my calf stretch, I'm basically going to do what they would call a downward dog in yoga.

2322
03:41:59,847 --> 03:42:03,073
So I'm here, I'm going to push back like this.

2323
03:42:03,173 --> 03:42:06,359
I'm going to straighten out my arms and now I'm just going to cross over.

2324
03:42:06,740 --> 03:42:16,498
So I'm going to put my left foot over that right foot and I'm going to try to get that right heel down towards the floor or as close as I can.

2325
03:42:16,478 --> 03:42:23,508
So I do have a straight knee, so we're stretching out what's called the gastrocnemius, that's the outside calf muscle.

2326
03:42:23,528 --> 03:42:29,676
So I shouldn't feel the stretch as much down in the ankle and the Achilles as we would on some of our hip mobility drills.

2327
03:42:30,077 --> 03:42:34,403
We should feel it on the outside of that calf muscle.

2328
03:42:35,227 --> 03:42:38,355
A lot of us aren't going to be able to get our heel all the way to the floor.

2329
03:42:38,396 --> 03:42:39,117
That's okay.

2330
03:42:39,478 --> 03:42:42,687
Just work on getting it down as low as we can.

2331
03:42:42,727 --> 03:42:46,738
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side.

2332
03:42:49,570 --> 03:42:50,251
What's up guys?

2333
03:42:50,411 --> 03:42:53,795
Quick minimum dose advice for phase three, day three.

2334
03:42:54,455 --> 03:42:56,277
Already a very short workout.

2335
03:42:56,577 --> 03:43:03,405
If you have to cut back, cut out the foam roller circuit, do the dynamic warm-up, cut out the box drop crossover step.

2336
03:43:03,745 --> 03:43:06,768
Love this exercise, but if you're in a rush, take that out.

2337
03:43:07,149 --> 03:43:10,372
You could take out the non-counter movement one leg pistol jump.

2338
03:43:10,893 --> 03:43:13,175
Always do the versatile jump drill.

2339
03:43:13,455 --> 03:43:16,759
We need this for building skill in our jump.

2340
03:43:16,739 --> 03:43:19,685
10-minute freestyle dunk session, always have to have it.

2341
03:43:20,166 --> 03:43:23,512
If you can't get to a court, just do it in your living room.

2342
03:43:23,653 --> 03:43:24,775
Do it wherever you can.

2343
03:43:25,136 --> 03:43:36,558
Literally just run as far as you can and jump high, whether that is a full three-point line run or that's just you in your living room taking four steps and jumping as high as you can.

2344
03:43:37,119 --> 03:43:38,983
Whatever you can get, let's do it.

2345
03:43:38,963 --> 03:43:42,309
Dratch RFESS, definitely do this.

2346
03:43:42,569 --> 03:43:45,114
We gotta build that concentric power.

2347
03:43:45,454 --> 03:43:47,418
We're getting the tendons and the muscles involved.

2348
03:43:47,778 --> 03:43:49,461
Never skip that exercise.

2349
03:43:49,782 --> 03:43:54,610
And then if you wanna skip the static stretch, I'm fine with that as long as you're already flexible.

2350
03:43:54,951 --> 03:43:55,572
Let's do it.

2351
03:43:55,552 --> 03:43:57,235
So we're going to get through a foam roller circuit.

2352
03:43:57,395 --> 03:43:59,098
I have a long roller from Skills.

2353
03:43:59,338 --> 03:44:06,210
You can do long or you can do one of the shorter rollers that you can get from Skills online, or you can just get it from Walmart or Target.

2354
03:44:06,571 --> 03:44:11,940
So the first muscle that we're going to focus on is the glutes, one of the most important muscles for us to foam roll.

2355
03:44:11,920 --> 03:44:15,084
So you can either go this way or you can go vertical.

2356
03:44:15,424 --> 03:44:24,576
So if you go this way, we're just going to lean over to one side and then I'm just going to roll from the bottom of my glute all the way up to the top of my glute.

2357
03:44:24,596 --> 03:44:31,024
Now, always, if we want more pressure, we can cross over here and add a little more pressure to make it a little tougher.

2358
03:44:31,725 --> 03:44:38,113
Or we could go vertical here and then we can lean over and get the glute horizontally as well.

2359
03:44:38,093 --> 03:44:40,397
So the next one we're going to move down the posterior chain.

2360
03:44:40,437 --> 03:44:41,839
We're going to focus on the hamstrings.

2361
03:44:42,179 --> 03:44:50,592
So I'm just going to sit on the roller and I'm going to cross over this foot and I'm just going to roll from the bottom of my glute all the way to the top of my knee.

2362
03:44:50,953 --> 03:45:02,751
So I'm just going to start in the center and then I'm gradually going to rock over a little bit so I can get the outside of my hamstrings and then I'm going to rock to the inside so I can get the inside of my hamstrings.

2363
03:45:02,967 --> 03:45:04,749
Now the next one we're gonna do is the calves.

2364
03:45:05,049 --> 03:45:16,761
So we're just gonna cross over and I'm gonna push myself up so my hips are off the ground and I'm just gonna roll basically from the bottom of the knee all the way up to the top of the ankle.

2365
03:45:16,821 --> 03:45:20,585
So we're going over that calf and also over that Achilles.

2366
03:45:20,985 --> 03:45:25,590
And our next one we're flipping over, we're going hip flexor all the way down to the quad.

2367
03:45:25,610 --> 03:45:32,957
So I'm gonna go on the side of the roller now and I'm just gonna come down into a plank position and I'm gonna roll

2368
03:45:32,937 --> 03:45:39,209
from that hip flexor all the way down towards the top of my thigh.

2369
03:45:39,930 --> 03:45:42,916
So I'm getting my whole quad in this one.

2370
03:45:43,357 --> 03:45:48,607
And if you can't get down to the quad muscles around your knee, then start here and finish.

2371
03:45:49,068 --> 03:45:55,620
And then you would scoot up and then just focus on those lower quad muscles down around the knee.

2372
03:45:55,600 --> 03:45:58,506
Our next one's going to be for the adductors, that's the inside of the leg.

2373
03:45:58,687 --> 03:46:00,410
So a lot of different ways that we can do this.

2374
03:46:00,751 --> 03:46:14,520
The way that I like to go is I like to just turn that roller here, come in a plank position, bring this foot up, and I'm just rolling from the inside, the top of the knee, all the way up through the groin area.

2375
03:46:16,289 --> 03:46:23,100
So we could go bent leg there or we could go straight leg there for a little bit deeper of a roll.

2376
03:46:23,300 --> 03:46:26,846
So after we're done with the foam rolling circuit, I like to get out a lacrosse ball.

2377
03:46:27,167 --> 03:46:30,432
You could use a golf ball, a baseball, anything hard.

2378
03:46:30,973 --> 03:46:33,657
And I'm just going to really dig into that heel.

2379
03:46:33,677 --> 03:46:35,360
So I'm going to apply some pressure in there.

2380
03:46:35,660 --> 03:46:39,867
I'm going to go from the heel all the way down through the ball of the foot.

2381
03:46:39,847 --> 03:46:42,614
and I'm gonna really loosen up that fascia.

2382
03:46:43,175 --> 03:46:54,143
A lot of times our fascia of the feet take a lot of excess stress because we're on our feet all day, we're moving, we're cutting, we're jumping, we gotta really start to loosen that up.

2383
03:46:55,473 --> 03:47:00,126
Now after that, it's optional if you want to go up and work on the smaller muscles of the hip.

2384
03:47:00,366 --> 03:47:03,896
You can work on the smaller muscles of the shoulder up against a wall if you'd like to.

2385
03:47:03,916 --> 03:47:09,110
I just want to make sure that we get that foam low circuit and we get that lacrosse ball on the feet.

2386
03:47:09,471 --> 03:47:11,136
Everything else is extra credit.

2387
03:47:14,221 --> 03:47:17,989
So the first thing we're gonna do for our dynamic warmup is stationary skips.

2388
03:47:18,250 --> 03:47:20,856
Now for all of these, you can take them on the move if you want.

2389
03:47:20,916 --> 03:47:24,865
For right now, I'm just gonna do them stationary just in case you don't have much room.

2390
03:47:25,386 --> 03:47:32,061
So we're just going up with the right, up with the left, just like we're running, and vice versa on that other side.

2391
03:47:32,041 --> 03:47:55,585
all right i'm staying stiff with the feet so i'm not letting my heel collapse i want to stay on the ball of the foot and i'm just going to go about 50 of my max speed i'm not going too fast yet we're going to go for 30 seconds on the skips for the seal jacks it's basically like a jumping jack except i'm going to coordinate arms with the legs so i'm going to go over with the right and over with the right hand at the same time back to neutral

2392
03:47:55,565 --> 03:47:58,091
over with the left, over with the left hand.

2393
03:47:58,411 --> 03:48:00,536
And then I'm just going to speed that up.

2394
03:48:00,556 --> 03:48:07,291
I'm going to get a good little rhythm going here, maybe somewhere between 30 and 50% of your max speed.

2395
03:48:07,351 --> 03:48:08,374
So we're not all out.

2396
03:48:08,815 --> 03:48:10,398
We're just getting that blood flowing.

2397
03:48:10,699 --> 03:48:12,122
We're going to go for 30 seconds.

2398
03:48:12,102 --> 03:48:16,548
For the over-under hamstring stretch, I'm just gonna go over with the left leg.

2399
03:48:16,868 --> 03:48:18,651
I'm gonna come down, touch the toe.

2400
03:48:18,751 --> 03:48:28,003
Now, if you can't touch the toe without rounding the back, then just go mid-shin or even to the knees, just as low as we can, but we don't wanna go to the point where we have to round our back.

2401
03:48:28,524 --> 03:48:36,034
Okay, so I'm gonna get down, touch my toes, back to neutral, and then I cross over the other way, and I'm going the other side.

2402
03:48:39,693 --> 03:48:44,059
All right, we're gonna go five over and back, so it's 10 total touches.

2403
03:48:44,260 --> 03:48:49,608
For the quad hamstring leans, I'm just gonna go into a quad stretch, so I'm gonna pull my right foot up.

2404
03:48:49,868 --> 03:48:56,438
I wanna make sure that my heel is touching my hip in that position, and I'm not out like this, I'm keeping that knee in.

2405
03:48:56,858 --> 03:49:04,890
Now from there, I'm gonna keep the left knee straight, and I'm just gonna go into a lean as low as I can,

2406
03:49:04,870 --> 03:49:09,799
So I'm getting a really good stretch in the quad by going down and getting my knee back.

2407
03:49:10,140 --> 03:49:15,750
I'm getting it into the hip flexor a little bit more and I'm getting this hamstring a good stretch.

2408
03:49:16,431 --> 03:49:18,775
And I'm also working on my balance at the same time.

2409
03:49:19,116 --> 03:49:23,725
I'm going to go five leans and then I'm going to switch over five leans on the other side.

2410
03:49:24,366 --> 03:49:26,710
For the hip opener, we're going to go push up position.

2411
03:49:27,635 --> 03:49:31,263
I'm going to go left leg up outside this left hand.

2412
03:49:31,684 --> 03:49:34,049
Now from here, I'm just going to rotate up and hold.

2413
03:49:34,109 --> 03:49:36,134
One, two, three.

2414
03:49:36,194 --> 03:49:38,459
Now I'm going to go elbow down towards the floor.

2415
03:49:38,800 --> 03:49:40,804
We might not be able to touch the elbow to the ground.

2416
03:49:40,844 --> 03:49:41,446
That's okay.

2417
03:49:41,786 --> 03:49:43,370
Let's just get as low as we can there.

2418
03:49:43,851 --> 03:49:44,833
One, two, three.

2419
03:49:44,813 --> 03:49:46,515
three, and back up.

2420
03:49:46,575 --> 03:49:48,578
So three there, three there.

2421
03:49:48,919 --> 03:49:55,208
I'm gonna go five cycles and then I'm gonna switch to the other side, five and five, same thing.

2422
03:49:55,288 --> 03:49:58,752
For the adductor hip flexor combo, I'm going lateral with one skip.

2423
03:49:58,793 --> 03:50:02,738
So it's one skip lateral and I'm going down, I'm trying to touch this floor

2424
03:50:02,718 --> 03:50:07,908
Keep this knee straight because I want to get that stretch on the inside of the leg in this adductor.

2425
03:50:08,228 --> 03:50:15,141
I'm going back with the hip like I would in a normal squat, and I'm getting nice and low, touch the floor, and I'm popping out to that other side.

2426
03:50:15,622 --> 03:50:18,668
All right, so let's just hold about one second at the bottom.

2427
03:50:18,648 --> 03:50:40,318
and pop out i need five of these down and back so it's 10 total and then i immediately go into a hip flexor same thing with the skip and now i land i turn this foot forward i pivot i'm here knee a couple inches off the floor i'm gonna rotate hold one and then come back and it's to the other side

2428
03:50:45,260 --> 03:50:51,789
At the bottom of this stretch, I'm gonna get that really good stretch in the hip flexor, and I always need to turn towards the lead leg.

2429
03:50:51,809 --> 03:50:53,271
Don't make the mistake of going here.

2430
03:50:53,632 --> 03:51:01,703
You need to rotate towards that lead leg as far as we can, and I'm gonna feel it through that hip flexor, and then I pop out to the other side.

2431
03:51:01,803 --> 03:51:07,692
For the overhead deep squat progression, I'm going high with the hands, basic squat stance, so I'm a little wider than shoulder width.

2432
03:51:07,772 --> 03:51:11,537
I can point the toes out just a little bit, and then I'm just gonna go here,

2433
03:51:11,517 --> 03:51:13,340
It's going to be a hamstring stretch.

2434
03:51:13,601 --> 03:51:15,544
One, two, three.

2435
03:51:15,705 --> 03:51:18,690
Keep the hands down and come into a deep squat.

2436
03:51:18,851 --> 03:51:21,055
Try to stay back on your heels if you can.

2437
03:51:21,696 --> 03:51:23,419
One, two, three.

2438
03:51:23,479 --> 03:51:24,962
Rock forward.

2439
03:51:25,042 --> 03:51:26,084
So I'm on my toes now.

2440
03:51:26,585 --> 03:51:28,769
Drive the knees out with the elbows.

2441
03:51:28,849 --> 03:51:29,170
Hold.

2442
03:51:29,791 --> 03:51:30,893
One, two, three.

2443
03:51:30,873 --> 03:51:31,514
Three.

2444
03:51:31,855 --> 03:51:32,577
Rock it back.

2445
03:51:32,938 --> 03:51:34,722
Heels back down to the ground.

2446
03:51:35,002 --> 03:51:36,626
One, two, three.

2447
03:51:36,726 --> 03:51:37,929
I need one hand up.

2448
03:51:38,490 --> 03:51:39,272
Two hand up.

2449
03:51:39,512 --> 03:51:40,174
Not out here.

2450
03:51:40,234 --> 03:51:41,717
We need it back behind the head.

2451
03:51:42,298 --> 03:51:42,940
And stand.

2452
03:51:43,501 --> 03:51:43,742
Alright.

2453
03:51:44,203 --> 03:51:45,586
So that's one cycle.

2454
03:51:45,846 --> 03:51:46,949
We're going to go for three of these.

2455
03:51:47,911 --> 03:51:49,354
So it's one, two, three.

2456
03:51:49,672 --> 03:51:51,936
One, two, three, lean.

2457
03:51:52,717 --> 03:51:55,000
One, two, three, heels back down.

2458
03:51:55,060 --> 03:51:59,087
One, two, three, one up, two up, stand, all right?

2459
03:51:59,367 --> 03:52:04,135
If you cannot get down in that deep position, then let's just go as low as we can right here.

2460
03:52:04,515 --> 03:52:07,680
And then on the lean, it's just gonna look like this, all right?

2461
03:52:07,700 --> 03:52:08,862
And then we're gonna come back.

2462
03:52:08,842 --> 03:52:12,028
hopefully parallel to the floor, one up, two up stand.

2463
03:52:12,409 --> 03:52:18,742
We just gotta get as low as we can and every day try to progress so that we can get lower and lower, better range of motion.

2464
03:52:18,762 --> 03:52:21,608
So for the hip bridge, it's gonna be a very basic hip bridge.

2465
03:52:21,648 --> 03:52:24,133
Even if you're an advanced athlete, I want you to do this version.

2466
03:52:24,113 --> 03:52:27,117
So we're gonna get up nice and flat in a hip bridge.

2467
03:52:27,457 --> 03:52:29,139
I need to be flat through the hips.

2468
03:52:29,439 --> 03:52:36,788
I'm driving through my mid-foot right now, and now I'm just gonna squeeze my glutes together as hard as I possibly can.

2469
03:52:37,189 --> 03:52:50,965
So just holding in this position isn't that difficult, but if I squeeze my glutes together as hard as I can so they're rock solid, I'm gonna get a really good isometric contraction, and I'm gonna activate a lot of muscle fibers.

2470
03:52:51,417 --> 03:52:58,031
and we're just gonna hold in this position for 25 seconds with a full squeeze and then relax.

2471
03:52:58,452 --> 03:53:06,810
This is all for hip activation, getting those glutes fired up, it's the most powerful muscle in the body, so we gotta get them revved up for our session.

2472
03:53:26,264 --> 03:53:30,149
So for my box drop crossover step, I'm going to use a box.

2473
03:53:30,190 --> 03:53:31,672
This box is about knee height.

2474
03:53:31,972 --> 03:53:34,295
I wouldn't want to go too much higher than that to start.

2475
03:53:34,856 --> 03:53:36,579
And I'm going to start on the box.

2476
03:53:36,599 --> 03:53:37,660
I'm going to drop off.

2477
03:53:37,940 --> 03:53:40,364
So I'm not jumping off, I'm dropping off.

2478
03:53:40,384 --> 03:53:42,867
My feet are going to land at the same time.

2479
03:53:43,008 --> 03:53:46,112
So it's dangle one off, drop.

2480
03:53:46,092 --> 03:54:09,585
feet hit at the same time now as soon as my feet hit I got to use that energy from the floor from that stretch shortening cycle and push out laterally into that crossover step so my left foot stays anchored I cross over that right foot and then I plant and with this left foot this outside foot I got to push off as hard as I can and

2481
03:54:09,565 --> 03:54:13,291
use the floor like a springboard straight into my crossover step.

2482
03:54:13,311 --> 03:54:18,019
So now my right foot is the anchor foot, my left foot becomes the stride foot.

2483
03:54:18,480 --> 03:54:22,566
The reason I'm using this hurdle is accountability for my stride length.

2484
03:54:22,647 --> 03:54:24,790
So if we can get this up

2485
03:54:24,770 --> 03:54:40,517
pretty high say four maybe three or four feet away from that first hurdle now in this position I got to work on striding and getting that knee nice and high so we want to work on explosiveness but we also want to work on stride length now

2486
03:54:40,497 --> 03:54:45,571
You know you got this too far when you feel like you have to reach to get over.

2487
03:54:45,993 --> 03:54:52,110
We never want to reach because one, it's slow, and two, that leads to hamstring injuries.

2488
03:54:52,170 --> 03:54:55,941
Hamstring strains come from people reaching, all right?

2489
03:54:55,921 --> 03:55:05,460
I need you to get stride length but still strike that foot right in front of the center of gravity or right underneath the center of gravity.

2490
03:55:05,761 --> 03:55:11,432
I don't want you to be striking the foot out here and then having to pull your body forward.

2491
03:55:11,412 --> 03:55:17,098
So work on that stride length, but also pay attention to how you feel when that foot is landing.

2492
03:55:17,419 --> 03:55:24,326
You should feel more explosive on that next step and not less explosive like you're having to pull your center of gravity over that foot.

2493
03:55:24,627 --> 03:55:27,810
If you don't have the box, of course, we can always just jump.

2494
03:55:27,890 --> 03:55:31,074
So we can jump and then on landing we go from there.

2495
03:55:31,094 --> 03:55:34,197
We're going to get the same effect, same stretch reflex.

2496
03:56:27,451 --> 03:56:33,539
So for our versatile jump drill, basically what we're going to do is introduce three different directions on the jump.

2497
03:56:33,579 --> 03:56:36,883
So it's going to be a penultimate step into our max jump.

2498
03:56:36,943 --> 03:56:38,205
I want you to work on the turn.

2499
03:56:38,526 --> 03:56:44,353
So of course, penultimate, take that long stride, get that turn, take off as high as we can.

2500
03:56:44,393 --> 03:56:48,699
Now, as soon as you land, first of all, I need you to correct yourself in the air.

2501
03:56:48,719 --> 03:56:50,101
So I don't want you spinning in the air.

2502
03:56:50,121 --> 03:56:54,066
I want you to jump and I want you to land back in that square stance.

2503
03:56:54,046 --> 03:56:59,093
As soon as we land, we're using the ground as energy to burst off into a crossover step.

2504
03:56:59,173 --> 03:57:00,635
So now we're going lateral into a jump.

2505
03:57:01,015 --> 03:57:04,039
So I land from my regular penultimate max jump.

2506
03:57:04,820 --> 03:57:05,181
Boom.

2507
03:57:05,301 --> 03:57:06,362
Push straight over.

2508
03:57:06,423 --> 03:57:07,424
One, two.

2509
03:57:07,925 --> 03:57:08,826
Straight up in the air.

2510
03:57:08,866 --> 03:57:11,189
Really work on decelerating yourself.

2511
03:57:11,209 --> 03:57:12,310
I don't want you fading.

2512
03:57:12,671 --> 03:57:14,974
I want you to get a good stop.

2513
03:57:15,275 --> 03:57:16,577
and a straight vertical.

2514
03:57:17,038 --> 03:57:27,498
From here, again, I'm going to use the floor as a springboard, and I'm springing back over into that crossover one, two, straight up in the air, and stick that landing, okay?

2515
03:57:27,518 --> 03:57:29,121
That counts as one rep.

2516
03:57:29,141 --> 03:57:33,449
So it was penultimate, lateral to the left, lateral to the right.

2517
03:57:33,750 --> 03:57:36,996
That's three jumps, that counts as one rep, okay?

2518
03:57:36,976 --> 03:57:41,967
Keep going until you get the desired reps done, and then you bring it back with the opposite.

2519
03:57:42,027 --> 03:57:45,895
So then it's left-right penultimate, and then it's right-left.

2520
03:57:46,596 --> 03:57:53,932
So what we're doing with this drill is a lot of things, but most importantly, we're introducing different movements into the jump.

2521
03:57:53,952 --> 03:57:55,896
So it's not always going to be as smooth as

2522
03:57:55,876 --> 03:57:57,938
normal linear penultimate.

2523
03:57:57,978 --> 03:58:08,170
There's a lot of times where you're gonna be in basketball, you gotta get over with the crossover step and get up, or you just grab the rebound and you gotta power dribble and get up off that lateral.

2524
03:58:08,190 --> 03:58:23,588
So we're working on just our footwork into that jump because you could be that jumper that jumps 45 inches in warmups and gets all the dunks, but when you get in the game, you gotta be able to jump out of any position, any situation, so that you can actually use that vertical in a game.

2525
03:58:26,605 --> 03:58:44,291
Now for our freestyle dunks, I put this in there because it's so important that you get out there and just allow your body to explore different approaches, different type of dunks, different type of jumping styles without me always trying to put you in a box and trying to get you to do one thing.

2526
03:58:44,612 --> 03:58:50,200
So I want you to set the clock for 10 minutes and I just want you to go get as many dunks as you can.

2527
03:58:50,180 --> 03:58:52,124
Take breaks in between if you need to.

2528
03:58:52,184 --> 03:58:54,708
I do want you to be recovered in between reps.

2529
03:58:54,728 --> 03:58:56,772
This isn't an endurance workout.

2530
03:58:57,133 --> 03:58:58,475
So get up off one foot.

2531
03:58:58,515 --> 03:58:59,337
Throw it down.

2532
03:58:59,798 --> 03:59:00,399
Walk back.

2533
03:59:00,439 --> 03:59:02,563
Recover for 30 seconds to a minute.

2534
03:59:02,883 --> 03:59:03,545
Come back in.

2535
03:59:03,665 --> 03:59:04,807
Take off off two.

2536
03:59:05,228 --> 03:59:06,450
Try to dunk left.

2537
03:59:06,430 --> 03:59:09,514
Whatever you want to do, get creative and do it.

2538
03:59:09,774 --> 03:59:13,820
Of course, if you can't dunk and all you can do is touch the bottom of the net, I don't care.

2539
03:59:13,840 --> 03:59:15,102
I still want you to get creative.

2540
03:59:15,442 --> 03:59:16,944
Come in off two and touch the net.

2541
03:59:17,304 --> 03:59:19,908
Come from baseline, get up off one and touch the net.

2542
03:59:20,228 --> 03:59:22,632
Try to jump off left, touch with the left.

2543
03:59:23,633 --> 03:59:32,725
Variability, variety is the key to longevity and it's super important for building kind of well-rounded explosiveness and athleticism.

2544
03:59:32,705 --> 03:59:37,467
And so I want you to get creative, set the clock for 10 minutes, and just freestyle dunk.

2545
03:59:54,676 --> 04:00:16,549
we need two boxes or two chairs or two benches anything that is the same height you could even do a box and a bench or a box in a chair doesn't matter as long as we got two things at the same height that are nice and stable now if we can do band resistance that's our best option so if you have some heavy dumbbells that we can anchor our bands to and then get the band right around the hip

2546
04:00:16,529 --> 04:00:20,034
So I'm in my shoulder elevated hip bridge position.

2547
04:00:20,134 --> 04:00:23,439
So my shoulder blades are on the box or on the bench.

2548
04:00:23,880 --> 04:00:28,907
I have one leg up and then my other leg, the leg that I'm working is at 90 degrees.

2549
04:00:29,187 --> 04:00:32,532
I want to make sure that my mid foot is on the corner of that box.

2550
04:00:32,612 --> 04:00:37,199
So I'm not driving down on the top of the box, but I'm also not on the side of the box.

2551
04:00:37,459 --> 04:00:39,482
I'm right on the corner of that box.

2552
04:00:39,462 --> 04:00:55,564
we do want to make sure that box is nice and stable if it's not heavy put some dumbbells or some weighted plates on the other side of it so that it doesn't slide out during this exercise so now from here i'm going band resisted and i'm just doing a single leg hip bridge so i hinge

2553
04:00:55,544 --> 04:01:01,515
My butt is gonna be about an inch to two inches off the floor and then explode up to full hip extension.

2554
04:01:01,915 --> 04:01:10,230
Squeeze for one to two seconds in that glute at the top and then release back down into your hip hinge, explode back into that hip extension.

2555
04:01:10,591 --> 04:01:12,574
We should feel a very big burn

2556
04:01:12,554 --> 04:01:30,917
in the glutes you'll also feel a little bit in the hamstrings if you feel it more in your lower back then you know that something is going wrong on this exercise we should feel a little burn in those erector muscles the muscles around your spine but those should not be the primary muscles involved in this exercise

2557
04:01:30,897 --> 04:01:36,302
Now we really want to use bands because at the top, the band resistance is at its highest.

2558
04:01:36,643 --> 04:01:42,168
And just like in sprinting, we need our glutes and our hamstrings to be strongest near hip extension.

2559
04:01:42,468 --> 04:01:49,835
And so with bands, it's not giving us a lot of resistance at the bottom, but near full hip extension, it's giving us the most resistance.

2560
04:01:50,096 --> 04:01:51,817
That's why we really want to use bands here.

2561
04:01:51,997 --> 04:01:58,744
But if you don't have bands and you just have a sandbag or a medicine ball or a kettlebell or something like that,

2562
04:01:58,724 --> 04:01:59,385
That's okay.

2563
04:01:59,526 --> 04:02:00,989
Go ahead and hold that in position.

2564
04:02:01,029 --> 04:02:02,452
Find a comfortable position.

2565
04:02:02,572 --> 04:02:09,126
Use a pad if you need to and then put the weight on top of that pad and you're just going through the same range of motion.

2566
04:02:09,446 --> 04:02:12,232
Get that good squeeze in the glute up at the top.

2567
04:02:12,473 --> 04:02:14,978
We want to build that mind muscle connection.

2568
04:02:14,958 --> 04:02:34,435
so this whole exercise i want to think about my body in a sea of white and that glute is lighting up bright red so studies have shown that we can actually get higher muscle activation when we start to get that mind muscle connection so that's a little trick think about that muscle that we're working and make it light up bright red

2569
04:02:50,699 --> 04:02:56,710
So for the Dratch RFESS, we are going to go in our normal rear foot elevated split squat position.

2570
04:02:57,010 --> 04:02:58,212
My dumbbells are on the ground.

2571
04:02:58,553 --> 04:03:01,118
My ankle is directly underneath that knee.

2572
04:03:01,438 --> 04:03:09,172
I'm going to grab the dumbbells and basically I'm going explosive rear foot elevated, except I'm going to slam into the ground with that front foot.

2573
04:03:09,212 --> 04:03:12,538
So I'm going to lift up a couple inches and I'm just going to push down.

2574
04:03:12,518 --> 04:03:27,827
then I'm gonna explode up so it's boom explode straight up now the reason why we're doing that is because we want to get that really hard ground reaction force so the issue is in lifting we do everything sort of

2575
04:03:27,807 --> 04:03:48,145
controlled and ground-based and then on the court everything is a hard foot strike we have high ground reaction forces and so this is an exercise that kind of blends the two kind of takes the best of both worlds where we're still getting the high force from strength training but we're also getting that tendon loading like we would get on the court

2576
04:03:48,125 --> 04:03:49,947
All right, so start light.

2577
04:03:50,648 --> 04:03:53,271
I generally go about 15 pounds in each hand.

2578
04:03:53,951 --> 04:03:57,535
If I was getting into a little of the heavier side, I would go about 25.

2579
04:03:58,456 --> 04:04:09,128
But you will notice when you're really slamming into the floor and trying to get up quick, as you go too heavy, if you get up to like 35 or 45 in each hand, you're going to start to get a little bit slower.

2580
04:04:09,468 --> 04:04:11,230
I do want you to be explosive.

2581
04:04:11,210 --> 04:04:15,179
but if you feel like you can leave the ground then it's too light.

2582
04:04:15,439 --> 04:04:23,417
So if you were holding 15s and you got up so explosively that you could actually leave the floor with that front foot then it is a little bit too light.

2583
04:04:23,778 --> 04:04:25,742
In that case I would want you to go up.

2584
04:04:28,642 --> 04:04:31,907
So the first one for our static stretch is just going to be a basic quad stretch.

2585
04:04:31,947 --> 04:04:36,214
So I'm just going to go heel to hip and I'm just going to get up nice and tall.

2586
04:04:36,495 --> 04:04:43,306
I'm going to raise my opposite hand and I'm just going to hold for 15 seconds and then I'm going to switch over to the other side.

2587
04:04:43,607 --> 04:04:47,092
If you need to hold on to something for balance, that's okay.

2588
04:04:47,373 --> 04:04:54,885
We're not going to get the same arm raise, but you can hold on and just make sure that we're nice and tall and that heel is touching the hip the whole time.

2589
04:04:54,865 --> 04:04:59,216
For the elevated hamstring stretch, I'm just gonna use a bench, a box, a chair.

2590
04:04:59,637 --> 04:05:01,602
I'm just gonna get my heel on there.

2591
04:05:01,942 --> 04:05:04,128
That toe is pointed up towards the ceiling.

2592
04:05:04,429 --> 04:05:06,754
And then I'm just gonna hinge from the hips.

2593
04:05:06,774 --> 04:05:09,000
So I don't wanna lean forward and round my back.

2594
04:05:09,281 --> 04:05:11,085
I'm just gonna lean forward.

2595
04:05:11,065 --> 04:05:31,892
from the hips keeping my back nice and straight if you want to reach down and touch your ankle or touch your toe you can but don't reach down and start to bend over from the back so i like to just keep my hands here to make sure that i'm not rounding the upper back and i'm just going to hold 15 seconds and then i'm going to switch over to the other side

2596
04:05:32,142 --> 04:05:34,125
15 seconds on the other side as well.

2597
04:05:34,145 --> 04:05:36,428
We should feel this stretch all in the hamstrings.

2598
04:05:36,448 --> 04:05:37,890
So that is the back of the thigh.

2599
04:05:38,130 --> 04:05:42,436
We'll feel it a little bit down into the calves, but we should feel it mostly hamstrings.

2600
04:05:42,456 --> 04:05:46,142
For our adductor stretch, I'm just gonna go one leg out.

2601
04:05:46,282 --> 04:05:48,705
I need to lock out this knee so I'm nice and straight.

2602
04:05:49,066 --> 04:05:51,389
I'm gonna sit back onto my heel.

2603
04:05:51,729 --> 04:05:53,312
So now look at this back foot.

2604
04:05:53,332 --> 04:05:54,994
I'm not curling the toe under.

2605
04:05:54,974 --> 04:05:58,799
I'm putting it down like this so the top of my foot is flat to the floor.

2606
04:05:59,380 --> 04:06:02,625
And I'm gonna sit my hips back to that heel.

2607
04:06:02,685 --> 04:06:08,413
Now from there, I can already feel a little bit of a stretch in the adductor.

2608
04:06:08,734 --> 04:06:17,286
Now if you don't really try to square your chest towards the floor, now from there, if you don't feel a big stretch already, we're gonna come down

2609
04:06:17,266 --> 04:06:21,793
to the elbows, and we're just gonna hang out in this position for 15 seconds.

2610
04:06:22,234 --> 04:06:26,620
Alright, so I should feel that stretch all through the adductors, that's the inside of the leg.

2611
04:06:27,101 --> 04:06:31,788
After 15 seconds, I'm gonna switch over to that other side, same thing.

2612
04:06:32,109 --> 04:06:34,993
For my glute stretch, I'm gonna pull this knee back.

2613
04:06:35,294 --> 04:06:38,599
Now make sure that this other leg stays down on the floor.

2614
04:06:38,579 --> 04:06:42,564
So I need my right knee and my right heel down through the ground.

2615
04:06:42,844 --> 04:06:50,474
I'm not going to lift off and I'm just going to lay my head back and just pull this knee as far towards the chest as I can.

2616
04:06:50,875 --> 04:06:56,362
Now, a lot of you, as you pull, the tendency is to rise here because we're tight in the hip flexors.

2617
04:06:56,762 --> 04:07:02,089
If that's the case, try to have somebody hold that leg down or strap it down with a band.

2618
04:07:02,069 --> 04:07:06,814
or just realize that you don't have that range of motion yet and you can only pull to right here.

2619
04:07:07,215 --> 04:07:14,863
But this is a glute stretch for this left leg, but at the same time, for a lot of you, this will be a hip flexor stretch on that right side.

2620
04:07:15,364 --> 04:07:18,167
So I'm just gonna pull back, hold for 15 seconds.

2621
04:07:18,607 --> 04:07:24,634
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side, trying to get full range of motion with that other leg.

2622
04:07:24,614 --> 04:07:27,697
So for our hip flexor stretch, make sure that we have something soft.

2623
04:07:27,757 --> 04:07:29,919
I don't want you guys putting your knee on a hardwood.

2624
04:07:30,159 --> 04:07:33,802
Make sure you have a pad or a soft floor to do this stretch on.

2625
04:07:34,283 --> 04:07:35,864
So I'm just going to go on one knee.

2626
04:07:35,884 --> 04:07:38,787
This knee is going to go 90 degrees.

2627
04:07:38,847 --> 04:07:39,768
So I'm 90 there.

2628
04:07:40,128 --> 04:07:42,911
My ankle is directly underneath that knee.

2629
04:07:43,271 --> 04:07:45,894
Now from here, I just got to get up nice and tall.

2630
04:07:45,914 --> 04:07:50,618
Some of you are already going to feel a stretch in the hip flexor because we're extra tight.

2631
04:07:50,958 --> 04:07:54,081
Now from there, I'm just going to lean forward

2632
04:07:54,061 --> 04:07:57,348
So I should have this knee back behind the hip.

2633
04:07:57,368 --> 04:08:02,137
And now from there, I'm just raising straight up and I'm going to hold.

2634
04:08:02,177 --> 04:08:03,620
All right.

2635
04:08:03,640 --> 04:08:09,512
So I feel a big stretch from here all the way down through the bottom of that hip flexor.

2636
04:08:10,253 --> 04:08:14,061
After 15 seconds, I'm going to switch over to that other side and do the same thing.

2637
04:08:14,041 --> 04:08:19,368
For my calf stretch, I'm basically going to do what they would call a downward dog in yoga.

2638
04:08:19,768 --> 04:08:22,993
So I'm here, I'm going to push back like this.

2639
04:08:23,093 --> 04:08:26,277
I'm going to straighten out my arms and now I'm just going to cross over.

2640
04:08:26,657 --> 04:08:36,370
So I'm going to put my left foot over that right foot and I'm going to try to get that right heel down towards the floor or as close as I can.

2641
04:08:36,670 --> 04:08:43,156
So I do have a straight knee, so we're stretching out what's called the gastrocnemius, that's the outside calf muscle.

2642
04:08:43,437 --> 04:08:49,583
So I shouldn't feel the stretch as much down in the ankle and the Achilles as we would on some of our hip mobility drills.

2643
04:08:49,983 --> 04:08:54,067
We should feel it on the outside of that calf muscle.

2644
04:08:55,229 --> 04:08:59,032
A lot of us aren't gonna be able to get our heel all the way to the floor, that's okay.

2645
04:08:59,413 --> 04:09:02,596
Just work on getting it down as low as we can.

2646
04:09:03,076 --> 04:09:06,660
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side.

2647
04:09:09,509 --> 04:09:10,170
What's up guys?

2648
04:09:10,251 --> 04:09:14,980
Quick minimum dose advice for phase three, day two, and day four.

2649
04:09:15,561 --> 04:09:17,125
Already a pretty short workout.

2650
04:09:17,165 --> 04:09:19,049
You probably shouldn't have to take out anything.

2651
04:09:19,630 --> 04:09:25,662
If you really need to cut down, we can take out the mobility drills if you're already pretty flexible and pretty mobile.

2652
04:09:25,642 --> 04:09:38,487
Now, if you don't want to go to the gym and you just want to do this workout at home, you could always hook up a band and do the split stance anti-rotation, or if you don't have a band, just skip the split stance anti-rotation.

2653
04:09:38,808 --> 04:09:40,251
You can do everything else at home.

2654
04:09:40,672 --> 04:09:42,736
The lateral flexion, you can do this with a band.

2655
04:09:43,036 --> 04:09:47,565
If you don't have a band, we can get the same qualities from a side plank.

2656
04:09:47,545 --> 04:09:56,723
So do a regular side plank, three times 30 seconds for your reps and everything else you can really do body weight at home.

2657
04:09:57,163 --> 04:10:01,251
So if it's a hassle to go to the gym, you could always do this workout from home.

2658
04:10:01,632 --> 04:10:07,984
If you're at the gym already, then obviously it's more beneficial to use the cable machine, but it's up to you.

2659
04:10:08,205 --> 04:10:10,549
Whatever's more convenient, let's get after it.

2660
04:10:10,529 --> 04:10:14,356
So the first thing we're going to do for our dynamic warm-up is stationary skips.

2661
04:10:14,636 --> 04:10:17,241
Now for all of these, you can take them on the move if you want.

2662
04:10:17,301 --> 04:10:21,248
For right now, I'm just going to do them stationary just in case you don't have much room.

2663
04:10:21,749 --> 04:10:28,340
So we're just going up with the right, up with the left, just like we're running, and vice versa on that other side.

2664
04:10:28,701 --> 04:10:32,407
All right, I'm staying stiff with the feet, so I'm not letting my heel collapse.

2665
04:10:32,427 --> 04:10:34,090
I want to stay on the ball of the foot.

2666
04:10:34,070 --> 04:10:59,453
and i'm just going to go about 50 of my max speed i'm not going too fast yet we're going to go for 30 seconds on the skips for the seal jacks it's basically like a jumping jack except i'm going to coordinate arms with the legs so i'm going to go over with the right and over with the right hand at the same time back to neutral over with the left over with the left hand and then i'm just going to speed that up i'm going to get a good little rhythm going here

2667
04:10:59,433 --> 04:11:04,740
maybe somewhere between 30 and 50 percent of your max speed, so we're not all out.

2668
04:11:05,200 --> 04:11:06,762
We're just getting that blood flowing.

2669
04:11:07,063 --> 04:11:08,404
We're going to go for 30 seconds.

2670
04:11:08,605 --> 04:11:12,930
For the over-under hamstring stretch, I'm just going to go over with the left leg.

2671
04:11:13,250 --> 04:11:15,053
I'm going to come down, touch the toe.

2672
04:11:15,133 --> 04:11:24,765
Now, if you can't touch the toe without rounding the back, then just go mid-shin or even to the knees, just as low as we can, but we don't want to go to the point where we have to round our back.

2673
04:11:24,745 --> 04:11:32,393
OK, so I'm going to get down, touch my toes back to neutral, and then I cross over the other way and I'm going the other side.

2674
04:11:36,085 --> 04:11:40,452
All right, we're gonna go five over and back, so it's 10 total touches.

2675
04:11:40,652 --> 04:11:45,981
For the quad hamstring leans, I'm just gonna go into a quad stretch, so I'm gonna pull my right foot up.

2676
04:11:46,262 --> 04:11:52,832
I wanna make sure that my heel is touching my hip in that position, and I'm not out like this, I'm keeping that knee in.

2677
04:11:53,253 --> 04:12:01,266
Now from there, I'm gonna keep the left knee straight, and I'm just gonna go into a lean as low as I can.

2678
04:12:01,246 --> 04:12:06,195
So I'm getting a really good stretch in the quad by going down and getting my knee back.

2679
04:12:06,535 --> 04:12:12,125
I'm getting it into the hip flexor a little bit more and I'm getting this hamstring a good stretch.

2680
04:12:12,807 --> 04:12:15,171
And I'm also working on my balance at the same time.

2681
04:12:15,491 --> 04:12:20,120
I'm going to go five leans and then I'm going to switch over five leans on the other side.

2682
04:12:20,761 --> 04:12:23,085
For the hip opener, we're going to go push up position.

2683
04:12:24,027 --> 04:12:27,613
I'm going to go left leg up outside this left hand.

2684
04:12:28,054 --> 04:12:32,521
Now from here, I'm just going to rotate up and hold one, two, three.

2685
04:12:32,581 --> 04:12:34,845
Now I'm going to go elbow down towards the floor.

2686
04:12:35,185 --> 04:12:37,209
We might not be able to touch the elbow to the ground.

2687
04:12:37,249 --> 04:12:37,830
That's okay.

2688
04:12:38,170 --> 04:12:39,773
Let's just get as low as we can there.

2689
04:12:40,233 --> 04:12:41,175
One, two, three.

2690
04:12:41,155 --> 04:13:07,618
three and back up so three there three there I'm gonna go five cycles and then I'm gonna switch to the other side five and five same thing for the adductor hip flexor combo I'm going lateral with one skip so it's one skip lateral and I'm going down I'm trying to touch this floor keep this knee straight because I want to get that stretch on the inside of the leg in this adductor I'm going back with the hip like I would in a normal squat

2691
04:13:07,598 --> 04:13:11,523
and I'm getting nice and low, touch the floor, and I'm popping out to that other side.

2692
04:13:12,023 --> 04:13:15,988
All right, so let's just hold about one second at the bottom and pop out.

2693
04:13:16,329 --> 04:13:21,856
I need five of these down and back, so it's 10 total, and then I immediately go into a hip flexor.

2694
04:13:22,476 --> 04:13:36,694
Same thing with the skip, and now I land, I turn this foot forward, I pivot, I'm here, knee a couple inches off the floor, I'm gonna rotate, hold one, and then come back, and it's to the other side.

2695
04:13:41,635 --> 04:13:48,164
At the bottom of this stretch, I'm gonna get that really good stretch in the hip flexor, and I always need to turn towards the lead leg.

2696
04:13:48,184 --> 04:13:49,646
Don't make the mistake of going here.

2697
04:13:50,026 --> 04:13:58,097
You need to rotate towards that lead leg as far as we can, and I'm gonna feel it through that hip flexor, and then I pop out to the other side.

2698
04:13:58,198 --> 04:14:04,066
For the overhead deep squat progression, I'm going high with the hands, basic squat stance, so I'm a little wider than shoulder width.

2699
04:14:04,146 --> 04:14:08,031
I can point the toes out just a little bit, and then I'm just gonna go here,

2700
04:14:08,011 --> 04:14:09,735
It's going to be a hamstring stretch.

2701
04:14:09,995 --> 04:14:11,939
One, two, three.

2702
04:14:12,080 --> 04:14:15,046
Keep the hands down and come into a deep squat.

2703
04:14:15,246 --> 04:14:17,431
Try to stay back on your heels if you can.

2704
04:14:18,072 --> 04:14:19,816
One, two, three.

2705
04:14:19,856 --> 04:14:21,359
Rock forward.

2706
04:14:21,440 --> 04:14:22,462
So I'm on my toes now.

2707
04:14:22,983 --> 04:14:25,188
Drive the knees out with the elbows.

2708
04:14:25,248 --> 04:14:25,568
Hold.

2709
04:14:26,190 --> 04:14:27,252
One, two, three.

2710
04:14:27,232 --> 04:14:27,913
Three.

2711
04:14:28,254 --> 04:14:28,976
Rock it back.

2712
04:14:29,336 --> 04:14:31,140
Heels back down to the ground.

2713
04:14:31,401 --> 04:14:33,024
One, two, three.

2714
04:14:33,124 --> 04:14:34,327
I need one hand up.

2715
04:14:34,868 --> 04:14:35,669
Two hand up.

2716
04:14:35,890 --> 04:14:36,571
Not out here.

2717
04:14:36,631 --> 04:14:38,114
We need it back behind the head.

2718
04:14:38,696 --> 04:14:39,317
And stand.

2719
04:14:39,918 --> 04:14:40,119
Alright.

2720
04:14:40,599 --> 04:14:41,962
So that's one cycle.

2721
04:14:42,223 --> 04:14:43,345
We're going to go for three of these.

2722
04:14:44,307 --> 04:14:45,730
So it's one, two, three.

2723
04:14:46,064 --> 04:14:48,327
One, two, three, lean.

2724
04:14:49,108 --> 04:14:51,371
One, two, three, heels back down.

2725
04:14:51,431 --> 04:14:55,457
One, two, three, one up, two up, stand, all right?

2726
04:14:55,757 --> 04:15:04,068
If you cannot get down in that deep position, then let's just go as low as we can right here, and then on the lean, it's just gonna look like this, all right?

2727
04:15:04,088 --> 04:15:08,454
And then we're gonna come back, hopefully parallel to the floor, one up, two up, stand.

2728
04:15:08,815 --> 04:15:15,143
We just gotta get as low as we can, and every day try to progress so that we can get lower and lower, better range of motion.

2729
04:15:15,123 --> 04:15:17,946
So for the hip bridge, it's gonna be a very basic hip bridge.

2730
04:15:18,006 --> 04:15:20,309
Even if you're an advanced athlete, I want you to do this version.

2731
04:15:20,729 --> 04:15:23,492
So we're gonna get up nice and flat in a hip bridge.

2732
04:15:23,833 --> 04:15:25,534
I need to be flat through the hips.

2733
04:15:25,835 --> 04:15:28,237
I'm driving through my midfoot right now.

2734
04:15:28,758 --> 04:15:33,203
And now I'm just gonna squeeze my glutes together as hard as I possibly can.

2735
04:15:33,563 --> 04:15:36,606
So just holding in this position isn't that difficult.

2736
04:15:36,626 --> 04:15:44,455
But if I squeeze my glutes together as hard as I can so they're rock solid, I'm gonna get a really good isometric contraction.

2737
04:15:44,435 --> 04:15:54,416
and I'm gonna activate a lot of muscle fibers, and we're just gonna hold in this position for 25 seconds with a full squeeze, and then relax.

2738
04:15:54,837 --> 04:16:03,355
This is all for hip activation, getting those glutes fired up, it's the most powerful muscle in the body, so we gotta get them revved up for our session.

2739
04:16:22,353 --> 04:16:31,393
So for our split stance anti-rotation ABCs, what I'm gonna do is capital letters A through J. Now I want you in a split stance.

2740
04:16:31,413 --> 04:16:38,168
So think about if you were gonna drop your feet, that is the position, that's our base position that we're working with here because

2741
04:16:38,823 --> 04:16:47,360
When we drop to that position and get into our drive, we always take hand checks, we always take hits to one side of our body and a lot of us fly into rotation.

2742
04:16:47,701 --> 04:16:53,273
We have to have that anti-rotation core strength so that we can push through those situations.

2743
04:16:53,333 --> 04:16:59,886
But too often we get good anti-rotation in that square stance and we never get it in that actual split stance.

2744
04:16:59,866 --> 04:17:17,368
What I'm gonna do is get to that position, nice and low, I gotta brace my core here, nice and strong, my breath is normal, and then I'm gonna press right out in front of my chest, and I'm gonna start that ABC, so capital letter A, capital B,

2745
04:17:18,530 --> 04:17:20,014
capital C, all right?

2746
04:17:20,655 --> 04:17:24,204
A through J, and then I switch it and I do it the other way.

2747
04:17:24,705 --> 04:17:31,662
Make sure that the inside foot, so the foot that's closer to the cable machine is back, all right?

2748
04:17:32,003 --> 04:17:35,070
And then when we switch, that left foot is back.

2749
04:17:35,050 --> 04:17:41,138
Now, if you don't have the cable machine, of course, you could just use a band hooked up to a power rack or something nice and stable.

2750
04:17:41,438 --> 04:17:42,900
We're going to get very similar effects there.

2751
04:17:43,040 --> 04:17:48,908
But if you can, we would want to use the cable and, of course, start light and gradually go up.

2752
04:17:49,168 --> 04:17:51,111
We do want to get as heavy as we can here.

2753
04:17:51,391 --> 04:18:03,066
The heavier we get, the more we're going to get stable in that split stance position, fire up that core, get nice and strong and stable so that we can be dominant once we hit the core or the field.

2754
04:18:20,613 --> 04:18:31,943
So for the band distracted hamstring stretch, I'm just gonna go around my right leg, so just one leg, and I'm gonna get the band as high as I can at that hip, right where that hip hinge is, okay?

2755
04:18:31,963 --> 04:18:48,038
I'm gonna step up and get some good tension, and I'm just gonna come to that heel, and I'm gonna try to straighten out that right knee, and then I'm just gonna let that band really pull my hips back into a big hip hinge as I slide my hands down until my hands touch my toe.

2756
04:18:48,018 --> 04:18:51,886
So I'm here, hip hinge, touch, and then back up.

2757
04:18:52,227 --> 04:18:55,494
Squeeze the glutes at the top to really pull your hips through.

2758
04:18:55,975 --> 04:18:57,899
Okay, so we have that initial slight bend.

2759
04:18:58,259 --> 04:19:03,310
From there, it's hips back, back, back, touch, and then pull through with the glutes.

2760
04:19:03,290 --> 04:19:08,016
I should feel a really big stretch in the hamstrings at the bottom of that stretch.

2761
04:19:08,476 --> 04:19:12,582
Now, a lot of you guys, to try to get down, you're gonna start to round your back.

2762
04:19:13,102 --> 04:19:15,445
If that's the case, then we don't have to go so low.

2763
04:19:15,926 --> 04:19:23,475
Make sure you keep your shoulder blades tight, like you're holding an imaginary pencil in between your shoulder blades, and just go as low as we can.

2764
04:19:23,455 --> 04:19:33,779
Now that might mean fingertips right past the knee, that might mean mid-shin, or ideally that's going to be touching the toe without rounding the back.

2765
04:19:33,799 --> 04:19:37,768
Whatever you can work with, work with that and let's get better over time.

2766
04:19:52,227 --> 04:19:55,030
So for my lateral flexion, I'm going to use a cable machine.

2767
04:19:55,090 --> 04:19:59,475
If you don't have a cable machine, just use a band hooked up to a power rack.

2768
04:19:59,495 --> 04:20:02,518
And I'm going to interlock my fingers on the handle.

2769
04:20:02,839 --> 04:20:03,660
I'm going to pull out.

2770
04:20:03,740 --> 04:20:08,986
Now make sure it's on the high setting so that when I'm in full extension, it's parallel to the floor.

2771
04:20:09,366 --> 04:20:13,511
So I don't want you standing up high so that it's slanted.

2772
04:20:13,851 --> 04:20:16,013
I need this cable to be parallel.

2773
04:20:16,033 --> 04:20:21,019
So that means I'm going to have to bend my knees and I'm going to have to have it on the highest setting.

2774
04:20:20,999 --> 04:20:29,592
We are here, the problem is most people go into back hyperextension and their pelvis anteriorly rotates.

2775
04:20:29,672 --> 04:20:33,178
So it's here, we need to posteriorly rotate.

2776
04:20:33,418 --> 04:20:37,525
So think about if you had a tail, we're tucking that tail so you're there.

2777
04:20:38,005 --> 04:20:41,671
That takes care of that back issue so we're nice and flat, all right?

2778
04:20:41,691 --> 04:20:45,858
We have to stay in that pelvis position the whole set.

2779
04:20:46,218 --> 04:20:49,403
And now from here, I'm just going lateral flexion,

2780
04:20:49,383 --> 04:20:51,867
and lateral flexion the other way, all right?

2781
04:20:52,207 --> 04:20:53,028
Don't cut it short.

2782
04:20:53,089 --> 04:20:56,394
A lot of people go here and then they just go concentric.

2783
04:20:56,414 --> 04:21:00,460
A big part of this exercise is that loading, that eccentric.

2784
04:21:00,680 --> 04:21:06,008
We're loading up that lateral line, getting that strong, powerful sling.

2785
04:21:07,490 --> 04:21:10,314
This is gonna be more of a slow and controlled exercise.

2786
04:21:10,775 --> 04:21:13,960
We do wanna go up as heavy as we can once we get our form down.

2787
04:21:14,320 --> 04:21:16,724
We should feel this in the side of the core.

2788
04:21:16,784 --> 04:21:24,115
Of course, you're gonna feel it a little bit in your back, a little bit in your front core, but those obliques is what we're really targeting with this exercise.

2789
04:21:36,008 --> 04:21:44,843
For the elastic leg kicks, I want you to think about a normal, kind of like a Frankenstein kick, except we're gonna make it a little bit more rapid and a little bit more elastic.

2790
04:21:45,143 --> 04:21:56,683
So I'm just gonna stay on the balls of the feet and I'm just gonna kick up my leg as high as I can, keeping that knee straight, and I'm just gonna switch every time so it ends up being a little bit of a skip.

2791
04:21:56,663 --> 04:21:58,847
and then a straight leg kick.

2792
04:21:59,328 --> 04:22:01,112
Now I'm popping off the balls of the feet.

2793
04:22:01,633 --> 04:22:03,577
I do not want your heels to touch the floor.

2794
04:22:04,058 --> 04:22:06,724
And the reason why we're doing this, you're not going to get a huge burn.

2795
04:22:06,764 --> 04:22:08,167
This isn't a huge workout.

2796
04:22:08,527 --> 04:22:13,778
We're trying to get some elasticity back in the post chain, some elasticity in the hamstrings.

2797
04:22:13,758 --> 04:22:19,313
So a lot of people sit there and stretch or even do a normal dynamic warmup for elasticity.

2798
04:22:19,674 --> 04:22:25,029
The thing is for a muscle to actually increase elasticity, it has to be under one second.

2799
04:22:25,410 --> 04:22:29,742
So if I'm going slow with that kick or if I'm holding

2800
04:22:29,722 --> 04:22:51,021
a stretch it might increase what we call plasticity how flexible we get but not elasticity and elasticity is what actually translates to sprinting and jumping so everything has to be under one second and that's why we're going rapid with those kicks i want you to think about getting that leg up as quick as you can as high as you can

2801
04:23:20,819 --> 04:23:25,665
So for the leg lowers, you gotta make sure that you anchor your hands to something stable.

2802
04:23:25,705 --> 04:23:27,307
So I'm holding onto a power rack.

2803
04:23:27,768 --> 04:23:31,573
Make sure that whatever you're holding onto is nice and stable so that that's your support.

2804
04:23:31,913 --> 04:23:38,461
If worse comes worse and all you have is a partner, your partner could stand over you and they could just grab onto your ankles, all right?

2805
04:23:38,842 --> 04:23:40,885
So what we're doing is negative.

2806
04:23:40,965 --> 04:23:44,289
So we're gonna go three to four seconds on the eccentric.

2807
04:23:44,309 --> 04:23:49,155
So that means my legs are straight up and I'm going three to four seconds down.

2808
04:23:49,135 --> 04:23:51,698
I'm trying to keep my knees as straight as possible.

2809
04:23:52,699 --> 04:23:59,788
So control down the heel, stop a couple inches short of the floor, and then we bend our knees and bring it back.

2810
04:24:00,309 --> 04:24:03,313
So I don't want the concentric to be the hard part.

2811
04:24:03,633 --> 04:24:12,544
So that's why we're bending our knees, coming back, extend the knees so that our legs are nice and long, and then we go back into that lowering phase.

2812
04:24:12,524 --> 04:24:26,162
If that is too easy, then we can keep our knees straight and go straight on the up and on the down, but I would rather you really focus on that slow, controlled, eccentric, really squeezing that core with every rep.

2813
04:24:26,403 --> 04:24:27,546
Now, where we wanna feel this,

2814
04:24:27,526 --> 04:24:32,858
exercise is mostly front core so that abdominal wall should be fired up.

2815
04:24:33,138 --> 04:24:36,205
This is one exercise where we are going to get a pretty good burn.

2816
04:24:36,505 --> 04:24:44,202
If you're not getting a burn I would extend the reps a little bit so go up a couple reps to the point where you are getting that big burn in the front core.

2817
04:24:47,438 --> 04:24:52,183
So for the double band lateral push out, what I'm going to do is use a mini band.

2818
04:24:52,203 --> 04:24:53,565
I'm going to put it right above my knees.

2819
04:24:53,845 --> 04:24:55,447
I'm using Ethereal.

2820
04:24:56,008 --> 04:25:00,252
It's more of like a cloth material, kind of stretchy material, so it's not going to break.

2821
04:25:00,473 --> 04:25:05,238
But if you have the normal basic elastic resistance bands, that's okay.

2822
04:25:05,258 --> 04:25:11,505
So right above the knees and then I'm stepping in to the pro band.

2823
04:25:13,966 --> 04:25:21,981
Alright, now I like to link two bands together and then link it to something nice and stable like a power rack just because it gives me a little more room.

2824
04:25:22,022 --> 04:25:29,055
If you don't have two bands, you could probably still just link one band around the power rack and then step in.

2825
04:25:29,035 --> 04:25:33,482
What I'm gonna do is step out until I got some good resistance with this pro band.

2826
04:25:33,843 --> 04:25:43,698
And then I'm just gonna start in a basic squat stance, and now from here I'm just pushing out laterally as hard as I can, and I'm gonna hold there for a second, and then push back.

2827
04:25:43,978 --> 04:25:47,584
So it's drive, push back, drive,

2828
04:25:47,564 --> 04:26:14,955
push back so what you'll notice is off this right leg I'm getting full extension at that knee so I'm not doing just a little step like we normally would with a mini band to light up the glutes okay I'm pushing out against this band boom full extension just like somebody's driving and I gotta really push into that first step okay so it's drive out push back drive out push back now

2829
04:26:14,935 --> 04:26:18,759
We get the typical workout that we would with a mini band, right?

2830
04:26:19,119 --> 04:26:21,321
So I'm getting that good abduction.

2831
04:26:21,661 --> 04:26:23,003
I'm firing up that glute.

2832
04:26:23,303 --> 04:26:27,767
I'm really firing up this glute because I'm also pushing against this band.

2833
04:26:27,787 --> 04:26:29,229
So it's the best of both worlds.

2834
04:26:29,249 --> 04:26:31,171
We're working abductors here.

2835
04:26:31,551 --> 04:26:42,141
We're working the extensor muscles that we need so badly when it comes to improving explosiveness, especially when it comes to improving our lateral speed.

2836
04:26:42,121 --> 04:26:48,633
This drill is insane at improving your ability to apply force in the ground laterally.

2837
04:26:48,834 --> 04:26:51,078
So I'm going to hit my reps to one side.

2838
04:26:51,439 --> 04:26:54,505
I'm going to flip over and I'm going to hit my reps to the other side.

2839
04:26:54,845 --> 04:26:56,789
Remember, it's all about max intent.

2840
04:26:57,049 --> 04:26:59,013
We need big speed, big force.

2841
04:26:59,294 --> 04:26:59,995
Let's get it.

2842
04:27:20,275 --> 04:27:28,058
If you don't have the ankle mobility to keep your heels down and sit in that bottom position, then I want you to grab the weight

2843
04:27:28,696 --> 04:27:31,641
and I want you to come into a deep squat without the heels on the ground.

2844
04:27:32,042 --> 04:27:42,661
So I would just come forward, my knees are over the toes, and now from here, elbows are resting on the knees, and I'm just trying to sit the heels down as low as I can.

2845
04:27:43,482 --> 04:27:45,365
If you can get the heels down, great.

2846
04:27:45,686 --> 04:27:53,640
Then we're going to just rock side to side, trying to drive that knee right over the middle of my foot.

2847
04:27:53,620 --> 04:27:54,981
And we're just going to rock there.

2848
04:27:55,021 --> 04:27:58,465
Now, if you can't get your heels down, just get as far as you can.

2849
04:27:58,825 --> 04:27:59,045
All right.

2850
04:27:59,085 --> 04:28:01,968
