06:30:30,856 --> 06:30:34,462
We want a minimal knee bend and we want to pop off nice and quick.

4166
06:30:34,822 --> 06:30:37,206
Make sure that we do not collapse the torso.

4167
06:30:37,507 --> 06:30:39,931
We got to keep the torso nice and upright.

4168
06:30:40,271 --> 06:30:44,218
Keep that stability through the core on this whole exercise.

4169
06:30:44,198 --> 06:30:50,987
I like to start at a box that's a round knee height or a little bit below or a chair or a bench or something nice and stable.

4170
06:30:51,508 --> 06:30:54,232
As you get better, you can raise it higher and higher and higher.

4171
06:30:54,292 --> 06:31:00,200
Now, we do not want to be landing or we do not want to get up on the box and have too much of a bent knee.

4172
06:31:00,501 --> 06:31:06,549
So if I have to get up and I have to land like this and push off, then that box is probably too high.

4173
06:31:06,949 --> 06:31:12,417
I want to land with almost straight knees with a little bit of a bend in my knees at the top.

4174
06:31:12,397 --> 06:31:14,964
like that, and then push off from there.

4175
06:31:15,064 --> 06:31:19,938
So don't become obsessed with the box height, just be obsessed with the quickness off the ground.

4176
06:31:20,258 --> 06:31:27,418
And even if you're on a low box, just think about jumping as high as you can and floating to that box instead of barely getting on the box.

4177
06:31:27,398 --> 06:31:43,515
Now for some of you guys your balance isn't quite to this level yet so when you start getting rapid and you start pushing off it's hard for you to get balance and go back up or at the top your balance isn't good enough to just land and push off the right amount so you're kind of stumbling on the top of the box.

4178
06:31:43,535 --> 06:31:51,263
If that's the case I want you just to regress and just get up and just stick on one foot and then you can just step it back down.

4179
06:31:51,243 --> 06:31:57,126
Or if you can, stick it on one foot and then hop down and get up, stick it on the other foot.

4180
06:31:57,527 --> 06:32:01,422
But again, once you pass that level, start to go more rapid with it.

4181
06:32:12,809 --> 06:32:16,339
So for our rhythm quarter squats, we're gonna use a barbell.

4182
06:32:16,980 --> 06:32:21,934
If you don't have a barbell, you could just use dumbbells, but we really want to use a barbell if possible.

4183
06:32:22,475 --> 06:32:25,664
We're gonna go about 50% of your one rep max.

4184
06:32:25,684 --> 06:32:28,371
So we're going pretty light to start.

4185
06:32:28,351 --> 06:32:30,716
If you feel good, we can gradually go up.

4186
06:32:31,116 --> 06:32:35,345
So what we're going to do is a normal barbell back squat position.

4187
06:32:36,226 --> 06:32:39,934
What you're going to do is you're going to get down into a quarter squat position.

4188
06:32:40,134 --> 06:32:43,260
So we don't want anything past 90 degrees.

4189
06:32:43,601 --> 06:32:49,212
We actually want to mimic the knee angle that you're going to use in a double leg takeoff.

4190
06:32:49,192 --> 06:33:16,482
I'm gonna get down to let's say maybe 60 to 75 degrees I'm not going all the way to 90 so I'm gonna get to that quarter squat position the easier version is just quarter squat and up the heels stay down and we're just gonna kind of bounce in that position and develop some rhythm there so I don't want you to get to the top and then rest and go again we're just getting that rhythmic

4191
06:33:16,462 --> 06:33:17,244
quarter squat.

4192
06:33:17,284 --> 06:33:20,029
So just working on that top half of the range of motion.

4193
06:33:20,410 --> 06:33:25,540
Now the better version, if you have the balance, we're going to come all the way up to the toes.

4194
06:33:25,901 --> 06:33:29,669
So it's going to be here all the way up to the toes at the top.

4195
06:33:30,450 --> 06:33:36,242
So you sort of go into that little calf raise and then we drop back down into that quarter squat.

4196
06:33:36,222 --> 06:33:41,413
All right guys, now keep in mind, it's about the load on the muscles, not the load on the bar.

4197
06:33:41,674 --> 06:33:43,818
So don't worry about going too heavy.

4198
06:33:43,858 --> 06:33:48,368
Again, start around 50% of your one rep max.

4199
06:33:48,708 --> 06:33:50,592
If that's too light, then you can go up.

4200
06:33:51,114 --> 06:33:54,180
But keep in mind, if you feel like you could jump

4201
06:33:54,160 --> 06:34:16,050
off the ground with the barbell then it's too light because then by not jumping we're holding back and we're not actually getting max intent so it should be a weight where you couldn't easily leave the floor all right because i do want your toes to stay down on the ground on this exercise

4202
06:34:29,142 --> 06:34:32,886
So for my cable pull through, we can use any normal cable machine.

4203
06:34:32,947 --> 06:34:34,949
I'm showing it on a Kaiser machine right now.

4204
06:34:34,969 --> 06:34:36,351
You don't need a Kaiser.

4205
06:34:36,591 --> 06:34:37,933
We just need a normal cable.

4206
06:34:38,353 --> 06:34:42,298
So I'm going to use the rope and I'm going to grab underhand.

4207
06:34:42,358 --> 06:34:45,762
So like a tricep extension, you might be used to an overhand grip.

4208
06:34:45,982 --> 06:34:47,364
We're actually going underhand.

4209
06:34:47,604 --> 06:34:50,087
So my thumbs are facing up.

4210
06:34:50,067 --> 06:34:54,853
and I'm grabbing that rope, stand up and step out a little bit.

4211
06:34:55,454 --> 06:34:57,016
We're going to go pretty wide with the feet.

4212
06:34:57,577 --> 06:35:02,002
Now I'm going to go slight bend in the knees and all it is is that normal RDL position.

4213
06:35:02,483 --> 06:35:06,128
Work on that hip hinge so it's hips back as far as we can.

4214
06:35:06,188 --> 06:35:09,392
Our knees don't bend anymore from there.

4215
06:35:09,372 --> 06:35:10,994
Hips back, back, back.

4216
06:35:11,074 --> 06:35:13,556
I'm loading up the hamstrings and the glutes.

4217
06:35:13,576 --> 06:35:17,681
And then at that bottom position, we're gonna explode up at the top.

4218
06:35:17,741 --> 06:35:23,126
I need you to squeeze your glutes as hard as you can and really pull the hips through.

4219
06:35:23,166 --> 06:35:26,550
At the top, we get a two second isometric hold.

4220
06:35:26,870 --> 06:35:29,513
So that means we squeeze the glutes as hard as we can.

4221
06:35:29,553 --> 06:35:32,796
One, two, and then we release, we go back into it.

4222
06:35:33,157 --> 06:35:36,600
So hip hinge, boom, explode on the way up.

4223
06:35:36,620 --> 06:35:39,143
Squeeze the glutes at the top, okay?

4224
06:35:39,443 --> 06:35:49,718
Now, if your form is good here and you're feeling it in the right places, we should really feel like we're getting a huge stretch in the hamstrings and in the glutes at the bottom position.

4225
06:35:50,139 --> 06:35:54,566
And then when we explode, you should feel a big burn in the glutes and a little bit in the hamstrings as well.

4226
06:35:55,206 --> 06:35:59,693
If we're feeling good on that, then what I want you to do is actually pull your toes up.

4227
06:36:00,014 --> 06:36:04,320
So as you go down, your toes are off the floor, all right?

4228
06:36:04,300 --> 06:36:12,015
As soon as we reverse to get up, I push my big toe down into the ground as hard as I can and I explode.

4229
06:36:12,416 --> 06:36:18,208
So we're trying to build that neurological connection between the big toe and the glute.

4230
06:36:19,009 --> 06:36:24,300
So if you're not advanced and you're just getting used to this exercise, don't worry about that aspect yet.

4231
06:36:24,280 --> 06:36:30,670
But, if you're good to go, then start to slam that toe into the ground on the way up, squeeze at the top.

4232
06:36:31,030 --> 06:36:42,728
This is a very good exercise for the post chain, glutes, hamstring, training that hip hinge and improving our velocity on the hip extension, which is essential for the vertical jump.

4233
06:36:58,115 --> 06:37:03,904
So for my sub max long duration jumps, what I'm gonna do is almost like a jump rope.

4234
06:37:03,944 --> 06:37:08,410
So you know in a jump rope, we're just nice and low and we're rhythmic and we're bouncy.

4235
06:37:08,691 --> 06:37:14,319
We're not going maximal on this and we're also not lowering low and trying to use a lot of muscular power.

4236
06:37:14,639 --> 06:37:19,286
We're really just using for the most part that Achilles to spring us off the ground.

4237
06:37:19,386 --> 06:37:22,791
So there's gonna be three different aspects here.

4238
06:37:22,952 --> 06:37:26,637
So your first one is gonna be a side to side hop.

4239
06:37:26,617 --> 06:37:30,121
Okay, I'm springing off the balls of the feet.

4240
06:37:30,482 --> 06:37:34,366
I am not letting my heel collapse down to the ground, all right?

4241
06:37:34,847 --> 06:37:40,414
We're not going maximal, we're just going light and bouncy off the ground, okay?

4242
06:37:40,434 --> 06:37:42,396
Now I'm going for a certain amount of time.

4243
06:37:42,516 --> 06:37:46,761
Pay attention to the reps because we're going to go up every week.

4244
06:37:46,781 --> 06:37:49,865
So let's say for week one, you're 30 seconds.

4245
06:37:50,165 --> 06:37:52,728
Okay, now the second one is gonna be front back.

4246
06:37:52,869 --> 06:37:55,712
So I'm just switching the feet

4247
06:37:55,692 --> 06:38:13,887
forwards and backwards same concept springing off the balls of the feet not letting that heel collapse let's say it's 30 seconds there so then the third one is just a normal low level jump same thing spring off the ball of the foot heel cannot collapse okay now

4248
06:38:13,867 --> 06:38:16,771
What we're gonna do is really go long duration.

4249
06:38:16,791 --> 06:38:27,524
You're gonna get a big burn in the calves, but what we're doing is we're reforming the fascia of our feet and we're training that Achilles to be an energy storing and releasing monster.

4250
06:38:27,664 --> 06:38:29,366
So pay attention to the reps.

4251
06:38:29,667 --> 06:38:33,472
This is one exercise where I do want you close to your max.

4252
06:38:33,852 --> 06:38:36,696
So let's say week one, I gave you 30, 30, 30.

4253
06:38:36,756 --> 06:38:38,518
That's a minute and a half total.

4254
06:38:38,838 --> 06:38:43,384
If you got to the end of that minute and a half and you feel like you could have kept going,

4255
06:38:43,364 --> 06:38:44,646
you need to keep going.

4256
06:38:44,686 --> 06:38:53,141
You need to push close to your max because if we want the fascia to actually reform around the feet and we want the Achilles to adapt, we gotta push close to that max.

4257
06:38:53,161 --> 06:38:56,687
So for some of you, that might be two minutes, that might be three minutes.

4258
06:38:56,968 --> 06:39:00,153
I just need you to progressively increase each week.

4259
06:39:00,494 --> 06:39:07,566
So if I were to do this drill right now, I would probably get about three minutes and at that three minute mark, personally,

4260
06:39:07,546 --> 06:39:11,952
I would start to feel like almost like a cramp in the calf.

4261
06:39:12,233 --> 06:39:14,616
I would feel a burn of like a nine out of 10.

4262
06:39:14,936 --> 06:39:16,699
I don't need you to get to a 10 out of 10.

4263
06:39:16,999 --> 06:39:22,026
I don't need your calves to fully cramp up, but get close to that point and then stop.

4264
06:39:22,327 --> 06:39:23,609
Take as long as you want.

4265
06:39:23,689 --> 06:39:28,896
Sometimes I take up to two or three minutes in between sets and then I go back in.

4266
06:39:28,876 --> 06:39:38,512
For most of you, I want you to follow the rep range, but again, if that is too easy, extend it, make sure you jot down your time, and each week I want you to go up on that.

4267
06:39:38,892 --> 06:39:43,941
By the end of the four weeks, our fascia and our achilles is gonna be a lot springier.

4268
06:39:43,981 --> 06:39:47,486
We're gonna be storing and releasing elastic energy like never before.

4269
06:39:47,807 --> 06:39:48,488
Let's get it.

4270
06:40:14,152 --> 06:40:18,177
For our 7-11 breathing, what we're going to do is just lay down on our back.

4271
06:40:18,297 --> 06:40:20,100
Make sure that you're in a relaxed place.

4272
06:40:20,140 --> 06:40:22,843
I know you're probably in a gym, so it might be a little bit loud.

4273
06:40:22,884 --> 06:40:29,392
If you have headphones, throw on some headphones, throw on some slow music, maybe some yoga or meditation type music.

4274
06:40:29,913 --> 06:40:35,861
And all I'm going to do is just lay down and I'm going to breathe in through my nose for seven seconds.

4275
06:40:36,141 --> 06:40:39,906
And I'm also going to breathe out through my nose for 11 seconds.

4276
06:40:39,886 --> 06:40:55,988
okay so i'm not going to open my mouth for this whole drill all right so it's in through the nose and i want to make sure that my stomach is rising okay your chest will naturally rise a little bit but most of you when you think of deep breathing what happens is your belly stays still

4277
06:40:56,963 --> 06:41:00,027
and your chest puffs up and your shoulders elevate.

4278
06:41:00,047 --> 06:41:06,756
That means we are not actually getting all of that air, all of that oxygen down to the deepest part of the lungs.

4279
06:41:07,317 --> 06:41:13,105
So I want you to think about letting the belly rise as you take that breath in, okay?

4280
06:41:13,125 --> 06:41:16,790
So we're here, in deep through the nose, let the stomach rise.

4281
06:41:19,093 --> 06:41:23,359
Seven seconds, once you finish that seven seconds, it's out through the nose.

4282
06:41:26,309 --> 06:41:28,232
and that stomach will fall, okay?

4283
06:41:28,933 --> 06:41:31,577
Initially, this is very uncomfortable for guys.

4284
06:41:32,338 --> 06:41:41,371
I've had NBA players that absolutely hated this until they're in their third or fourth session and they started to get used to it because you do have to learn how to pace your breath.

4285
06:41:42,152 --> 06:41:49,924
If you just breathe in as hard as you can and breathe out as hard as you can, you're not gonna be able to go for seven in and 11 out.

4286
06:41:50,184 --> 06:41:54,190
You gotta learn to go very slow and pace that breath, okay?

4287
06:41:54,170 --> 06:42:23,097
this is doing a lot of stuff I mean for one we're helping you expand the lungs we're teaching you how to to breathe yourself into a more calmer state but from a recovery standpoint this could possibly be the best thing that you can do after a workout better than foam rolling better than static stretching because after a workout we're in that sympathetic state that's that fight that's that workout that's that game mode okay I got to get you to the parasympathetic state that's relax recover all recovery

4288
06:42:23,330 --> 06:42:25,835
happens in the parasympathetic state.

4289
06:42:26,376 --> 06:42:30,525
Okay, so if I'm still hyped up after the workout, I'm killing my recovery.

4290
06:42:30,866 --> 06:42:44,494
So as soon as we're done with the workout, we wanna do these breathing exercises to get us into that parasympathetic state and then I can really start to aid my recovery and I'm back better than ever tomorrow, ready to train again.

4291
06:42:46,313 --> 06:42:49,618
So the first one for our static stretch is just going to be a basic quad stretch.

4292
06:42:49,638 --> 06:42:53,905
So I'm just going to go heel to hip and I'm just going to get up nice and tall.

4293
06:42:54,185 --> 06:43:00,996
I'm going to raise my opposite hand and I'm just going to hold for 15 seconds and then I'm going to switch over to the other side.

4294
06:43:01,296 --> 06:43:04,782
If you need to hold on to something for balance, that's okay.

4295
06:43:05,062 --> 06:43:12,574
We're not going to get the same arm raise, but you can hold on and just make sure that we're nice and tall and that heel is touching the hip the whole time.

4296
06:43:12,554 --> 06:43:16,905
For the elevated hamstring stretch, I'm just gonna use a bench, a box, a chair.

4297
06:43:17,326 --> 06:43:19,311
I'm just gonna get my heel on there.

4298
06:43:19,331 --> 06:43:21,837
That toe is pointed up towards the ceiling.

4299
06:43:22,118 --> 06:43:24,183
And then I'm just gonna hinge from the hips.

4300
06:43:24,463 --> 06:43:26,689
So I don't wanna lean forward and round my back.

4301
06:43:26,990 --> 06:43:28,774
I'm just gonna lean forward.

4302
06:43:28,754 --> 06:43:49,530
from the hips keeping my back nice and straight if you want to reach down and touch your ankle or touch your toe you can but don't reach down and start to bend over from the back so i like to just keep my hands here to make sure that i'm not rounding the upper back and i'm just going to hold 15 seconds and then i'm going to switch over to the other side

4303
06:43:49,848 --> 06:43:51,811
15 seconds on the other side as well.

4304
06:43:51,831 --> 06:43:53,974
We should feel this stretch all in the hamstrings.

4305
06:43:54,155 --> 06:43:55,577
So that is the back of the thigh.

4306
06:43:55,817 --> 06:44:00,124
We'll feel it a little bit down into the calves, but we should feel it mostly hamstrings.

4307
06:44:00,144 --> 06:44:03,829
For our adductor stretch, I'm just gonna go one leg out.

4308
06:44:03,990 --> 06:44:06,413
I need to lock out this knee so I'm nice and straight.

4309
06:44:06,754 --> 06:44:09,077
I'm gonna sit back onto my heel.

4310
06:44:09,438 --> 06:44:11,000
So now look at this back foot.

4311
06:44:11,020 --> 06:44:12,683
I'm not curling the toe under.

4312
06:44:12,663 --> 06:44:16,509
I'm putting it down like this so the top of my foot is flat to the floor.

4313
06:44:17,090 --> 06:44:20,335
And I'm going to sit my hips back to that heel.

4314
06:44:20,756 --> 06:44:26,124
Now from there, I can already feel a little bit of a stretch in the adductor.

4315
06:44:26,425 --> 06:44:39,666
Now if you don't really try to square your chest towards the floor, now from there, if you don't feel a big stretch already, we're going to come down to the elbows and we're just going to hang out in this position for 15 seconds.

4316
06:44:39,646 --> 06:44:42,949
Alright, so I should feel that stretch all through the adductors.

4317
06:44:42,989 --> 06:44:44,311
That's the inside of the leg.

4318
06:44:44,791 --> 06:44:48,175
After 15 seconds, I'm going to switch over to that other side.

4319
06:44:48,755 --> 06:44:49,436
Same thing.

4320
06:44:49,776 --> 06:44:52,659
For my glute stretch, I'm going to pull this knee back.

4321
06:44:52,980 --> 06:44:56,103
Now make sure that this other leg stays down on the floor.

4322
06:44:56,383 --> 06:45:00,287
So I need my right knee and my right heel down through the ground.

4323
06:45:00,567 --> 06:45:05,232
I'm not going to lift off and I'm just going to lay my head back and just pull

4324
06:45:05,212 --> 06:45:08,155
this knee as far towards the chest as I can.

4325
06:45:08,555 --> 06:45:14,020
Now, a lot of you, as you pull, the tendency is to rise here because we're tight in the hip flexors.

4326
06:45:14,440 --> 06:45:24,529
If that's the case, try to have somebody hold that leg down or strap it down with a band or just realize that you don't have that range of motion yet and you can only pull to right here.

4327
06:45:24,910 --> 06:45:32,957
But this is a glute stretch for this left leg, but at the same time, for a lot of you, this will be a hip flexor stretch on that right side.

4328
06:45:32,937 --> 06:45:35,843
So I'm just gonna pull back, hold for 15 seconds.

4329
06:45:36,305 --> 06:45:42,218
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side, trying to get full range of motion with that other leg.

4330
06:45:42,438 --> 06:45:45,425
So for our hip flexor stretch, make sure that we have something soft.

4331
06:45:45,485 --> 06:45:47,650
I don't want you guys putting your knee on a hardwood.

4332
06:45:47,870 --> 06:45:51,739
Make sure you have a pad or a soft floor to do this stretch on.

4333
06:45:51,719 --> 06:45:53,522
So I'm just going to go on one knee.

4334
06:45:53,582 --> 06:45:56,486
This knee is going to go 90 degrees.

4335
06:45:56,546 --> 06:45:57,448
So I'm 90 there.

4336
06:45:57,808 --> 06:46:00,613
My ankle is directly underneath that knee.

4337
06:46:00,973 --> 06:46:03,257
Now from here, I just got to get up nice and tall.

4338
06:46:03,617 --> 06:46:08,304
Some of you are already going to feel a stretch in the hip flexor because we're extra tight.

4339
06:46:08,665 --> 06:46:11,650
Now from there, I'm just going to lean forward.

4340
06:46:11,930 --> 06:46:14,714
So I should have this knee back behind the hip.

4341
06:46:15,095 --> 06:46:20,443
And now from there, I'm just raising straight up and I'm going to hold.

4342
06:46:20,423 --> 06:46:27,192
All right, so I feel a big stretch from here all the way down through the bottom of that hip flexor.

4343
06:46:27,933 --> 06:46:31,698
After 15 seconds, I'm gonna switch over to that other side and do the same thing.

4344
06:46:31,798 --> 06:46:37,105
For my calf stretch, I'm basically gonna do what they would call a downward dog in yoga.

4345
06:46:37,466 --> 06:46:40,710
So I'm here, I'm gonna push back like this.

4346
06:46:40,790 --> 06:46:42,212
I'm gonna straighten out my arms.

4347
06:46:42,192 --> 06:46:43,954
And now I'm just going to cross over.

4348
06:46:44,335 --> 06:46:53,967
So I'm going to put my left foot over that right foot and I'm going to try to get that right heel down towards the floor or as close as I can.

4349
06:46:54,448 --> 06:46:56,210
So I do have a straight knee.

4350
06:46:56,630 --> 06:46:59,114
So we're stretching out what's called the gastrocnemius.

4351
06:46:59,174 --> 06:47:00,876
That's the outside calf muscle.

4352
06:47:01,136 --> 06:47:07,324
So I shouldn't feel the stretch as much down in the ankle and the Achilles as we would on some of our hip mobility drills.

4353
06:47:07,705 --> 06:47:12,030
We should feel it on the outside of that calf muscle.

4354
06:47:12,837 --> 06:47:15,947
A lot of us aren't going to be able to get our heel all the way to the floor.

4355
06:47:16,008 --> 06:47:16,730
That's okay.

4356
06:47:17,091 --> 06:47:20,282
Just work on getting it down as low as we can.

4357
06:47:20,342 --> 06:47:24,315
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side.

4358
06:47:27,113 --> 06:47:27,754
What's up guys?

4359
06:47:28,034 --> 06:47:32,379
Minimum dose advice for day two and day four of phase five.

4360
06:47:32,580 --> 06:47:36,464
Really there is no minimum dose advice for this workout as you see.

4361
06:47:36,525 --> 06:47:39,048
It's extremely short, extremely fast.

4362
06:47:39,728 --> 06:47:48,379
There are some days in our workouts where we're going to go short and light and efficient because we can't just beat the body up

4363
06:47:48,359 --> 06:47:49,380
all year round.

4364
06:47:49,520 --> 06:47:54,266
Sometimes we have to have those days that are actually a little bit lighter than previous phases.

4365
06:47:54,326 --> 06:47:56,629
So you'll notice that there's no mobility.

4366
06:47:56,669 --> 06:48:03,497
You should have built all the mobility by now if that's not the case and add in some mobility drills from the earlier phases.

4367
06:48:03,777 --> 06:48:07,542
But most of you guys have built enough mobility, so we're not super setting anything there.

4368
06:48:07,842 --> 06:48:11,406
So you can pretty much do this workout as is the leg climb.

4369
06:48:11,827 --> 06:48:13,028
You're going to get a good burn.

4370
06:48:13,589 --> 06:48:17,353
You could increase the reps if you don't feel a big burn, but you really should.

4371
06:48:17,333 --> 06:48:19,516
Feel it burn in the front core.

4372
06:48:19,857 --> 06:48:24,703
Hand walkout is not really a big burning exercise, but it is fatiguing overall.

4373
06:48:24,784 --> 06:48:28,269
It's full body stability, so that is pretty tiring.

4374
06:48:28,749 --> 06:48:34,978
Da Vinci plank, the way we make that harder is we always just load up more and more and more, so we never want to increase reps.

4375
06:48:35,038 --> 06:48:36,380
We don't want to hold for longer.

4376
06:48:36,661 --> 06:48:42,649
We just want to see how much total weight we can hold in that 30 second time frame with perfect form.

4377
06:48:42,629 --> 06:48:51,745
and then that cable drop step rotation, same thing, the reps are pretty low, so we can progressively overload by increasing the amount of weight we use.

4378
06:49:02,761 --> 06:49:05,847
So for my leg climbs, I'm going to go down on my back.

4379
06:49:05,907 --> 06:49:08,031
I'm going to make sure that my back is nice and flat.

4380
06:49:08,411 --> 06:49:11,016
I'm going to go about six inches off the ground with this left leg.

4381
06:49:11,336 --> 06:49:15,384
And then I'm going to go straight up 90 degree angle with that right leg.

4382
06:49:15,464 --> 06:49:16,806
Some of you will be a little less.

4383
06:49:16,846 --> 06:49:17,427
That's okay.

4384
06:49:17,788 --> 06:49:18,189
All right.

4385
06:49:18,209 --> 06:49:21,134
So what I'm going to do is three grabs to the leg.

4386
06:49:21,174 --> 06:49:24,600
So it's going to be left, right, left.

4387
06:49:25,101 --> 06:49:25,342
All right.

4388
06:49:25,923 --> 06:49:27,165
Left, right, left.

4389
06:49:27,584 --> 06:49:48,175
left and i'm not really grabbing and pulling on my leg much i'm just doing this so that i can really control that contraction from the abs all right so left right left and come back down left right left and come back down so this is really isolating the abs we're also getting a very good

4390
06:49:48,155 --> 06:49:56,797
hamstring stretch, and for some of you it'll be an opposite hip flexor stretch because when we're in that 90 degree angle, a lot of you guys like to lift that leg.

4391
06:49:57,138 --> 06:50:03,514
So we're getting hip flexor, we're getting hamstring, and then you're gonna feel we're gonna get a huge abdominal contraction.

4392
06:50:03,915 --> 06:50:04,476
Let's do it.

4393
06:50:25,128 --> 06:50:36,187
So for my hand walkouts, I'm gonna go wrist directly underneath the shoulder, knees directly underneath the hips, and then I'm just pushing up a couple inches so my knees are off the ground.

4394
06:50:36,628 --> 06:50:43,280
I'm gonna keep my torso nice and flat, and I'm just gonna step forward a couple inches with the hands every time.

4395
06:50:43,660 --> 06:50:45,263
Now for some of you,

4396
06:50:45,563 --> 06:50:50,629
You might only be able to get about right there, and then you walk it back.

4397
06:50:50,669 --> 06:50:52,151
That counts as one rep.

4398
06:50:52,171 --> 06:50:58,219
The better you get, the further out you can actually get the hands.

4399
06:50:58,900 --> 06:51:03,806
I don't want you to get so far that you start to hyperextend from the lower back.

4400
06:51:04,106 --> 06:51:07,611
I want you to go to that point where you can still stay flat from the back.

4401
06:51:07,631 --> 06:51:13,258
You can feel a good burn in the core, but you're not quite losing that position, all right?

4402
06:51:13,238 --> 06:51:18,265
Should feel this a lot in the front abs, a little bit in the obliques, a little bit in the low back.

4403
06:51:18,686 --> 06:51:22,871
Of course, we're going to feel a lot in the shoulders because we're getting a lot of shoulder stability.

4404
06:51:23,633 --> 06:51:26,036
This is going to be a full body stability exercise.

4405
06:51:26,376 --> 06:51:28,479
You should feel a little bit of a burn in the core.

4406
06:51:28,880 --> 06:51:35,449
If you feel it more in your lower back, then you're probably doing something wrong and you'll want to regress this to a normal plank.

4407
06:51:48,440 --> 06:51:51,003
So for the DaVinci plank, I'm gonna use a cable machine.

4408
06:51:51,283 --> 06:51:53,446
If you don't have a cable machine, we could use a band.

4409
06:51:53,866 --> 06:51:59,412
And if you don't have a band, then we're gonna go with this side plank with a leg raise, which I'll show in a second.

4410
06:51:59,452 --> 06:52:05,218
But if we have that cable machine, right now I'm going on 100 pounds because I've been doing this for a long time.

4411
06:52:05,679 --> 06:52:07,321
I would really say start very light.

4412
06:52:07,461 --> 06:52:09,283
Start all the way at 30 pounds.

4413
06:52:09,303 --> 06:52:10,444
Try it out, see how it feels.

4414
06:52:10,504 --> 06:52:15,730
If it's easy, then go up and up and up until we can find that perfect weight.

4415
06:52:15,710 --> 06:52:21,152
But so I'm going to set this up where the cable is in line with my mid chest.

4416
06:52:21,172 --> 06:52:22,417
Now I'm just going to step out.

4417
06:52:22,437 --> 06:52:23,762
I'm going to pick it up.

4418
06:52:23,945 --> 06:52:47,185
take a step out I'm in this wide stance my chest is right over my pelvis so I'm not leaning shoulders nice and flat now from there I'm gonna lift up this outside foot so I'm gonna lift up my left leg about an inch off the ground and I'm just stabilizing so I got to stabilize with this right leg but more importantly this left side of the core right now is fired up and I'm going left arm out

4419
06:52:47,165 --> 06:52:49,230
My shoulders should be completely flat.

4420
06:52:49,551 --> 06:52:51,656
Most of you naturally will be here.

4421
06:52:52,077 --> 06:52:55,586
I need you to fight with that core to get your shoulders flat.

4422
06:52:55,967 --> 06:52:58,032
And we're holding, we're feeling that in the left oblique.

4423
06:52:58,052 --> 06:53:00,538
We'll feel it a little bit in the right oblique and the core as well.

4424
06:53:01,140 --> 06:53:03,385
But mostly on that left side of the core.

4425
06:53:03,365 --> 06:53:06,533
And then after we're done, make sure that you walk it back in.

4426
06:53:06,594 --> 06:53:08,799
Don't just let it pull you back in, of course.

4427
06:53:09,120 --> 06:53:12,249
So if we don't have the cable machine, we could use a band.

4428
06:53:12,549 --> 06:53:17,864
I'm using a one inch perform better band, hook it up to a tree or to a power rack or something nice and stable.

4429
06:53:18,204 --> 06:53:19,568
I'm going to pull out

4430
06:53:19,548 --> 06:53:22,491
as far as I can really to get some really good tension on that.

4431
06:53:22,872 --> 06:53:24,494
And then I'm going to pull that right foot up.

4432
06:53:24,554 --> 06:53:26,856
Of course, that outside foot is always the one that comes up.

4433
06:53:27,337 --> 06:53:30,680
Other arm straight out and I'm just holding in that position.

4434
06:53:30,700 --> 06:53:32,042
So that's actually not enough tension.

4435
06:53:32,442 --> 06:53:39,050
I'd have to go a little further and then from there pull up and I'm not letting that band pull me in.

4436
06:53:39,130 --> 06:53:43,214
So I'm staying nice and strong with that right oblique and I'm flat with the shoulders.

4437
06:53:43,555 --> 06:53:48,340
I'm consciously squeezing the core in this position for the full duration of the set.

4438
06:53:48,320 --> 06:53:54,108
Now, if you don't have the cable or the band, then you're just gonna go in a side plank position, and you're gonna get nice and flat.

4439
06:53:54,148 --> 06:54:05,322
So option one is bent knees, stack them together, stack the legs, get nice and flat here, and then we're just gonna lift this leg, stay nice and flat through that knee all the way through the shoulder.

4440
06:54:05,723 --> 06:54:09,728
I'm feeling that on the inside, so I'm feeling that on the right side of the core.

4441
06:54:10,029 --> 06:54:11,451
I'm gonna feel that in the hips here.

4442
06:54:11,771 --> 06:54:13,453
I'm gonna feel that in my right hip as well.

4443
06:54:13,814 --> 06:54:15,576
I can just get this other arm.

4444
06:54:15,556 --> 06:54:18,684
and hang out in this position, nice and strong and stable.

4445
06:54:19,085 --> 06:54:31,236
If that is too easy, then go straight leg, and we're up nice and flat from the feet all the way through the shoulders, squeeze that core, and then we're just gonna lift here and other hand up, all right?

4446
06:54:55,837 --> 06:55:04,501
Okay, for the cable drop step rotation, I'm just going to use a cable, start light and build up gradually, or if you don't have a cable, you could use a band.

4447
06:55:04,922 --> 06:55:10,858
I'm going to interlock my fingers over the handle and just step it out just a little bit, all right?

4448
06:55:10,838 --> 06:55:13,304
We're going to come into a quarter squat position.

4449
06:55:13,365 --> 06:55:17,816
Now to open up that way, I got to drive off the right foot.

4450
06:55:18,197 --> 06:55:23,070
I'm going to open up and I'm going to get that left foot down so that that toe is pointing that way.

4451
06:55:23,330 --> 06:55:23,551
All right.

4452
06:55:23,992 --> 06:55:27,902
I don't want you to go into rotation until that foot is down.

4453
06:55:27,882 --> 06:55:34,014
So I'm here, I push into position, and then from here I can open up and explode there.

4454
06:55:34,034 --> 06:55:43,111
Now on the way back, I'm coming halfway, hands right in front of the chest, fire up that core, two to three seconds, and then release back to the start.

4455
06:55:43,492 --> 06:55:48,000
So it's foot down, explode, come back, hold.

4456
06:55:47,980 --> 06:55:48,641
and release.

4457
06:55:49,542 --> 06:56:02,217
So the reason that I want you to not just go into rotation but get the foot down first is we're then going to work that kind of recoil core, we're going to work as the full fascia system instead of just muscular power.

4458
06:56:03,118 --> 06:56:13,330
So we're getting here and then we get a good recoil through the core and we get here and then coming back we get that pause and then release.

4459
06:56:13,310 --> 06:56:18,767
do the desired reps to one side, and then go back and do the desired reps to the other side.

4460
06:56:19,129 --> 06:56:23,623
We should feel a burn through the core, especially the side in the obliques.

4461
06:56:27,130 --> 06:56:31,614
What's up guys, quick minimum dose advice for phase five, day three.

4462
06:56:32,055 --> 06:56:42,125
So if we're pressed for time, take out that foam roller circuit, do the dynamic warm up, do the band deceleration, take out the back pedal deceleration.

4463
06:56:43,906 --> 06:56:47,530
Do the angled cone bounds, if you want to take that down to two sets you can.

4464
06:56:48,090 --> 06:56:53,035
Do the rotational hurdle jumps, if you have the time, you can take that down to two sets as well.

4465
06:56:53,876 --> 06:56:55,838
Take out the one leg jump,

4466
06:56:55,818 --> 06:56:59,244
Still do the one foot approach jump.

4467
06:56:59,264 --> 06:57:01,788
We still got to rep out those one foot mechanics.

4468
06:57:01,988 --> 06:57:04,131
Do the one leg RDL swings.

4469
06:57:04,171 --> 06:57:05,514
It's already very low rep.

4470
06:57:05,534 --> 06:57:07,897
We're only doing a couple reps on each side.

4471
06:57:08,559 --> 06:57:11,704
Do the single leg broad hop to vertical hop.

4472
06:57:11,724 --> 06:57:15,590
If you want to take down the reps from four to two, you can do that.

4473
06:57:15,910 --> 06:57:17,573
So still do your four sets.

4474
06:57:17,553 --> 06:57:20,257
but keep it down at around two reps each side.

4475
06:57:20,557 --> 06:57:24,223
If you have time, do the hyperextension hold plate drop.

4476
06:57:24,243 --> 06:57:33,256
It's good to go back to an exercise that we've done before and be able to progressively overload so we can now get a harder squeeze in that post chain.

4477
06:57:33,757 --> 06:57:38,404
We can use a heavier weight than we're doing back when we did these in phase one.

4478
06:57:38,804 --> 06:57:43,932
So if you can do that, if you had to take it down to two sets, that's okay.

4479
06:57:43,912 --> 06:57:50,083
If you have to skip the sub max long duration jumps, you can do that because we're already doing it in Monday, Friday.

4480
06:57:50,464 --> 06:57:52,227
I really recommend that you get that in.

4481
06:57:53,049 --> 06:58:02,266
But of course, if we are pressed for time or our volume on the court is so high that we have to decrease our volume here, that is one exercise that you could take out.

4482
06:58:02,286 --> 06:58:04,570
As always, do our 7-Eleven breathing.

4483
06:58:04,550 --> 06:58:07,634
and then we don't even have a static stretch in here.

4484
06:58:07,754 --> 06:58:13,160
So if you need the static stretch because you're overly tight, you can always add it in at the end of your workout.

4485
06:58:13,521 --> 06:58:15,083
Most of you guys probably don't need it.

4486
06:58:15,403 --> 06:58:15,783
Let's get it.

4487
06:58:15,884 --> 06:58:17,445
We're going to get through a foam roller circuit.

4488
06:58:17,586 --> 06:58:19,308
I have a long roller from Skills.

4489
06:58:19,548 --> 06:58:26,416
You can do long or you can do one of the shorter rollers that you can get from Skills online, or you can just get it from Walmart or Target.

4490
06:58:26,777 --> 06:58:32,143
So the first muscle that we're going to focus on is the glutes, one of the most important muscles for us to foam roll.

4491
06:58:32,123 --> 06:58:35,268
So you can either go this way or you can go vertical.

4492
06:58:35,609 --> 06:58:44,765
So if you go this way, we're just going to lean over to one side and then I'm just going to roll from the bottom of my glute all the way up to the top of my glute.

4493
06:58:44,785 --> 06:58:51,516
Now, always, if we want more pressure, we can cross over here and add a little more pressure to make it a little tougher.

4494
06:58:51,496 --> 06:58:58,007
Or we could go vertical here and then we could lean over and get the glute horizontally as well.

4495
06:58:58,387 --> 06:59:00,591
So the next one we're going to move down the posterior chain.

4496
06:59:00,631 --> 06:59:02,033
We're going to focus on the hamstrings.

4497
06:59:02,374 --> 06:59:10,808
So I'm just going to sit on the roller and I'm going to cross over this foot and I'm just going to roll from the bottom of my glute all the way to the top of my knee.

4498
06:59:11,148 --> 06:59:18,280
So I'm just going to start in the center and then I'm gradually going to rock over a little bit so I can get the outside of my hamstrings.

4499
06:59:18,260 --> 06:59:22,887
and then I'm gonna rock to the inside so I can get the inside of my hamstrings.

4500
06:59:23,153 --> 06:59:24,935
Now the next one we're going to do is the calves.

4501
06:59:25,235 --> 06:59:28,638
So we're just going to cross over and I'm going to push myself up.

4502
06:59:28,739 --> 06:59:36,947
So my hips are off the ground and I'm just going to roll basically from the bottom of the knee all the way up to the top of the ankle.

4503
06:59:37,007 --> 06:59:42,532
So we're going over that calf and also over that Achilles and our next one we're flipping over.

4504
06:59:42,612 --> 06:59:45,776
We're going hip flexor all the way down to the quad.

4505
06:59:45,796 --> 06:59:53,143
So I'm going to go on the side of the roller now and I'm just going to come down into a plank position and I'm going to roll

4506
06:59:53,123 --> 06:59:59,415
from that hip flexor all the way down towards the top of my thigh.

4507
07:00:00,117 --> 07:00:15,807
So I'm getting my whole quad in this one and if you can't get down to the quad muscles around your knee then start here and finish and then you would scoot up and then just focus on those lower quad muscles down around the knee.

4508
07:00:15,787 --> 07:00:17,551
Our next one is going to be for the adductors.

4509
07:00:17,571 --> 07:00:18,693
That's the inside of the leg.

4510
07:00:18,874 --> 07:00:20,617
So a lot of different ways that we can do this.

4511
07:00:20,938 --> 07:00:34,707
The way that I like to go is I like to just turn that roller here, come in a plank position, bring this foot up, and I'm just rolling from the inside, the top of the knee, all the way up through the groin area.

4512
07:00:36,475 --> 07:00:43,283
So we could go bent leg there or we could go straight leg there for a little bit deeper of a roll.

4513
07:00:43,484 --> 07:00:47,048
So after we're done with the foam rolling circuit, I like to get out a lacrosse ball.

4514
07:00:47,348 --> 07:00:50,593
You could use a golf ball, a baseball, anything hard.

4515
07:00:51,153 --> 07:00:53,857
And I'm just gonna really dig into that heel.

4516
07:00:53,897 --> 07:00:55,559
So I'm gonna apply some pressure in there.

4517
07:00:55,859 --> 07:00:59,884
I'm gonna go from the heel all the way down through the ball of the foot.

4518
07:00:59,864 --> 07:01:02,790
And I'm going to really loosen up that fascia.

4519
07:01:03,352 --> 07:01:09,264
A lot of times our fascia of the feet take a lot of excess stress because we're on our feet all day.

4520
07:01:09,565 --> 07:01:11,108
We're moving, we're cutting, we're jumping.

4521
07:01:11,449 --> 07:01:14,295
We got to really start to loosen that up.

4522
07:01:15,642 --> 07:01:20,534
Now after that, it's optional if you want to go up and work on the smaller muscles of the hip.

4523
07:01:20,555 --> 07:01:24,084
You can work on the smaller muscles of the shoulder up against a wall if you'd like to.

4524
07:01:24,104 --> 07:01:29,297
I just want to make sure that we get that foam roll circuit and we get that lacrosse ball on the feet.

4525
07:01:29,658 --> 07:01:31,322
Everything else is extra credit.

4526
07:01:34,424 --> 07:01:38,169
So the first thing we're gonna do for our dynamic warmup is stationary skips.

4527
07:01:38,449 --> 07:01:41,012
Now for all of these, you can take them on the move if you want.

4528
07:01:41,093 --> 07:01:45,058
For right now, I'm just gonna do them stationary, just in case you don't have much room.

4529
07:01:45,558 --> 07:01:52,147
So we're just going up with the right, up with the left, just like we're running, and vice versa on that other side.

4530
07:01:52,507 --> 07:01:56,172
All right, I'm staying stiff with the feet, so I'm not letting my heel collapse.

4531
07:01:56,212 --> 07:01:57,934
I wanna stay on the ball of the foot.

4532
07:01:57,914 --> 07:02:01,118
and I'm just gonna go about 50% of my max speed.

4533
07:02:01,459 --> 07:02:02,901
I'm not going too fast yet.

4534
07:02:03,221 --> 07:02:05,384
We're gonna go for 30 seconds on the skips.

4535
07:02:05,624 --> 07:02:10,170
For the seal jacks, it's basically like a jumping jack, except I'm gonna coordinate arms with the legs.

4536
07:02:10,190 --> 07:02:18,321
So I'm gonna go over with the right and over with the right hand at the same time, back to neutral, over with the left, over with the left hand.

4537
07:02:18,641 --> 07:02:20,864
And then I'm just gonna speed that up.

4538
07:02:20,884 --> 07:02:23,247
I'm gonna get a good little rhythm going here.

4539
07:02:23,227 --> 07:02:48,525
maybe somewhere between 30 and 50 percent of your max speed so we're not all out we're just getting that blood flowing we're gonna go for 30 seconds for the over under hamstring stretch i'm just gonna go over with the left leg i'm gonna come down touch the toe now if you can't touch the toe without rounding the back then just go mid-shin or even to the knees just as low as we can but we don't want to go to the point where we have to round our back

4540
07:02:48,505 --> 07:02:56,220
OK, so I'm going to get down, touch my toes back to neutral, and then I cross over the other way and I'm going the other side.

4541
07:02:59,879 --> 07:03:04,246
All right, we're gonna go five over and back, so it's 10 total touches.

4542
07:03:04,446 --> 07:03:09,794
For the quad hamstring leans, I'm just gonna go into a quad stretch, so I'm gonna pull my right foot up.

4543
07:03:10,074 --> 07:03:16,624
I wanna make sure that my heel is touching my hip in that position, and I'm not out like this, I'm keeping that knee in.

4544
07:03:17,045 --> 07:03:25,077
Now from there, I'm gonna keep the left knee straight, and I'm just gonna go into a lean as low as I can,

4545
07:03:25,057 --> 07:03:29,986
So I'm getting a really good stretch in the quad by going down and getting my knee back.

4546
07:03:30,326 --> 07:03:35,936
I'm getting it into the hip flexor a little bit more and I'm getting this hamstring a good stretch.

4547
07:03:36,618 --> 07:03:38,982
And I'm also working on my balance at the same time.

4548
07:03:39,302 --> 07:03:43,931
I'm going to go five leans and then I'm going to switch over five leans on the other side.

4549
07:03:44,572 --> 07:03:46,896
For the hip opener, we're going to go push up position.

