10:40:46,664 --> 10:40:49,748
On the barbell, we would normally finish here.

7063
10:40:50,289 --> 10:40:52,331
With the trap bar, we finish here.

7064
10:40:52,712 --> 10:40:56,157
So the elbows go backwards instead of out to the side.

7065
10:40:57,298 --> 10:41:13,139
Now, if these are too advanced for you because this is several years of strength training before you should really be doing explosive hang high pulls, if that's the case, I want you to go hinge and explode to the toes.

7066
10:41:13,539 --> 10:41:14,781
So it's just hinge here.

7067
10:41:15,419 --> 10:41:20,728
explode to the toes, and then back to that slight bend in the knee, hinge, boom, explode to the toes.

7068
10:41:21,069 --> 10:41:25,116
You're really thinking about pulling the hips through, squeezing the glutes.

7069
10:41:25,517 --> 10:41:30,625
This is going to set a good foundation and really build towards that hang high pull.

7070
10:41:30,886 --> 10:41:32,128
All right, let's get it.

7071
10:41:50,705 --> 10:41:58,197
So for my one leg RDL swing, what I'm going to do is hold two dumbbells by my side, come to an RDL position.

7072
10:41:58,258 --> 10:42:04,067
So that's one leg, slight bend in the knee, of course, from there it's a hip hinge, we're not going down with the knee.

7073
10:42:04,748 --> 10:42:13,122
Once I get down to that bottom position, which right now is going to be hands past the knee, so the dumbbells are going to be about mid-shin for most of us.

7074
10:42:13,303 --> 10:42:16,628
If you're a little more tight, it's okay to just go down to your knees.

7075
10:42:16,608 --> 10:42:22,119
So I'm gonna get down to that position and then I'm gonna aggressively swing as fast as I can.

7076
10:42:22,139 --> 10:42:27,309
I'm gonna keep my elbow straight and I'm gonna swing the dumbbells up over my head.

7077
10:42:27,650 --> 10:42:35,726
I'm gonna bring it down while I'm still on one leg to challenge our stability and then bring that other foot down, bring the dumbbells back down, okay?

7078
10:42:36,107 --> 10:42:38,211
So it's slight bend.

7079
10:42:38,191 --> 10:43:02,545
RDL as fast as we can explode up to that top position do not think about doing an RDL and then a lift with the arms the arms are just swinging from the momentum of that aggressive explosive hip extension okay so it's here swing them stabilize at the top bring it down come all the way down

7080
10:43:02,525 --> 10:43:10,018
Now, this is a very advanced exercise, so if you don't have the stability to do it on one leg, I'd rather you come to a split stance.

7081
10:43:10,138 --> 10:43:15,667
So, if you did it in a split stance, we would be here in a little baby split.

7082
10:43:16,288 --> 10:43:21,597
My feet have to be pretty narrow, I can't be very wide, otherwise I'm going to hit the dumbbell on my leg.

7083
10:43:22,235 --> 10:43:23,437
Here, baby split.

7084
10:43:23,497 --> 10:43:25,120
From there, it's a hip hinge.

7085
10:43:25,501 --> 10:43:27,064
Notice I'm on the ball of the foot.

7086
10:43:27,124 --> 10:43:31,552
I'm not on my heel on that back leg, but I am on my heel on the front leg.

7087
10:43:31,612 --> 10:43:35,018
So it's gonna be here and then boom, explode.

7088
10:43:35,479 --> 10:43:37,483
Come back down and reset.

7089
10:43:38,004 --> 10:43:38,725
Boom.

7090
10:43:38,705 --> 10:43:41,789
explode, come back down, reset.

7091
10:43:42,450 --> 10:43:48,598
Now, if you're gonna do that single leg RDL, start very light, start five or 10 pound dumbbells in each hand.

7092
10:43:49,359 --> 10:43:51,622
Once you're good to go, then you can start to go up.

7093
10:43:51,963 --> 10:43:54,586
Most of our athletes don't get past 20 pounds.

7094
10:43:54,606 --> 10:43:57,270
20 pounds is a pretty good weight.

7095
10:43:57,250 --> 10:44:03,819
as far as really just utilizing that hip extension velocity, hamstring and glute, instead of using the arms.

7096
10:44:04,140 --> 10:44:09,067
If you start to get too heavy, you're going to feel like you're really working your arms to lift, alright?

7097
10:44:09,448 --> 10:44:18,060
So, start light, gradually go up, let's get it.

7098
10:44:24,875 --> 10:44:30,663
So for our rear foot elevated split squat, if you have a Smith machine, I advise that we use that.

7099
10:44:30,883 --> 10:44:38,393
It's one of the best things that we can do for the RFPSS simply because we have enough stability to where we can really get max intent.

7100
10:44:38,433 --> 10:44:43,039
We can load up the weight and get explosive without worrying about the balance factor.

7101
10:44:43,339 --> 10:44:47,845
So it's one of the best ways to build pure strength and power in the rear foot elevated.

7102
10:44:47,825 --> 10:44:52,096
If you don't have a Smith machine, I would rather not go barbell.

7103
10:44:52,457 --> 10:44:54,122
I would rather just go to dumbbells.

7104
10:44:54,142 --> 10:44:57,150
So we're gonna do the same thing, just with dumbbells as heavy as you can.

7105
10:44:57,410 --> 10:44:59,877
So for this rear foot elevated,

7106
10:45:00,802 --> 10:45:03,626
We are going to go balanced glute and quad.

7107
10:45:03,686 --> 10:45:06,870
So sometimes we go ankle underneath the knee.

7108
10:45:06,890 --> 10:45:08,092
That's going to be more glute.

7109
10:45:08,112 --> 10:45:17,845
Right now at that bottom position, when I got my rear foot up and I'm down on my knee, I want my knee directly over the toe.

7110
10:45:18,205 --> 10:45:19,407
So not beyond the toe.

7111
10:45:19,527 --> 10:45:21,770
I just want it right over that toe.

7112
10:45:22,130 --> 10:45:24,193
So that's the position that we're going to work with.

7113
10:45:25,793 --> 10:45:31,842
Of course, we would always start with just the bar, and then we would gradually load up heavier and heavier if we're feeling good.

7114
10:45:32,863 --> 10:45:38,712
So, unrack it, and then it's control down, tap that knee, explode up as hard as I can.

7115
10:45:38,752 --> 10:45:43,479
Now, if I'm loaded heavy, of course I'm not gonna be able to get up very fast.

7116
10:45:43,759 --> 10:45:55,176
It should be taking between half a second and a second to get from the bottom all the way to the top, but we have the intent to move that bar with a fast speed.

7117
10:45:55,156 --> 10:45:59,240
Okay, so we have two options for unracking that bar.

7118
10:45:59,341 --> 10:46:06,268
So the first option is what I just described where we get that position from there and then we go up and we unrack.

7119
10:46:06,608 --> 10:46:20,083
The other option is just to mark out maybe with a piece of tape or a weight where our toe will be and then I can lift up with two and then I can get that toe right where that piece of tape is and then I can go back from there.

7120
10:46:20,063 --> 10:46:25,048
With the Smith machine, we have the luxury of doing that since we have some stability, we don't have to worry about the balance as much.

7121
10:46:25,469 --> 10:46:29,714
So I can go here, and then I can work from there.

7122
10:46:30,374 --> 10:46:35,300
Now, if you have the dumbbells, you don't have that luxury, so I would rather see you start from the bottom up.

7123
10:46:35,860 --> 10:46:43,048
I would rather see the dumbbells be on the floor, and then we set up in our position, grab the dumbbells, and then we go from there.

7124
10:46:43,428 --> 10:46:44,890
All right, let's get after it.

7125
10:46:55,973 --> 10:47:01,759
So for our Nordic hamstring curls, if you have a partner, this is the easiest way to go.

7126
10:47:01,799 --> 10:47:05,642
So your partner is going to sit behind you and hold down your ankles.

7127
10:47:06,043 --> 10:47:09,626
Now he's got to push pretty hard because your whole body weight is going to be coming down.

7128
10:47:09,706 --> 10:47:12,830
So if he's light, then you're going to lift him up.

7129
10:47:12,910 --> 10:47:14,912
So he's got to put a little bit of force in there.

7130
10:47:15,252 --> 10:47:17,114
Now I like to use a foam roller.

7131
10:47:17,394 --> 10:47:22,159
So you put the front of your ankle on a foam roller, and then you kind of dig your toes into the ground.

7132
10:47:22,539 --> 10:47:25,542
And it's just a little bit more comfortable on the ankles.

7133
10:47:25,522 --> 10:47:28,125
Now, I know a lot of you guys don't have a partner.

7134
10:47:28,726 --> 10:47:31,670
So this is how we would do it without a partner.

7135
10:47:32,031 --> 10:47:34,414
I would set up a barbell and make sure it's nice and heavy.

7136
10:47:34,834 --> 10:47:36,777
Make sure you got weights on both sides.

7137
10:47:37,197 --> 10:47:43,065
If you have a rack, then put it on the inside of the rack and then you put a weighted plate on the other side so that the barbell is not going to roll.

7138
10:47:43,486 --> 10:47:50,395
If you don't have a rack, we would use the barbell and then we would put a weight behind it and we would put another 45 pound plate in front of it.

7139
10:47:50,735 --> 10:47:54,280
So it's still kind of trapped in there and it's not going to roll back and forth.

7140
10:47:54,260 --> 10:48:03,004
this is optional but i like to use this because it's a little bit softer so i just use a pad there and then you always need a pad

7141
10:48:03,322 --> 10:48:33,328
for your knees all right so this is your setup now from here a lot of people go tall and they come down i if you're super advanced that's fine i would rather see a little bit of hip flexion so we're initially in just a little bit of hip flexion and then from there we're going down i want you to go basically as slow as you can or four seconds all the way down this is a lowering exercise once i get to the bottom i'm going to push back up and i'm coming all the way back up pretty fast you don't have to go slow on the way up

7142
10:48:33,308 --> 10:48:51,722
so initial hip flexion from there i'm not bending the hips more i stay in this initial hip flexion and i slowly lower lower lower lower push off and come back up if you can get a light push off that's great a lot of you guys to start

7143
10:48:51,702 --> 10:48:57,555
you're going to have to really push off hard to get back up, otherwise you're going to get stuck halfway up.

7144
10:48:57,816 --> 10:49:09,762
So if you get extremely good at this, we can eventually either go a very light tap or there's some people who have such good strength to body weight ratios, they can just put their hands behind their back and do the whole thing.

7145
10:49:09,742 --> 10:49:16,210
Now, you might cramp up on this exercise if you're not used to this intense of a hamstring contraction.

7146
10:49:16,250 --> 10:49:17,952
It's a very hard hamstring contraction.

7147
10:49:18,432 --> 10:49:20,975
So if you cramp, then stretch it out.

7148
10:49:21,456 --> 10:49:26,662
Try to get back into it, but this might be a little bit too advanced and your hamstrings aren't quite used to it yet.

7149
10:49:27,183 --> 10:49:31,007
So just try to make it easier or come up with an alternative if you continue to cramp.

7150
10:49:30,987 --> 10:49:36,113
Now the other mistake that people make is they point the toes and they go from there.

7151
10:49:36,434 --> 10:49:39,918
A lot of times your calf will start to cramp when you're in that position.

7152
10:49:39,958 --> 10:49:43,983
So I like to go toes kind of straight down into the ground.

7153
10:49:44,424 --> 10:49:54,717
So I'm digging into the ground and then I get a lot less in the calf and I really just feel it straight through the hamstrings, through the glutes and then you should feel a little bit through the low back as well.

7154
10:50:18,558 --> 10:50:22,583
For our 7-11 breathing, what we're going to do is just lay down on our back.

7155
10:50:22,703 --> 10:50:24,506
Make sure that you're in a relaxed place.

7156
10:50:24,546 --> 10:50:27,249
I know you're probably in a gym, so it might be a little bit loud.

7157
10:50:27,290 --> 10:50:33,798
If you have headphones, throw on some headphones, throw on some slow music, maybe some yoga or meditation type music.

7158
10:50:34,319 --> 10:50:40,267
And all I'm going to do is just lay down and I'm going to breathe in through my nose for seven seconds.

7159
10:50:40,547 --> 10:50:44,312
And I'm also going to breathe out through my nose for 11 seconds.

7160
10:50:44,292 --> 10:50:48,201
So I'm not going to open my mouth for this whole drill.

7161
10:50:48,622 --> 10:50:52,973
So it's in through the nose and I want to make sure that my stomach is rising.

7162
10:50:53,033 --> 10:51:00,411
Your chest will naturally rise a little bit, but most of you when you think of deep breathing, what happens is your belly stays still.

7163
10:51:01,370 --> 10:51:04,435
and your chest puffs up and your shoulders elevate.

7164
10:51:04,455 --> 10:51:11,186
That means we are not actually getting all of that air, all of that oxygen down to the deepest part of the lungs.

7165
10:51:11,546 --> 10:51:17,516
So I want you to think about letting the belly rise as you take that breath in, okay?

7166
10:51:17,536 --> 10:51:21,182
So we're here, in deep through the nose, let the stomach rise.

7167
10:51:23,505 --> 10:51:27,732
Seven seconds, once you finish that seven seconds, it's out through the nose.

7168
10:51:30,715 --> 10:51:32,638
and that stomach will fall, okay?

7169
10:51:33,359 --> 10:51:35,983
Initially, this is very uncomfortable for guys.

7170
10:51:36,744 --> 10:51:45,778
I've had NBA players that absolutely hated this until they're in their third or fourth session and they started to get used to it because you do have to learn how to pace your breaths.

7171
10:51:46,560 --> 10:51:54,552
If you just breathe in as hard as you can and breathe out as hard as you can, you're not gonna be able to go for seven in and 11 out.

7172
10:51:54,572 --> 10:51:58,478
You gotta learn to go very slow and pace that breath, okay?

7173
10:51:58,728 --> 10:52:27,486
this is doing a lot of stuff I mean for one we're helping you expand the lungs we're teaching you how to to breathe yourself into a more calmer state but from a recovery standpoint this could possibly be the best thing that you could do after a workout better than foam rolling better than static stretching because after a workout we're in that sympathetic state that's that fight that's that workout that's that game mode okay I got to get you to the parasympathetic state that's relax recover all recovery

7174
10:52:27,736 --> 10:52:30,240
happens in the parasympathetic state.

7175
10:52:30,962 --> 10:52:34,909
So if I'm still hyped up after the workout, I'm killing my recovery.

7176
10:52:35,270 --> 10:52:48,934
So as soon as we're done with the workout, we want to do these breathing exercises to get us into that parasympathetic state and then I can really start to aid my recovery and I'm back better than ever tomorrow, ready to train again.

7177
10:52:50,686 --> 10:52:53,991
So the first one for our static stretch is just going to be a basic quad stretch.

7178
10:52:54,011 --> 10:52:58,277
So I'm just going to go heel to hip and I'm just going to get up nice and tall.

7179
10:52:58,577 --> 10:53:05,367
I'm going to raise my opposite hand and I'm just going to hold for 15 seconds and then I'm going to switch over to the other side.

7180
10:53:05,667 --> 10:53:09,152
If you need to hold on to something for balance, that's okay.

7181
10:53:09,432 --> 10:53:16,963
We're not going to get the same arm raise, but you can hold on and just make sure that we're nice and tall and that heel is touching the hip the whole time.

7182
10:53:16,943 --> 10:53:21,274
For the elevated hamstring stretch, I'm just gonna use a bench, a box, a chair.

7183
10:53:21,695 --> 10:53:23,660
I'm just gonna get my heel on there.

7184
10:53:24,020 --> 10:53:26,206
That toe is pointed up towards the ceiling.

7185
10:53:26,487 --> 10:53:28,572
And then I'm just gonna hinge from the hips.

7186
10:53:28,852 --> 10:53:31,058
So I don't wanna lean forward and round my back.

7187
10:53:31,359 --> 10:53:33,163
I'm just gonna lean forward.

7188
10:53:33,143 --> 10:53:53,886
from the hips keeping my back nice and straight if you want to reach down and touch your ankle or touch your toe you can but don't reach down and start to bend over from the back so i like to just keep my hands here to make sure that i'm not rounding the upper back and i'm just going to hold 15 seconds and then i'm going to switch over to the other side

7189
10:53:54,237 --> 10:53:56,080
15 seconds on the other side as well.

7190
10:53:56,220 --> 10:53:58,504
We should feel this stretch all in the hamstrings.

7191
10:53:58,524 --> 10:53:59,966
So that is the back of the thigh.

7192
10:54:00,186 --> 10:54:04,393
We'll feel it a little bit down into the calves, but we should feel it mostly hamstrings.

7193
10:54:04,513 --> 10:54:08,218
For our adductor stretch, I'm just gonna go one leg out.

7194
10:54:08,359 --> 10:54:10,782
I need to lock out this knee so I'm nice and straight.

7195
10:54:11,143 --> 10:54:13,466
I'm gonna sit back onto my heel.

7196
10:54:13,807 --> 10:54:15,389
So now look at this back foot.

7197
10:54:15,409 --> 10:54:17,072
I'm not curling the toe under.

7198
10:54:17,052 --> 10:54:20,877
I'm putting it down like this so the top of my foot is flat to the floor.

7199
10:54:21,458 --> 10:54:24,702
And I'm gonna sit my hips back to that heel.

7200
10:54:25,122 --> 10:54:30,469
Now from there, I can already feel a little bit of a stretch in the adductor.

7201
10:54:30,790 --> 10:54:44,207
Now if you don't really try to square your chest towards the floor, now from there, if you don't feel a big stretch already, we're gonna come down to the elbows and we're just gonna hang out in this position for 15 seconds.

7202
10:54:44,187 --> 10:54:47,334
Alright, so I should feel that stretch all through the adductors.

7203
10:54:47,374 --> 10:54:48,697
That's the inside of the leg.

7204
10:54:49,178 --> 10:54:52,545
After 15 seconds, I'm gonna switch over to that other side.

7205
10:54:53,147 --> 10:54:53,848
Same thing.

7206
10:54:54,169 --> 10:54:57,075
For my glute stretch, I'm gonna pull this knee back.

7207
10:54:57,356 --> 10:55:00,643
Now make sure that this other leg stays down on the floor.

7208
10:55:00,623 --> 10:55:04,608
So I need my right knee and my right heel down through the ground.

7209
10:55:04,928 --> 10:55:12,577
I'm not going to lift off, and I'm just going to lay my head back and just pull this knee as far towards the chest as I can.

7210
10:55:12,937 --> 10:55:18,423
Now, a lot of you, as you pull, the tendency is to rise here because we're tight in the hip flexors.

7211
10:55:18,844 --> 10:55:24,150
If that's the case, try to have somebody hold that leg down or strap it down with a band.

7212
10:55:24,130 --> 10:55:28,879
or just realize that you don't have that range of motion yet and you can only pull to right here.

7213
10:55:29,280 --> 10:55:36,934
But this is a glute stretch for this left leg, but at the same time, for a lot of you, this will be a hip flexor stretch on that right side.

7214
10:55:37,455 --> 10:55:40,240
So I'm just gonna pull back, hold for 15 seconds.

7215
10:55:40,701 --> 10:55:46,712
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side, trying to get full range of motion with that other leg.

7216
10:55:46,692 --> 10:55:49,775
So for our hip flexor stretch, make sure that we have something soft.

7217
10:55:49,815 --> 10:55:51,997
I don't want you guys putting your knee on a hardwood.

7218
10:55:52,237 --> 10:55:55,880
Make sure you have a pad or a soft floor to do this stretch on.

7219
10:55:56,361 --> 10:55:57,922
So I'm just going to go on one knee.

7220
10:55:58,323 --> 10:56:00,845
This knee is going to go 90 degrees.

7221
10:56:00,925 --> 10:56:01,866
So I'm 90 there.

7222
10:56:02,186 --> 10:56:04,969
My ankle is directly underneath that knee.

7223
10:56:05,349 --> 10:56:07,631
Now from here, I just got to get up nice and tall.

7224
10:56:07,992 --> 10:56:12,676
Some of you are already going to feel a stretch in the hip flexor because we're extra tight.

7225
10:56:13,036 --> 10:56:16,159
Now from there, I'm just going to lean forward.

7226
10:56:16,139 --> 10:56:19,426
So I should have this knee back behind the hip.

7227
10:56:19,446 --> 10:56:24,215
And now from there, I'm just raising straight up and I'm going to hold.

7228
10:56:24,255 --> 10:56:25,658
All right.

7229
10:56:25,698 --> 10:56:31,590
So I feel a big stretch from here all the way down through the bottom of that hip flexor.

7230
10:56:32,331 --> 10:56:36,139
After 15 seconds, I'm going to switch over to that other side and do the same thing.

7231
10:56:36,119 --> 10:56:41,448
For my calf stretch, I'm basically going to do what they would call a downward dog in yoga.

7232
10:56:41,829 --> 10:56:45,055
So I'm here, I'm going to push back like this.

7233
10:56:45,155 --> 10:56:48,340
I'm going to straighten out my arms and now I'm just going to cross over.

7234
10:56:48,741 --> 10:56:58,498
So I'm going to put my left foot over that right foot and I'm going to try to get that right heel down towards the floor or as close as I can.

7235
10:56:58,478 --> 10:57:05,234
So I do have a straight knee, so we're stretching out what's called the gastrocnemius, that's the outside calf muscle.

7236
10:57:05,514 --> 10:57:11,689
So I shouldn't feel the stretch as much down in the ankle and the Achilles as we would on some of our hip mobility drills.

7237
10:57:12,070 --> 10:57:16,420
We should feel it on the outside of that calf muscle.

7238
10:57:17,210 --> 10:57:20,338
A lot of us aren't going to be able to get our heel all the way to the floor.

7239
10:57:20,378 --> 10:57:21,099
That's okay.

7240
10:57:21,460 --> 10:57:24,668
Just work on getting it down as low as we can.

7241
10:57:24,708 --> 10:57:28,738
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side.

7242
10:57:31,418 --> 10:57:36,528
What's up guys, quick minimum dose advice for phase nine, day one and day four.

7243
10:57:37,290 --> 10:57:42,400
So always do our dynamic warm up if you want to skip that foam roller circuit you can.

7244
10:57:42,961 --> 10:57:49,073
If we have to skip anything today, just skip the one-two push out and the hip swivel back pedal.

7245
10:57:49,053 --> 10:57:53,643
So take out the agility and do everything else on today's program.

7246
10:57:54,024 --> 10:57:58,815
Of course, we want to do those agility drills, but if you're really short on time, cut those two out.

7247
10:57:59,757 --> 10:58:07,855
We are on this six day a week program, so four days of lower body, which means by nature, our workouts need to be short and more efficient.

7248
10:58:07,835 --> 10:58:15,249
If we're in the gym for longer than an hour with this workout, you're doing too much, you should probably be cutting out some of these drills.

7249
10:58:15,750 --> 10:58:29,996
This entire workout should probably only take you around 45 minutes, so you should be able to get in and get a good high intensity session and get out and start your recovery process because we gotta recover for tomorrow's lower body workout.

7250
10:58:30,357 --> 10:58:31,058
Let's do it.

7251
10:58:31,038 --> 10:58:32,621
So we're going to get through a foam roller circuit.

7252
10:58:32,761 --> 10:58:34,464
I have a long roller from Skills.

7253
10:58:34,725 --> 10:58:41,597
You can do long or you can do one of the shorter rollers that you can get from Skills online, or you can just get it from Walmart or Target.

7254
10:58:41,958 --> 10:58:47,308
So the first muscle that we're going to focus on is the glutes, one of the most important muscles for us to foam roll.

7255
10:58:47,288 --> 10:58:50,453
So you can either go this way or you can go vertical.

7256
10:58:50,793 --> 10:58:59,948
So if you go this way, we're just going to lean over to one side and then I'm just going to roll from the bottom of my glute all the way up to the top of my glute.

7257
10:58:59,968 --> 10:59:06,698
Now, always, if we want more pressure, we can cross over here and add a little more pressure to make it a little tougher.

7258
10:59:06,678 --> 10:59:13,185
or we could go vertical here and then we can lean over and get the glute horizontally as well.

7259
10:59:13,566 --> 10:59:15,768
So the next one, we're going to move down the posterior chain.

7260
10:59:15,808 --> 10:59:17,210
We're going to focus on the hamstrings.

7261
10:59:17,550 --> 10:59:25,960
So I'm just going to sit on the roller and I'm going to cross over this foot and I'm just going to roll from the bottom of my glute all the way to the top of my knee.

7262
10:59:26,320 --> 10:59:33,428
So I'm just going to start in the center and then I'm gradually going to rock over a little bit so I can get the outside of my hamstrings.

7263
10:59:33,408 --> 10:59:38,119
and then I'm gonna rock to the inside so I can get the inside of my hamstrings.

7264
10:59:38,335 --> 10:59:40,117
Now the next one we're going to do is the calves.

7265
10:59:40,418 --> 10:59:43,822
So we're just going to cross over and I'm going to push myself up.

7266
10:59:43,902 --> 10:59:52,132
So my hips are off the ground and I'm just going to roll basically from the bottom of the knee all the way up to the top of the ankle.

7267
10:59:52,192 --> 10:59:57,719
So we're going over that calf and also over that Achilles and our next one we're flipping over.

7268
10:59:57,779 --> 11:00:00,923
We're going hip flexor all the way down to the quad.

7269
11:00:00,983 --> 11:00:08,292
So I'm going to go on the side of the roller now and I'm just going to come down into a plank position and I'm going to roll

7270
11:00:08,272 --> 11:00:14,582
from that hip flexor all the way down towards the top of my thigh.

7271
11:00:15,303 --> 11:00:18,288
So I'm getting my whole quad in this one.

7272
11:00:18,729 --> 11:00:23,977
And if you can't get down to the quad muscles around your knee, then start here and finish.

7273
11:00:24,438 --> 11:00:30,988
And then you would scoot up and then just focus on those lower quad muscles down around the knee.

7274
11:00:30,968 --> 11:00:33,875
Our next one's going to be for the adductors, that's the inside of the leg.

7275
11:00:34,055 --> 11:00:35,819
So a lot of different ways that we can do this.

7276
11:00:36,120 --> 11:00:49,872
The way that I like to go is I like to just turn that roller here, come in a plank position, bring this foot up, and I'm just rolling from the inside, the top of the knee, all the way up through the groin area.

7277
11:00:51,657 --> 11:00:58,467
So we could go bent leg there or we could go straight leg there for a little bit deeper of a roll.

7278
11:00:58,668 --> 11:01:02,233
So after we're done with the foam rolling circuit, I like to get out a lacrosse ball.

7279
11:01:02,534 --> 11:01:05,779
You could use a golf ball, a baseball, anything hard.

7280
11:01:06,339 --> 11:01:09,044
And I'm just gonna really dig into that heel.

7281
11:01:09,064 --> 11:01:10,726
So I'm gonna apply some pressure in there.

7282
11:01:11,047 --> 11:01:14,873
I'm gonna go from the heel all the way down through the ball of the foot.

7283
11:01:15,313 --> 11:01:18,458
And I'm gonna really loosen up that fascia.

7284
11:01:18,438 --> 11:01:26,290
A lot of times our fascia of the feet take a lot of excess stress because we're on our feet all day, we're moving, we're cutting, we're jumping.

7285
11:01:26,631 --> 11:01:29,335
We got to really start to loosen that up.

7286
11:01:30,917 --> 11:01:35,504
Now after that, it's optional if you want to go up and work on the smaller muscles of the hip.

7287
11:01:35,745 --> 11:01:39,270
You can work on the smaller muscles of the shoulder up against a wall if you'd like to.

7288
11:01:40,011 --> 11:01:44,478
I just want to make sure that we get that foam roll circuit and we get that lacrosse ball on the feet.

7289
11:01:44,838 --> 11:01:46,521
Everything else is extra credit.

7290
11:01:49,572 --> 11:01:53,317
So the first thing we're gonna do for our dynamic warmup is stationary skips.

7291
11:01:53,598 --> 11:01:56,161
Now for all of these, you can take them on the move if you want.

7292
11:01:56,241 --> 11:02:00,207
For right now, I'm just gonna do them stationary just in case you don't have much room.

7293
11:02:00,708 --> 11:02:07,317
So we're just going up with the right, up with the left, just like we're running, and vice versa on that other side.

7294
11:02:07,657 --> 11:02:11,343
All right, I'm staying stiff with the feet, so I'm not letting my heel collapse.

7295
11:02:11,363 --> 11:02:13,065
I wanna stay on the ball of the foot.

7296
11:02:13,045 --> 11:02:16,248
and I'm just gonna go about 50% of my max speed.

7297
11:02:16,609 --> 11:02:18,050
I'm not going too fast yet.

7298
11:02:18,371 --> 11:02:20,753
We're gonna go for 30 seconds on the skips.

7299
11:02:20,773 --> 11:02:25,318
For the seal jacks, it's basically like a jumping jack, except I'm gonna coordinate arms with the legs.

7300
11:02:25,338 --> 11:02:33,447
So I'm gonna go over with the right and over with the right hand at the same time, back to neutral, over with the left, over with the left hand.

7301
11:02:33,787 --> 11:02:36,009
And then I'm just gonna speed that up.

7302
11:02:36,029 --> 11:02:38,412
I'm gonna get a good little rhythm going here.

7303
11:02:38,392 --> 11:02:42,617
maybe somewhere between 30 and 50 percent of your max speed.

7304
11:02:42,677 --> 11:02:43,679
So we're not all out.

7305
11:02:44,139 --> 11:02:45,721
We're just getting that blood flowing.

7306
11:02:46,022 --> 11:02:47,363
We're going to go for 30 seconds.

7307
11:02:47,564 --> 11:02:51,889
For the over under hamstring stretch, I'm just going to go over with the left leg.

7308
11:02:52,209 --> 11:02:54,032
I'm going to come down, touch the toe.

7309
11:02:54,092 --> 11:03:00,180
Now, if you can't touch the toe without rounding the back, then just go mid shin or even to the knees just as low as we can.

7310
11:03:00,240 --> 11:03:03,724
But we don't want to go to the point where we have to round our back.

7311
11:03:03,704 --> 11:03:11,419
Okay, so I'm gonna get down, touch my toes, back to neutral, and then I cross over the other way, and I'm going the other side.

7312
11:03:15,027 --> 11:03:19,394
All right, we're going to go five over and back, so it's 10 total touches.

7313
11:03:19,594 --> 11:03:24,922
For the quad hamstring leans, I'm just going to go into a quad stretch, so I'm going to pull my right foot up.

7314
11:03:25,222 --> 11:03:30,470
I want to make sure that my heel is touching my hip in that position, and I'm not out like this.

7315
11:03:30,530 --> 11:03:31,772
I'm keeping that knee in.

7316
11:03:32,193 --> 11:03:40,225
Now from there, I'm going to keep the left knee straight, and I'm just going to go into a lean as low as I can.

7317
11:03:40,205 --> 11:03:45,134
So I'm getting a really good stretch in the quad by going down and getting my knee back.

7318
11:03:45,494 --> 11:03:51,084
I'm getting it into the hip flexor a little bit more and I'm getting this hamstring a good stretch.

7319
11:03:51,766 --> 11:03:54,130
And I'm also working on my balance at the same time.

7320
11:03:54,450 --> 11:03:59,079
I'm going to go five leans and then I'm going to switch over five leans on the other side.

7321
11:03:59,720 --> 11:04:02,044
For the hip opener, we're going to go push up position.

7322
11:04:02,969 --> 11:04:06,595
I'm going to go left leg up outside this left hand.

7323
11:04:07,016 --> 11:04:11,463
Now from here, I'm just going to rotate up and hold one, two, three.

7324
11:04:11,523 --> 11:04:13,807
Now I'm going to go elbow down towards the floor.

7325
11:04:14,127 --> 11:04:16,151
We might not be able to touch the elbow to the ground.

7326
11:04:16,191 --> 11:04:16,792
That's okay.

7327
11:04:17,112 --> 11:04:18,715
Let's just get as low as we can there.

7328
11:04:19,175 --> 11:04:20,117
One, two, three.

7329
11:04:20,097 --> 11:04:46,577
three and back up so three there three there I'm gonna go five cycles and then I'm gonna switch to the other side five and five same thing for the adductor hip flexor combo I'm going lateral with one skip so it's one skip lateral and I'm going down I'm trying to touch this floor keep this knee straight because I want to get that stretch on the inside of the leg in this adductor I'm going back with the hip like I would in a normal squat

7330
11:04:46,557 --> 11:05:15,535
and i'm getting nice and low touch the floor and i'm popping out to that other side all right so let's just hold about one second at the bottom and pop out i need five of these down and back so it's 10 total and then i immediately go into a hip flexor same thing with the skip and now i land i turn this foot forward i pivot i'm here knee a couple inches off the floor i'm gonna rotate hold one and then come back and it's to the other side

7331
11:05:20,594 --> 11:05:27,122
At the bottom of this stretch, I'm gonna get that really good stretch in the hip flexor, and I always need to turn towards the lead leg.

7332
11:05:27,142 --> 11:05:28,604
Don't make the mistake of going here.

7333
11:05:28,984 --> 11:05:37,035
You need to rotate towards that lead leg as far as we can, and I'm gonna feel it through that hip flexor, and then I pop out to the other side.

7334
11:05:37,155 --> 11:05:43,022
For the overhead deep squat progression, I'm going high with the hands, basic squat stance, so I'm a little wider than shoulder width.

7335
11:05:43,102 --> 11:05:47,007
I can point the toes out just a little bit, and then I'm just gonna go here,

7336
11:05:46,987 --> 11:06:05,502
it's gonna be a hamstring stretch one two three keep the hands down and come into a deep squat try to stay back on your heels if you can one two three rock forward so i'm on my toes now drive the knees out with the elbows hold one

7337
11:06:05,482 --> 11:06:24,672
two, three, rock it back, heels back down to the ground, one, two, three, I need one hand up, two hand up, not out here, we need it back behind the head, and stand, alright, so that's one cycle, we're going to go for three of these, so it's one, two, three,

7338
11:06:25,006 --> 11:06:42,559
one two three lean one two three heels back down one two three one up two up stand all right if you cannot get down in that deep position then let's just go as low as we can right here and then on the lean it's just going to look like this

7339
11:06:42,539 --> 11:06:47,388
All right, and then we're going to come back, hopefully parallel to the floor, one up, two up stand.

7340
11:06:47,748 --> 11:06:54,079
We just got to get as low as we can and every day try to progress so that we can get lower and lower, better range of motion.

7341
11:06:54,099 --> 11:06:56,924
So for the hip bridge, it's going to be a very basic hip bridge.

7342
11:06:56,985 --> 11:06:59,309
Even if you're an advanced athlete, I want you to do this version.

7343
11:06:59,689 --> 11:07:02,474
So we're going to get up nice and flat in a hip bridge.

7344
11:07:02,815 --> 11:07:04,518
I need to be flat through the hips.

7345
11:07:04,818 --> 11:07:07,483
I'm driving through my midfoot right now.

7346
11:07:07,463 --> 11:07:12,132
and now I'm just gonna squeeze my glutes together as hard as I possibly can.

7347
11:07:12,513 --> 11:07:26,181
So just holding in this position isn't that difficult, but if I squeeze my glutes together as hard as I can so they're rock solid, I'm gonna get a really good isometric contraction and I'm gonna activate a lot of muscle fibers.

7348
11:07:26,752 --> 11:07:33,363
And we're just going to hold in this position for 25 seconds with a full squeeze and then relax.

7349
11:07:33,784 --> 11:07:37,931
This is all for hip activation, getting those glutes fired up.

7350
11:07:37,951 --> 11:07:39,914
It's the most powerful muscle in the body.

7351
11:07:39,934 --> 11:07:42,178
So we got to get them revved up for our session.

7352
11:07:53,228 --> 11:07:57,155
So for our one-two push out, I just like to go on the lane line.

7353
11:07:57,475 --> 11:08:01,241
So we're looking at about 18 feet from baseline to the free throw line.

7354
11:08:01,462 --> 11:08:05,429
If you're not on a court, just mark out about 18 to 20 feet and let's work with that.

7355
11:08:05,549 --> 11:08:09,555
So if I'm going to my left, I need to lead with my left leg.

7356
11:08:09,896 --> 11:08:17,008
So I go over the line or if you have like rings or agility ladder or something, it's here, here,

7357
11:08:16,988 --> 11:08:17,950
here, here.

7358
11:08:18,291 --> 11:08:20,597
So we're pushing over the line and we're pushing back.

7359
11:08:20,958 --> 11:08:23,544
So it's left, right, left, right.

7360
11:08:23,584 --> 11:08:27,133
But when that right foot hits, now we push laterally as far as we can.

7361
11:08:27,574 --> 11:08:30,080
So it's left, right, left, right.

7362
11:08:30,701 --> 11:08:33,107
Land, left, right, left, right.

7363
11:08:33,087 --> 11:08:34,489
left, right, left, right.

7364
11:08:34,810 --> 11:08:40,178
Alright, you're pushing as far as you can with that right foot.

7365
11:08:40,779 --> 11:08:43,984
Now once I get down to that side, I would bring it back the other way.

7366
11:08:44,024 --> 11:08:51,957
So then it would be the other way, right, left, right, left, right, left, push, right, left, right, left,

7367
11:08:51,937 --> 11:09:16,257
right left right left alright so there's a lot of rhythm working on that pure quickness most importantly we're working on that punch out so boom punching when we slam the floor like that we really involve the tendons instead of just the muscles so I don't want it to be get the foot here and then a soft push out I want you to slam the floor and push out aggressively let's do it

7368
11:09:32,943 --> 11:09:41,278
So for my bound sprints, what I'm going to do, if you have a court and a half, then we're going to go a full court and a half with the bound sprint.

7369
11:09:41,559 --> 11:09:45,085
We're going to bound six times, three each leg, get as far as we can.

7370
11:09:45,426 --> 11:09:50,194
And then after that six, one, boom, hit the ground running, sprint it through a court and a half.

7371
11:09:50,214 --> 11:09:52,839
Now I know a lot of you guys don't have two courts set up this way.

7372
11:09:53,160 --> 11:09:55,163
So what you're going to do is just 54 meters.

7373
11:09:55,224 --> 11:09:56,065
So you could

7374
11:09:56,045 --> 11:10:01,180
Mark it out on a track or on a field or anywhere where you have 54 meters.

7375
11:10:01,621 --> 11:10:03,587
Look, if you don't have that space, it's okay.

7376
11:10:03,868 --> 11:10:11,269
Let's just do the bounds to half court or six times, which will get you around half court and then sprint it through the other half court, all right?

7377
11:10:11,249 --> 11:10:19,005
So, work with what you've got, but if you have the room, I'm going to start in a split stance, and I'm getting out as far as I can.

7378
11:10:19,426 --> 11:10:24,256
Of course, on my bounds, I do want to get some height with it, and I got to get off the ground quick, quick, quick.

7379
11:10:24,336 --> 11:10:30,810
So, it's going to be boom, one, two, three, four, five, six,

7380
11:10:30,790 --> 11:10:35,279
sprint it out as fast as we can through the rest of that 54 meters.

7381
11:10:35,299 --> 11:10:44,798
Main goals of this exercise is to get as far as we can with the bounds and then to get from point A to point B as fast as we possibly can.

7382
11:10:44,838 --> 11:10:46,582
So time yourself every session.

7383
11:10:46,602 --> 11:10:48,225
I want you to beat that record.

7384
11:10:56,558 --> 11:11:00,445
So for my lateral bound with dumbbell punch, I'm going to go with the light dumbbell.

7385
11:11:00,485 --> 11:11:03,691
Most of you will go five, maybe up to 10 pounds.

7386
11:11:04,112 --> 11:11:06,256
So I'm just going to go a lateral bound.

7387
11:11:06,316 --> 11:11:09,201
So you guys know the regular lateral bound.

7388
11:11:09,582 --> 11:11:11,405
But now I'm going to go opposite.

7389
11:11:11,465 --> 11:11:17,436
So as I push out and as I land on that left leg, I'm punching across.

7390
11:11:17,416 --> 11:11:34,952
with this dumbbell and i'm trying to do it pretty forcefully so the harder i punch with the dumbbell the more force i got going down in the ground the more i have to absorb with this left leg and then the more i have to redirect and push in that direction so you'll notice with the dumbbell it's a punch

7391
11:11:34,932 --> 11:11:36,013
and then it's a pull.

7392
11:11:36,354 --> 11:11:45,065
So a punch, and then I pull it to the side of my chest, and now all that additional force for absorption and redirection is on that left leg.

7393
11:11:45,105 --> 11:11:46,486
So I'll give you a slow motion here.

7394
11:11:46,546 --> 11:11:53,074
It's bam, push, absorb, push, absorb, push, absorb, push.

7395
11:11:54,116 --> 11:11:58,341
Notice I'm not just going with the arm, I'm actually dipping the shoulder.

7396
11:11:58,321 --> 11:12:02,026
So I'm getting a little bit of rotational power in there.

7397
11:12:02,066 --> 11:12:06,212
So it's rotation, drive out, rotation, drive out.

7398
11:12:06,592 --> 11:12:09,837
Now this exercise takes a lot of coordination and a lot of timing.

7399
11:12:09,857 --> 11:12:16,866
If we can't get that down with the dumbbell, it's okay to just go with no weights and just use your hand and do it in the same way.

7400
11:12:17,227 --> 11:12:19,570
That reach is still beneficial because

7401
11:12:19,550 --> 11:12:24,157
We got to be able to stabilize that knee when our upper body is rotating, right?

7402
11:12:24,177 --> 11:12:26,360
Because that's where a lot of injuries happen on the court.

7403
11:12:26,841 --> 11:12:35,573
It's not when we're in this perfect posture, it's when we're in these positions and we're rotating with our upper body and we have rotational forces.

7404
11:12:35,613 --> 11:12:37,116
That's when a lot of knee injuries happen.

7405
11:12:37,536 --> 11:12:44,967
So we got to get used to being able to absorb and explode while our upper body is moving in space.

7406
11:12:55,544 --> 11:12:59,452
So for our box drop med ball toss, we're going to hold a med ball.

7407
11:12:59,512 --> 11:13:00,915
Now work with what you've got.

7408
11:13:01,075 --> 11:13:04,763
So I like to go 20 up to about 30 pounds here.

7409
11:13:05,685 --> 11:13:09,753
If you have lighter, that's okay because we are getting a drop from the box.

7410
11:13:09,774 --> 11:13:12,439
So we're getting some good eccentric loading.

7411
11:13:12,419 --> 11:13:15,866
I like to go in a box around knee height or just below knee height.

7412
11:13:16,227 --> 11:13:19,954
Now, if you're not as advanced, go in a smaller box with a lighter weight.

7413
11:13:20,195 --> 11:13:22,659
If you're more advanced, we can start to raise that box up.

7414
11:13:22,960 --> 11:13:26,968
I wouldn't go too much higher than knee height for this exercise though.

7415
11:13:28,062 --> 11:13:31,728
So all I'm gonna do is just hold it here, right in front of my belly button.

7416
11:13:32,088 --> 11:13:33,350
I'm gonna drop down.

7417
11:13:33,791 --> 11:13:41,964
As soon as my feet land, I end up arms extended, and then I gotta transition out of the bottom as fast as I can, toss as high as I can.

7418
11:13:42,365 --> 11:13:43,827
So it's drop,

7419
11:13:43,958 --> 11:14:10,084
load up toss as high as we can we will get a little bit of a jump naturally but I don't want you to consciously think about jumping so you might come to your toes and leave the ground just a couple inches all I want you to really think about is transitioning from eccentric to concentric as fast as you can and tossing this ball as high as you possibly can every rep compete with yourself try to get it higher and higher and higher

7420
11:14:10,064 --> 11:14:14,950
Now, of course, anytime we're throwing something overhead, we got to make sure that we get out of the way.

7421
11:14:15,051 --> 11:14:18,595
So don't be distracted and throw it up and have it come down and hit you in the head.

7422
11:14:18,976 --> 11:14:19,877
It's very dangerous.

7423
11:14:19,897 --> 11:14:25,384
So throw it up, step out of the way, keep your eye on it the whole time so that you can see it drop.

7424
11:14:25,685 --> 11:14:32,173
Make sure nobody else is in the way because it could be very dangerous if you're throwing this in a super crowded place.

7425
11:14:32,153 --> 11:14:37,219
If you're in a gym that's way too crowded to do this, I want you to just jump with it.

7426
11:14:37,539 --> 11:14:42,765
So we're just going to hold a light medicine ball right by the chest, or you can even hug it.

7427
11:14:43,126 --> 11:14:49,533
Sometimes I like to hug it here, cross the arms, and then just drop, land, and jump.

7428
11:14:49,974 --> 11:14:54,840
So that's your option if you're in a place that's too crowded to actually throw it overhead.

7429
11:14:55,260 --> 11:14:56,001
Let's do it.

7430
11:14:59,035 --> 11:15:16,739
Now for our freestyle dunks, I put this in there because it's so important that you get out there and just allow your body to explore different approaches, different type of dunks, different type of jumping styles without me always trying to put you in a box and trying to get you to do one thing.

7431
11:15:17,079 --> 11:15:22,647
So I want you to set the clock for 10 minutes and I just want you to go get as many dunks as you can.

7432
11:15:22,627 --> 11:15:24,590
Take breaks in between if you need to.

7433
11:15:24,630 --> 11:15:27,175
I do want you to be recovered in between reps.

7434
11:15:27,195 --> 11:15:29,238
This isn't an endurance workout.

7435
11:15:29,599 --> 11:15:30,921
So get up off one foot.

7436
11:15:30,981 --> 11:15:31,802
Throw it down.

7437
11:15:32,263 --> 11:15:32,844
Walk back.

7438
11:15:32,884 --> 11:15:35,008
Recover for 30 seconds to a minute.

7439
11:15:35,348 --> 11:15:35,989
Come back in.

7440
11:15:36,129 --> 11:15:37,251
Take off off two.

7441
11:15:37,692 --> 11:15:38,914
Try to dunk left.

7442
11:15:38,894 --> 11:15:41,978
Whatever you want to do, get creative and do it.

7443
11:15:42,219 --> 11:15:46,265
Of course, if you can't dunk and all you can do is touch the bottom of the net, I don't care.

7444
11:15:46,305 --> 11:15:47,547
I still want you to get creative.

7445
11:15:47,927 --> 11:15:49,409
Come in off two and touch the net.

7446
11:15:49,770 --> 11:15:52,654
Come from baseline, get up off one and touch the net.

7447
11:15:52,674 --> 11:15:55,077
Try to jump off left, touch with the left.

7448
11:15:56,099 --> 11:16:05,172
Variability, variety is the key to longevity and it's super important for building kind of well-rounded explosiveness and athleticism.

7449
11:16:05,152 --> 11:16:09,947
and so I want you to get creative, set the clock for 10 minutes, and just freestyle dunk.

7450
11:16:35,122 --> 11:16:39,167
For our 7-11 breathing, what we're going to do is just lay down on our back.

7451
11:16:39,287 --> 11:16:41,069
Make sure that you're in a relaxed place.

7452
11:16:41,129 --> 11:16:43,832
I know you're probably in a gym, so it might be a little bit loud.

7453
11:16:43,873 --> 11:16:50,380
If you have headphones, throw on some headphones, throw on some slow music, maybe some yoga or meditation type music.

7454
11:16:50,901 --> 11:16:56,848
And all I'm going to do is just lay down and I'm going to breathe in through my nose for seven seconds.

7455
11:16:57,128 --> 11:17:00,893
And I'm also going to breathe out through my nose for 11 seconds.

7456
11:17:00,873 --> 11:17:04,759
So I'm not going to open my mouth for this whole drill.

7457
11:17:05,200 --> 11:17:09,546
So it's in through the nose and I want to make sure that my stomach is rising.

7458
11:17:09,607 --> 11:17:16,958
Your chest will naturally rise a little bit, but most of you when you think of deep breathing, what happens is your belly stays still.

7459
11:17:17,950 --> 11:17:20,673
and your chest puffs up and your shoulders elevate.

7460
11:17:21,034 --> 11:17:27,742
That means we are not actually getting all of that air, all of that oxygen down to the deepest part of the lungs.

7461
11:17:28,303 --> 11:17:34,090
So I want you to think about letting the belly rise as you take that breath in, okay?

7462
11:17:34,110 --> 11:17:37,775
So we're here, in deep through the nose, let the stomach rise.

7463
11:17:40,058 --> 11:17:44,363
Seven seconds, once you finish that seven seconds, it's out through the nose.

7464
11:17:47,296 --> 11:17:49,198
and that stomach will fall, okay?

7465
11:17:49,919 --> 11:17:52,562
Initially, this is very uncomfortable for guys.

7466
11:17:53,323 --> 11:18:03,013
I've had NBA players that absolutely hated this until they're in their third or fourth session and they started to get used to it because you do have to learn how to pace your breaths.

7467
11:18:03,134 --> 11:18:10,902
If you just breathe in as hard as you can and breathe out as hard as you can, you're not gonna be able to go for seven in and 11 out.

7468
11:18:11,142 --> 11:18:15,227
You gotta learn to go very slow and pace that breath, okay?

7469
11:18:15,207 --> 11:18:44,067
this is doing a lot of stuff I mean for one we're helping you expand the lungs we're teaching you how to to breathe yourself into a more calmer state but from a recovery standpoint this could possibly be the best thing that you can do after a workout better than foam rolling better than static stretching because after a workout we're in that sympathetic state that's that fight that's that workout that's that game mode okay I gotta get you to the parasympathetic state that's relax recover all recovery

7470
11:18:44,317 --> 11:18:46,822
happens in the parasympathetic state.

7471
11:18:47,363 --> 11:18:51,491
Okay, so if I'm still hyped up after the workout, I'm killing my recovery.

7472
11:18:51,852 --> 11:19:05,498
So as soon as we're done with the workout, we wanna do these breathing exercises to get us into that parasympathetic state, and then I can really start to aid my recovery, and I'm back better than ever tomorrow, ready to train again.

7473
11:19:07,283 --> 11:19:10,588
So the first one for our static stretch is just going to be a basic quad stretch.

7474
11:19:10,608 --> 11:19:14,894
So I'm just going to go heel to hip and I'm just going to get up nice and tall.

7475
11:19:15,174 --> 11:19:21,984
I'm going to raise my opposite hand and I'm just going to hold for 15 seconds and then I'm going to switch over to the other side.

7476
11:19:22,285 --> 11:19:25,770
If you need to hold on to something for balance, that's OK.

7477
11:19:26,050 --> 11:19:33,561
We're not going to get the same arm raise, but you can hold on and just make sure that we're nice and tall and that heel is touching the hip the whole time.

7478
11:19:33,541 --> 11:19:37,892
For the elevated hamstring stretch, I'm just gonna use a bench, a box, a chair.

7479
11:19:38,313 --> 11:19:40,298
I'm just gonna get my heel on there.

7480
11:19:40,318 --> 11:19:42,804
That toe is pointed up towards the ceiling.

7481
11:19:43,105 --> 11:19:45,430
And then I'm just gonna hinge from the hips.

7482
11:19:45,450 --> 11:19:47,676
So I don't wanna lean forward and round my back.

7483
11:19:47,957 --> 11:19:49,761
I'm just gonna lean forward.

7484
11:19:49,741 --> 11:20:10,483
from the hips keeping my back nice and straight if you want to reach down and touch your ankle or touch your toe you can but don't reach down and start to bend over from the back so i like to just keep my hands here to make sure that i'm not rounding the upper back and i'm just going to hold 15 seconds and then i'm going to switch over to the other side

7485
11:20:10,835 --> 11:20:12,798
15 seconds on the other side as well.

7486
11:20:12,818 --> 11:20:14,941
We should feel this stretch all in the hamstrings.

7487
11:20:15,142 --> 11:20:16,564
So that is the back of the thigh.

7488
11:20:16,804 --> 11:20:21,111
We'll feel it a little bit down into the calves, but we should feel it mostly hamstrings.

7489
11:20:21,131 --> 11:20:24,816
For our adductor stretch, I'm just going to go one leg out.

7490
11:20:24,977 --> 11:20:27,400
I need to lock out this knee so I'm nice and straight.

7491
11:20:27,741 --> 11:20:30,064
I'm going to sit back onto my heel.

7492
11:20:30,425 --> 11:20:31,987
So now look at this back foot.

7493
11:20:32,007 --> 11:20:33,670
I'm not curling the toe under.

7494
11:20:33,650 --> 11:20:37,496
I'm putting it down like this so the top of my foot is flat to the floor.

7495
11:20:38,057 --> 11:20:41,322
And I'm going to sit my hips back to that heel.

7496
11:20:41,742 --> 11:20:47,070
Now from there, I can already feel a little bit of a stretch in the adductor.

7497
11:20:47,411 --> 11:21:00,771
Now if you don't really try to square your chest towards the floor, now from there, if you don't feel a big stretch already, we're going to come down to the elbows and we're just going to hang out in this position for 15 seconds.

7498
11:21:00,751 --> 11:21:03,940
Alright, so I should feel that stretch all through the adductors.

7499
11:21:03,980 --> 11:21:05,303
That's the inside of the leg.

7500
11:21:05,784 --> 11:21:09,173
After 15 seconds, I'm gonna switch over to that other side.

7501
11:21:09,755 --> 11:21:10,457
Same thing.

7502
11:21:10,778 --> 11:21:13,685
For my glute stretch, I'm gonna pull this knee back.

7503
11:21:13,966 --> 11:21:17,275
Now make sure that this other leg stays down on the floor.

7504
11:21:17,255 --> 11:21:21,240
So I need my right knee and my right heel down through the ground.

7505
11:21:21,520 --> 11:21:29,170
I'm not going to lift off and I'm just going to lay my head back and just pull this knee as far towards the chest as I can.

7506
11:21:29,551 --> 11:21:35,038
Now, a lot of you, as you pull, the tendency is to rise here because we're tight in the hip flexors.

7507
11:21:35,438 --> 11:21:40,765
If that's the case, try to have somebody hold that leg down or strap it down with a band.

7508
11:21:40,745 --> 11:21:45,490
or just realize that you don't have that range of motion yet and you can only pull to right here.

7509
11:21:45,891 --> 11:21:53,539
But this is a glute stretch for this left leg, but at the same time, for a lot of you, this will be a hip flexor stretch on that right side.

7510
11:21:54,040 --> 11:21:56,843
So I'm just gonna pull back, hold for 15 seconds.

7511
11:21:57,283 --> 11:22:03,310
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side, trying to get full range of motion with that other leg.

7512
11:22:03,290 --> 11:22:06,353
So for our hip flexor stretch, make sure that we have something soft.

7513
11:22:06,433 --> 11:22:08,595
I don't want you guys putting your knee on a hardwood.

7514
11:22:08,835 --> 11:22:12,478
Make sure you have a pad or a soft floor to do this stretch on.

7515
11:22:12,959 --> 11:22:14,540
So I'm just going to go on one knee.

7516
11:22:14,560 --> 11:22:17,463
This knee is going to go 90 degrees.

7517
11:22:17,523 --> 11:22:18,464
So I'm 90 there.

7518
11:22:18,804 --> 11:22:21,587
My ankle is directly underneath that knee.

7519
11:22:21,947 --> 11:22:24,249
Now from here, I just got to get up nice and tall.

7520
11:22:24,610 --> 11:22:29,294
Some of you are already going to feel a stretch in the hip flexor because we're extra tight.

7521
11:22:29,634 --> 11:22:32,757
Now from there, I'm just going to lean forward.

7522
11:22:32,737 --> 11:22:35,682
So I should have this knee back behind the hip.

7523
11:22:36,042 --> 11:22:40,810
And now from there, I'm just raising straight up and I'm going to hold.

7524
11:22:40,850 --> 11:22:42,293
All right.

7525
11:22:42,313 --> 11:22:48,182
So I feel a big stretch from here all the way down through the bottom of that hip flexor.

7526
11:22:48,924 --> 11:22:52,770
After 15 seconds, I'm going to switch over to that other side and do the same thing.

7527
11:22:52,750 --> 11:22:58,058
For my calf stretch, I'm basically going to do what they would call a downward dog in yoga.

7528
11:22:58,439 --> 11:23:01,664
So I'm here, I'm going to push back like this.

7529
11:23:01,764 --> 11:23:04,929
I'm going to straighten out my arms and now I'm just going to cross over.

7530
11:23:05,330 --> 11:23:15,045
So I'm going to put my left foot over that right foot and I'm going to try to get that right heel down towards the floor or as close as I can.

7531
11:23:15,346 --> 11:23:21,832
So I do have a straight knee, so we're stretching out what's called the gastrocnemius, that's the outside calf muscle.

7532
11:23:22,113 --> 11:23:28,259
So I shouldn't feel the stretch as much down in the ankle and the Achilles as we would on some of our hip mobility drills.

7533
11:23:28,659 --> 11:23:32,743
We should feel it on the outside of that calf muscle.

7534
11:23:33,925 --> 11:23:37,708
A lot of us aren't gonna be able to get our heel all the way to the floor, that's okay.

7535
11:23:38,089 --> 11:23:41,272
Just work on getting it down as low as we can.

7536
11:23:41,752 --> 11:23:45,336
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side.

7537
11:23:47,999 --> 11:23:53,245
What's up guys, quick minimum dose advice for phase nine, day two and day five.

7538
11:23:53,566 --> 11:23:57,310
So this is our lower body strength day, already very efficient.

7539
11:23:58,872 --> 11:24:03,357
Definitely skip the foam roller circuit if you're short on time.

7540
11:24:03,798 --> 11:24:06,201
Always do the lateral step core stiffness.

7541
11:24:06,681 --> 11:24:09,545
All of these next exercises we have to do.

7542
11:24:10,085 --> 11:24:15,812
If you have to skip one of the strength exercises, you could skip the band stability ball hamstring curl.

7543
11:24:15,792 --> 11:24:17,014
Love that exercise.

7544
11:24:17,314 --> 11:24:19,137
But if you're short on time, cut that out.

7545
11:24:19,577 --> 11:24:23,683
And then if you're short on time, cut out the rear foot elevated foot pops.

7546
11:24:24,324 --> 11:24:26,207
So that one is a lower priority.

7547
11:24:26,688 --> 11:24:32,636
Very great for building strength in the ankle and in the foot and building that functional stiffness that we need.

7548
11:24:33,217 --> 11:24:35,721
But if you're short on time, cut that out.

7549
11:24:35,741 --> 11:24:39,005
And then of course, if you're short on time, cut out that static stretch.

7550
11:24:39,386 --> 11:24:40,247
Let's do it.

7551
11:24:40,362 --> 11:24:41,906
We're going to get through a foam roller circuit.

7552
11:24:42,046 --> 11:24:43,730
I have a long roller from Skills.

7553
11:24:43,991 --> 11:24:50,868
You can do long or you can do one of the shorter rollers that you can get from Skills online, or you can just get it from Walmart or Target.

7554
11:24:51,229 --> 11:24:56,582
So the first muscle that we're going to focus on is the glutes, one of the most important muscles for us to foam roll.

7555
11:24:56,562 --> 11:25:22,738
so you could either go this way or you could go vertical so if you go this way we're just going to lean over to one side and then i'm just going to roll from the bottom of my glute all the way up to the top of my glute now always if we want more pressure we could cross over here and add a little more pressure to make it a little tougher or we could go vertical here and then we could lean over and get the glute horizontally as well

7556
11:25:22,718 --> 11:25:25,041
So the next one we're going to move down the posterior chain.

7557
11:25:25,081 --> 11:25:26,483
We're going to focus on the hamstrings.

7558
11:25:26,824 --> 11:25:35,216
So I'm just going to sit on the roller and I'm going to cross over this foot and I'm just going to roll from the bottom of my glute all the way to the top of my knee.

7559
11:25:35,596 --> 11:25:47,393
So I'm just going to start in the center and then I'm gradually going to rock over a little bit so I can get the outside of my hamstrings and then I'm going to rock to the inside so I can get the inside of my hamstrings.

7560
11:25:47,626 --> 11:25:49,388
Now the next one we're going to do is the calves.

7561
11:25:49,688 --> 11:25:53,091
So we're just going to cross over and I'm going to push myself up.

7562
11:25:53,192 --> 11:26:01,400
So my hips are off the ground and I'm just going to roll basically from the bottom of the knee all the way up to the top of the ankle.

7563
11:26:01,460 --> 11:26:06,985
So we're going over that calf and also over that Achilles and our next one we're flipping over.

7564
11:26:07,025 --> 11:26:10,229
We're going hip flexor all the way down to the quad.

7565
11:26:10,249 --> 11:26:17,616
So I'm going to go on the side of the roller now and I'm just going to come down into a plank position and I'm going to roll

7566
11:26:17,596 --> 11:26:40,262
from that hip flexor all the way down towards the top of my thigh so i'm getting my whole quad in this one and if you can't get down to the quad muscles around your knee then start here and finish and then you would scoot up and then just focus on those lower quad muscles down around the knee

7567
11:26:40,242 --> 11:26:43,148
Our next one is going to be for the adductors, that's the inside of the leg.

7568
11:26:43,329 --> 11:26:45,092
So a lot of different ways that we can do this.

7569
11:26:45,393 --> 11:26:59,162
The way that I like to go is I like to just turn that roller here, come in a plank position, bring this foot up, and I'm just rolling from the inside, the top of the knee, all the way up through the groin area.

7570
11:27:00,931 --> 11:27:07,742
So we could go bent leg there or we could go straight leg there for a little bit deeper of a roll.

7571
11:27:07,942 --> 11:27:11,508
So after we're done with the foam rolling circuit, I like to get out a lacrosse ball.

7572
11:27:11,809 --> 11:27:15,074
You could use a golf ball, a baseball, anything hard.

7573
11:27:15,615 --> 11:27:18,319
And I'm just gonna really dig into that heel.

7574
11:27:18,339 --> 11:27:20,022
So I'm gonna apply some pressure in there.

7575
11:27:20,323 --> 11:27:24,289
I'm gonna go from the heel all the way down through the ball of the foot.

7576
11:27:24,269 --> 11:27:27,254
and I'm gonna really loosen up that fascia.

7577
11:27:27,815 --> 11:27:38,734
A lot of times our fascia of the feet take a lot of excess stress because we're on our feet all day, we're moving, we're cutting, we're jumping, we gotta really start to loosen that up.

7578
11:27:40,115 --> 11:27:44,768
Now after that, it's optional if you want to go up and work on the smaller muscles of the hip.

7579
11:27:45,029 --> 11:27:48,538
You can work on the smaller muscles of the shoulder up against a wall if you'd like to.

7580
11:27:48,558 --> 11:27:53,752
I just want to make sure that we get that foam roll circuit and we get that lacrosse ball on the feet.

7581
11:27:54,113 --> 11:27:55,778
Everything else is extra credit.

7582
11:27:58,846 --> 11:28:02,592
So the first thing we're gonna do for our dynamic warmup is stationary skips.

7583
11:28:02,873 --> 11:28:05,457
Now for all of these, you can take them on the move if you want.

7584
11:28:05,517 --> 11:28:09,484
For right now, I'm just gonna do them stationary, just in case you don't have much room.

7585
11:28:09,985 --> 11:28:16,596
So we're just going up with the right, up with the left, just like we're running, and vice versa on that other side.

7586
11:28:16,936 --> 11:28:20,622
All right, I'm staying stiff with the feet, so I'm not letting my heel collapse.

7587
11:28:20,642 --> 11:28:22,305
I wanna stay on the ball of the foot.

7588
11:28:22,285 --> 11:28:25,530
and I'm just gonna go about 50% of my max speed.

7589
11:28:25,871 --> 11:28:27,353
I'm not going too fast yet.

7590
11:28:27,653 --> 11:28:29,797
We're gonna go for 30 seconds on the skips.

7591
11:28:30,057 --> 11:28:34,584
For the seal jacks, it's basically like a jumping jack except I'm gonna coordinate arms with the legs.

7592
11:28:34,604 --> 11:28:38,791
So I'm gonna go over with the right and over with the right hand at the same time.

7593
11:28:39,192 --> 11:28:42,757
Back to neutral, over with the left, over with the left hand.

7594
11:28:43,058 --> 11:28:45,301
And then I'm just gonna speed that up.

7595
11:28:45,321 --> 11:28:47,685
I'm gonna get a good little rhythm going here.

7596
11:28:47,665 --> 11:28:52,974
maybe somewhere between 30 and 50 percent of your max speed, so we're not all out.

7597
11:28:53,415 --> 11:28:54,997
We're just getting that blood flowing.

7598
11:28:55,298 --> 11:28:56,640
We're going to go for 30 seconds.

7599
11:28:56,840 --> 11:29:01,167
For the over-under hamstring stretch, I'm just going to go over with the left leg.

7600
11:29:01,508 --> 11:29:03,291
I'm going to come down, touch the toe.

7601
11:29:03,371 --> 11:29:12,947
Now, if you can't touch the toe without rounding the back, then just go mid-shin or even to the knees, just as low as we can, but we don't want to go to the point where we have to round our back.

7602
11:29:12,927 --> 11:29:20,642
OK, so I'm going to get down, touch my toes back to neutral, and then I cross over the other way and I'm going the other side.

7603
11:29:24,318 --> 11:29:28,705
All right, we're going to go five over and back, so it's 10 total touches.

7604
11:29:28,885 --> 11:29:34,214
For the quad hamstring leans, I'm just going to go into a quad stretch, so I'm going to pull my right foot up.

7605
11:29:34,494 --> 11:29:39,722
I want to make sure that my heel is touching my hip in that position, and I'm not out like this.

7606
11:29:39,803 --> 11:29:41,045
I'm keeping that knee in.

7607
11:29:41,465 --> 11:29:49,498
Now from there, I'm going to keep the left knee straight, and I'm just going to go into a lean as low as I can.

7608
11:29:49,478 --> 11:30:11,335
so i'm getting a really good stretch in the quad by going down and getting my knee back i'm getting it into the hip flexor a little bit more and i'm getting this hamstring a good stretch and i'm also working on my balance at the same time i'm going to go five leans and then i'm going to switch over five leans on the other side for the hip opener we're going to go push up position

7609
11:30:12,243 --> 11:30:15,868
I'm going to go left leg up outside this left hand.

7610
11:30:16,289 --> 11:30:20,735
Now from here, I'm just going to rotate up and hold one, two, three.

7611
11:30:20,795 --> 11:30:23,079
Now I'm going to go elbow down towards the floor.

7612
11:30:23,399 --> 11:30:25,422
We might not be able to touch the elbow to the ground.

7613
11:30:25,462 --> 11:30:26,063
That's okay.

7614
11:30:26,384 --> 11:30:27,986
Let's just get as low as we can there.

7615
11:30:28,467 --> 11:30:29,408
One, two, three.

7616
11:30:29,388 --> 11:30:50,063
Three and back up so three there three there I'm gonna go five cycles and then I'm gonna switch to the other side five and five same thing for the adductor hip flexor combo I'm going lateral with one skip so it's one skip lateral and I'm going down I'm trying to touch this floor keep this knee straight because I want to get that

7617
11:30:50,043 --> 11:30:52,506
stretch on the inside of the leg in this adductor.

7618
11:30:52,827 --> 11:30:59,776
I'm going back with the hip like I would in a normal squat, and I'm getting nice and low, touch the floor, and I'm popping out to that other side.

