10089
15:11:32,991 --> 15:11:46,879
I want you to stay nice and rapid and bouncy because if you lose that speed and you lose that bouncy and that springiness, then we're getting away from the Achilles and we're getting more on to strictly using that calf muscle contraction.

10090
15:11:47,199 --> 15:11:50,586
We want the perfect combination of both on this exercise.

10091
15:11:51,007 --> 15:11:51,568
Let's do it.

10092
15:12:17,755 --> 15:12:21,799
For our 7-11 breathing, what we're going to do is just lay down on our back.

10093
15:12:21,900 --> 15:12:23,701
Make sure that you're in a relaxed place.

10094
15:12:23,742 --> 15:12:26,444
I know you're probably in a gym, so it might be a little bit loud.

10095
15:12:26,484 --> 15:12:32,992
If you have headphones, throw on some headphones, throw on some slow music, maybe some yoga or meditation type music.

10096
15:12:33,512 --> 15:12:39,479
And all I'm going to do is just lay down and I'm going to breathe in through my nose for seven seconds.

10097
15:12:39,739 --> 15:12:43,543
And I'm also going to breathe out through my nose for 11 seconds.

10098
15:12:43,523 --> 15:12:47,410
So I'm not going to open my mouth for this whole drill.

10099
15:12:47,831 --> 15:12:52,179
So it's in through the nose, and I want to make sure that my stomach is rising.

10100
15:12:52,239 --> 15:12:59,592
Your chest will naturally rise a little bit, but most of you, when you think of deep breathing, what happens is your belly stays still.

10101
15:13:00,567 --> 15:13:03,290
and your chest puffs up and your shoulders elevate.

10102
15:13:03,651 --> 15:13:10,378
That means we are not actually getting all of that air, all of that oxygen down to the deepest part of the lungs.

10103
15:13:10,939 --> 15:13:16,705
So I want you to think about letting the belly rise as you take that breath in, okay?

10104
15:13:16,725 --> 15:13:20,390
So we're here, in deep through the nose, let the stomach rise.

10105
15:13:22,692 --> 15:13:26,997
Seven seconds, once you finish that seven seconds, it's out through the nose.

10106
15:13:29,913 --> 15:13:31,836
and that stomach will fall, okay?

10107
15:13:32,557 --> 15:13:35,180
Initially, this is very uncomfortable for guys.

10108
15:13:35,941 --> 15:13:44,973
I've had NBA players that absolutely hated this until they were in their third or fourth session and they started to get used to it because you do have to learn how to pace your breath.

10109
15:13:45,754 --> 15:13:53,524
If you just breathe in as hard as you can and breathe out as hard as you can, you're not gonna be able to go for seven in and 11 out.

10110
15:13:53,785 --> 15:13:57,810
You gotta learn to go very slow and pace that breath, okay?

10111
15:13:57,790 --> 15:14:26,683
this is doing a lot of stuff I mean for one we're helping you expand the lungs we're teaching you how to to breathe yourself into a more calmer state but from a recovery standpoint this could possibly be the best thing that you could do after a workout better than foam rolling better than static stretching because after a workout we're in that sympathetic state that's that fight that's that workout that's that game mode okay I got to get you to the parasympathetic state that's relax recover all recovery

10112
15:14:26,933 --> 15:14:29,437
happens in the parasympathetic state.

10113
15:14:29,977 --> 15:14:34,124
Okay, so if I'm still hyped up after the workout, I'm killing my recovery.

10114
15:14:34,464 --> 15:14:48,064
So as soon as we're done with the workout, we wanna do these breathing exercises to get us into that parasympathetic state and then I can really start to aid my recovery and I'm back better than ever tomorrow, ready to train again.

10115
15:14:49,934 --> 15:14:53,220
So the first one for our static stretch is just going to be a basic quad stretch.

10116
15:14:53,240 --> 15:14:57,507
So I'm just going to go heel to hip and I'm just going to get up nice and tall.

10117
15:14:57,807 --> 15:15:04,619
I'm going to raise my opposite hand and I'm just going to hold for 15 seconds and then I'm going to switch over to the other side.

10118
15:15:04,899 --> 15:15:08,405
If you need to hold on to something for balance, that's okay.

10119
15:15:08,685 --> 15:15:16,178
We're not going to get the same arm raise, but you can hold on and just make sure that we're nice and tall and that heel is touching the hip the whole time.

10120
15:15:16,158 --> 15:15:20,509
For the elevated hamstring stretch, I'm just gonna use a bench, a box, a chair.

10121
15:15:20,930 --> 15:15:22,895
I'm just gonna get my heel on there.

10122
15:15:23,256 --> 15:15:25,441
That toe is pointed up towards the ceiling.

10123
15:15:25,722 --> 15:15:27,807
And then I'm just gonna hinge from the hips.

10124
15:15:28,087 --> 15:15:30,293
So I don't wanna lean forward and round my back.

10125
15:15:30,594 --> 15:15:32,378
I'm just gonna lean forward.

10126
15:15:32,358 --> 15:15:53,134
from the hips keeping my back nice and straight if you want to reach down and touch your ankle or touch your toe you can but don't reach down and start to bend over from the back so i like to just keep my hands here to make sure that i'm not rounding the upper back and i'm just going to hold 15 seconds and then i'm going to switch over to the other side

10127
15:15:53,468 --> 15:15:55,330
15 seconds on the other side as well.

10128
15:15:55,450 --> 15:15:57,573
We should feel this stretch all in the hamstrings.

10129
15:15:57,753 --> 15:15:59,195
So that is the back of the thigh.

10130
15:15:59,415 --> 15:16:03,620
We'll feel it a little bit down into the calves, but we should feel it mostly hamstrings.

10131
15:16:03,760 --> 15:16:07,444
For our adductor stretch, I'm just gonna go one leg out.

10132
15:16:07,585 --> 15:16:10,007
I need to lock out this knee so I'm nice and straight.

10133
15:16:10,368 --> 15:16:12,691
I'm gonna sit back onto my heel.

10134
15:16:13,031 --> 15:16:14,613
So now look at this back foot.

10135
15:16:14,633 --> 15:16:16,035
I'm not curling the toe under.

10136
15:16:16,435 --> 15:16:20,640
I'm putting it down like this so the top of my foot is flat to the floor.

10137
15:16:20,620 --> 15:16:23,946
and I'm gonna sit my hips back to that heel.

10138
15:16:24,367 --> 15:16:29,697
Now from there, I can already feel a little bit of a stretch in the adductor.

10139
15:16:30,017 --> 15:16:43,422
Now if you don't really try to square your chest towards the floor, now from there, if you don't feel a big stretch already, we're gonna come down to the elbows and we're just gonna hang out in this position for 15 seconds.

10140
15:16:43,402 --> 15:16:46,567
Alright, so I should feel that stretch all through the adductors.

10141
15:16:46,587 --> 15:16:47,929
That's the inside of the leg.

10142
15:16:48,410 --> 15:16:51,775
After 15 seconds, I'm gonna switch over to that other side.

10143
15:16:52,376 --> 15:16:53,057
Same thing.

10144
15:16:53,398 --> 15:16:56,282
For my glute stretch, I'm gonna pull this knee back.

10145
15:16:56,583 --> 15:16:59,908
Now make sure that this other leg stays down on the floor.

10146
15:16:59,888 --> 15:17:03,874
So I need my right knee and my right heel down through the ground.

10147
15:17:04,175 --> 15:17:11,806
I'm not gonna lift off and I'm just gonna lay my head back and just pull this knee as far towards the chest as I can.

10148
15:17:12,167 --> 15:17:17,655
Now a lot of you, as you pull, the tendency is to rise here because we're tight in the hip flexors.

10149
15:17:18,076 --> 15:17:23,584
If that's the case, try to have somebody hold that leg down or strap it down with a band

10150
15:17:23,564 --> 15:17:28,112
or just realize that you don't have that range of motion yet and you can only pull to right here.

10151
15:17:28,513 --> 15:17:36,166
But this is a glute stretch for this left leg, but at the same time, for a lot of you, this will be a hip flexor stretch on that right side.

10152
15:17:36,687 --> 15:17:39,472
So I'm just gonna pull back, hold for 15 seconds.

10153
15:17:39,913 --> 15:17:45,943
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side, trying to get full range of motion with that other leg.

10154
15:17:45,923 --> 15:17:48,986
So for our hip flexor stretch, make sure that we have something soft.

10155
15:17:49,046 --> 15:17:51,228
I don't want you guys putting your knee on a hardwood.

10156
15:17:51,468 --> 15:17:55,111
Make sure you have a pad or a soft floor to do this stretch on.

10157
15:17:55,592 --> 15:17:57,133
So I'm just going to go on one knee.

10158
15:17:57,554 --> 15:18:00,076
This knee is going to go 90 degrees.

10159
15:18:00,156 --> 15:18:01,097
So I'm 90 there.

10160
15:18:01,437 --> 15:18:04,220
My ankle is directly underneath that knee.

10161
15:18:04,580 --> 15:18:07,203
Now from here, I just got to get up nice and tall.

10162
15:18:07,223 --> 15:18:11,927
Some of you are already going to feel a stretch in the hip flexor because we're extra tight.

10163
15:18:12,267 --> 15:18:15,390
Now from there, I'm just going to lean forward

10164
15:18:15,370 --> 15:18:18,657
So I should have this knee back behind the hip.

10165
15:18:18,677 --> 15:18:23,426
And now from there, I'm just raising straight up and I'm going to hold.

10166
15:18:23,466 --> 15:18:24,929
All right.

10167
15:18:24,949 --> 15:18:30,821
So I feel a big stretch from here all the way down through the bottom of that hip flexor.

10168
15:18:31,562 --> 15:18:35,370
After 15 seconds, I'm going to switch over to that other side and do the same thing.

10169
15:18:35,350 --> 15:18:40,677
For my calf stretch, I'm basically going to do what they would call a downward dog in yoga.

10170
15:18:41,057 --> 15:18:44,282
So I'm here, I'm going to push back like this.

10171
15:18:44,382 --> 15:18:47,586
I'm going to straighten out my arms and now I'm just going to cross over.

10172
15:18:47,966 --> 15:18:57,679
So I'm going to put my left foot over that right foot and I'm going to try to get that right heel down towards the floor or as close as I can.

10173
15:18:57,980 --> 15:19:04,467
So I do have a straight knee, so we're stretching out what's called the gastrocnemius, that's the outside calf muscle.

10174
15:19:04,727 --> 15:19:10,894
So I shouldn't feel the stretch as much down in the ankle and the Achilles as we would on some of our hip mobility drills.

10175
15:19:11,275 --> 15:19:15,359
We should feel it on the outside of that calf muscle.

10176
15:19:16,540 --> 15:19:20,345
A lot of us aren't going to be able to get our heel all the way to the floor, that's okay.

10177
15:19:20,705 --> 15:19:23,929
Just work on getting it down as low as we can.

10178
15:19:23,949 --> 15:19:27,953
After 15 seconds, I'm switching over to that other side.

10179
15:19:30,582 --> 15:19:33,846
So quick minimum dose advice for day three and day six.

10180
15:19:34,146 --> 15:19:35,328
This is our core day.

10181
15:19:35,628 --> 15:19:38,211
We're going to get a little bit of mobility, but not too much.

10182
15:19:38,672 --> 15:19:41,716
As you can see, already extremely efficient.

10183
15:19:42,657 --> 15:19:46,702
If you want to add core exercises from previous phases, go ahead.

10184
15:19:47,503 --> 15:19:53,350
I've just made this one very, very short, straight to the point, since our other days are pretty tough.

10185
15:19:53,330 --> 15:19:58,419
I don't want you to kill yourself and drain your nervous system by doing way too much core work.

10186
15:19:59,000 --> 15:20:00,642
Cable dead bug, got to do it.

10187
15:20:00,682 --> 15:20:02,385
If you got to do that with a band, that's fine.

10188
15:20:02,906 --> 15:20:06,212
Elastic leg kick, do this even if you are flexible.

10189
15:20:07,194 --> 15:20:08,816
Hollow press, very important.

10190
15:20:09,638 --> 15:20:16,950
Kneeling hip series, this one is going to be challenging from a hip mobility standpoint, but also from a hip stability standpoint.

10191
15:20:17,391 --> 15:20:18,713
Definitely don't skip that.

10192
15:20:18,693 --> 15:20:21,316
Lateral step core stiffness, very important.

10193
15:20:21,777 --> 15:20:25,981
If you feel like you need a warmup for that, go through an additional lower body warmup.

10194
15:20:26,362 --> 15:20:31,768
Some people have creaky knees and they can't quite get into this intense little partial lunge.

10195
15:20:32,629 --> 15:20:37,154
So if you feel like you need to warm up for that, go ahead and do an extra dynamic warmup.

10196
15:20:37,655 --> 15:20:40,378
And then at the end of that, add whatever core you want.

10197
15:20:40,738 --> 15:20:44,523
And of course, if you want to add a third core day, that's completely fine.

10198
15:20:44,963 --> 15:20:45,544
Let's do it.

10199
15:20:53,236 --> 15:20:57,162
So for our cable dead bug, I'm using a bench and a cable machine right now.

10200
15:20:57,462 --> 15:20:58,283
You don't need the bench.

10201
15:20:58,303 --> 15:21:20,374
You could go on the floor with the cable machine or if you don't have the cable machine or it's inconvenient in your gym, set up with a power rack or anything that you could hook a band around and you're just going to go on the floor and hold that band right here just so that you have to fire up your core, fire up your lats and stay nice and stable through that torso throughout this exercise.

10202
15:21:20,354 --> 15:21:24,158
What I'm going to do is reach back and grab the rope.

10203
15:21:24,178 --> 15:21:29,184
Notice I have it at a cable setting to where I can hold straight out.

10204
15:21:29,585 --> 15:21:33,329
If that's too low, then that line of pull is going to be really awkward.

10205
15:21:34,270 --> 15:21:35,511
So I'm holding right here.

10206
15:21:35,571 --> 15:21:37,814
I got to engage my lats and engage my core.

10207
15:21:38,295 --> 15:21:40,157
And then I'm going up with the feet.

10208
15:21:40,557 --> 15:21:44,742
My back is nice and flat so I don't have an exaggerated curve.

10209
15:21:44,722 --> 15:22:13,176
nice and flat and then I'm just going alternating all the way out back up and the other side all the way out back up all right you got to squeeze that core and keep that good neutral spine all the way through this exercise now you're not necessarily going to feel a burn of like a crunch or a sit-up but you should feel a little bit of a burn in the core more importantly this type of core strength and stability actually translates to the core

10210
15:22:25,441 --> 15:22:34,574
For the elastic leg kicks, I want you to think about a normal, kind of like a Frankenstein kick, except we're gonna make it a little bit more rapid and a little bit more elastic.

10211
15:22:34,594 --> 15:22:47,972
So I'm just gonna stay on the balls of the feet and I'm just gonna kick up my leg as high as I can, keeping that knee straight, and I'm just gonna switch every time so it ends up being a little bit of a skip and then a straight leg kick.

10212
15:22:47,952 --> 15:22:48,273
Okay.

10213
15:22:48,733 --> 15:22:50,556
Now I'm popping off the balls of the feet.

10214
15:22:51,077 --> 15:22:53,001
I do not want your heels to touch the floor.

10215
15:22:53,481 --> 15:22:56,166
And the reason why we're doing this, you're not going to get a huge burn.

10216
15:22:56,206 --> 15:22:57,608
This isn't a huge workout.

10217
15:22:57,969 --> 15:23:03,278
We're trying to get some elasticity back in the post chain, some elasticity in the hamstrings.

10218
15:23:03,258 --> 15:23:08,750
So a lot of people sit there and stretch or even do a normal dynamic warm-up for elasticity.

10219
15:23:09,131 --> 15:23:14,443
The thing is, for a muscle to actually increase elasticity, it has to be under one second.

10220
15:23:14,844 --> 15:23:19,174
So if I'm going slow with that kick or if I'm holding

10221
15:23:19,154 --> 15:23:40,437
a stretch it might increase what we call plasticity how flexible we get but not elasticity and elasticity is what actually translates to sprinting and jumping so everything has to be under one second and that's why we're going rapid with those kicks i want you to think about getting that leg up as quick as you can as high as you can

10222
15:23:51,233 --> 15:23:53,958
So for our hollow press, this is a core exercise.

10223
15:23:54,038 --> 15:23:55,480
It looks like I'm working my chest.

10224
15:23:55,801 --> 15:23:57,163
I'm not actually working my chest.

10225
15:23:57,183 --> 15:24:00,489
You will get a little pump in your pecs and your triceps and your shoulders.

10226
15:24:00,770 --> 15:24:02,312
Most importantly, this is for the core.

10227
15:24:02,372 --> 15:24:06,860
So whatever you would normally dumbbell bench press, we're going to go about half of that.

10228
15:24:06,940 --> 15:24:13,432
So if normally you would for 10, you rep out like 60s, I want you to go a 30 pound dumbbell.

10229
15:24:13,893 --> 15:24:14,153
All right.

10230
15:24:14,133 --> 15:24:16,577
position here and then I'm just leaning back.

10231
15:24:16,637 --> 15:24:22,686
I'm bringing my feet off the ground about six inches and now I'm bringing my shoulder off the ground about six inches.

10232
15:24:22,726 --> 15:24:26,371
So my lower back is flat to the ground and my butt is on the ground.

10233
15:24:26,752 --> 15:24:27,813
Nothing else is touching.

10234
15:24:28,655 --> 15:24:30,998
A lot of people make the mistake of going up here.

10235
15:24:31,058 --> 15:24:35,024
I need you laid down flat and then just come up a little bit.

10236
15:24:35,825 --> 15:24:39,010
From here, I'm going to touch my elbow to the floor.

10237
15:24:38,990 --> 15:24:41,657
And then I'm just going to press, lock out at the top.

10238
15:24:42,178 --> 15:24:42,519
All right.

10239
15:24:42,539 --> 15:24:49,518
So I'm challenging that anti-rotation and I'm challenging those front abs by holding in this position.

10240
15:24:50,079 --> 15:24:50,360
All right.

10241
15:24:50,420 --> 15:24:51,663
Keep it nice and slow.

10242
15:24:52,185 --> 15:24:55,834
Don't let yourself fly into rotation with that dumbbell.

10243
15:24:55,814 --> 15:25:04,289
So this is an exercise where we can load up as heavy as possible, but I do want you to start light and gradually increase as we go.

10244
15:25:04,850 --> 15:25:11,342
For most of us, like I said, you're gonna be about 50% of what you would normally hit a dumbbell bench press with.

10245
15:25:36,027 --> 15:25:39,491
Okay, so for my kneeling hip series, we're gonna use a band.

10246
15:25:39,872 --> 15:25:44,177
I like to hook two bands together so that I actually have a little more room.

10247
15:25:44,197 --> 15:25:51,605
Make sure whatever you're hooking the band to is nice and stable like a towel rack or a heavy couch or something that's not gonna be pulled along with the band.

10248
15:25:51,625 --> 15:25:56,571
Of course, the thicker we go with that band, the more difficult this is gonna be, okay?

10249
15:25:56,611 --> 15:25:59,294
And the further out we go, the more difficult it's gonna be.

10250
15:25:59,314 --> 15:26:03,199
So I would start with just light tension until you get used to this drill.

10251
15:26:03,938 --> 15:26:05,802
I use a pad so there's light on the knees.

10252
15:26:06,222 --> 15:26:10,511
I'm going to curl the toes and I'm going to sit my hips back.

10253
15:26:10,932 --> 15:26:14,939
First of all, right there, I'm getting some decent toe range motion, which is really important for us.

10254
15:26:15,360 --> 15:26:17,945
Now from here, I'm just going to explode forward.

10255
15:26:17,965 --> 15:26:19,849
So I'm going to come to full hip extension.

10256
15:26:19,869 --> 15:26:24,057
I'm going to squeeze my glutes for two seconds as hard as I can at the top.

10257
15:26:24,037 --> 15:26:29,066
Now from here, I'm going to bring this right foot out around and get that foot down.

10258
15:26:29,387 --> 15:26:31,310
So I'm going to try not to lean the shoulders.

10259
15:26:31,350 --> 15:26:35,618
Try to stay level, stable with the shoulders and with the hips.

10260
15:26:36,319 --> 15:26:37,561
And I'm bringing it around.

10261
15:26:38,242 --> 15:26:39,645
Get that foot flat.

10262
15:26:39,665 --> 15:26:43,893
And then from here, I'm driving out and I'm going to squeeze the right foot down.

10263
15:26:43,913 --> 15:26:45,235
Drive out.

10264
15:26:45,215 --> 15:26:49,120
Get this leg parallel to the floor and squeeze this right glute.

10265
15:26:49,220 --> 15:26:50,502
Hold for two.

10266
15:26:50,522 --> 15:26:52,765
And we're right back down.

10267
15:26:52,785 --> 15:26:53,866
So it's here.

10268
15:26:53,906 --> 15:26:55,228
Extend.

10269
15:26:55,468 --> 15:26:56,009
Squeeze.

10270
15:26:56,249 --> 15:26:56,830
One, two.

10271
15:26:57,791 --> 15:26:59,093
Right foot up.

10272
15:26:59,113 --> 15:26:59,874
Drive out.

10273
15:26:59,954 --> 15:27:00,855
Squeeze.

10274
15:27:01,256 --> 15:27:01,977
One, two.

10275
15:27:02,457 --> 15:27:04,540
And then we're right back down.

10276
15:27:04,520 --> 15:27:08,445
This is challenging our hip stability in so many different ways.

10277
15:27:08,465 --> 15:27:12,530
We're activating our glutes with that explosive extension.

10278
15:27:12,550 --> 15:27:14,673
We're getting some toe range of motion.

10279
15:27:14,693 --> 15:27:22,082
We're getting some lateral hip stability, those little tiny hip stabilizer muscles when we're on that half kneel and we're bringing that leg up.

10280
15:27:22,102 --> 15:27:26,127
So there's so many different aspects of hip stability going on here.

10281
15:27:26,367 --> 15:27:27,709
This drill is great.

10282
15:27:27,689 --> 15:27:44,095
for building a good solid base so we can add more explosiveness to it later on and then of course you're going to do the desired reps with the right foot going forward and then we're going to do the desired reps then with the left foot going forward so we always balance out each side

10283
15:27:56,528 --> 15:28:02,281
So for my lateral step core stiffness, what I'm gonna do is use a cable machine.

10284
15:28:02,641 --> 15:28:05,267
I'm gonna get that cable set at around hip height.

10285
15:28:05,628 --> 15:28:11,601
Now if you don't have a cable machine, you could just do these with a band, get it around something stable, around hip height.

10286
15:28:12,526 --> 15:28:16,251
Either one will work, but I like to use a cable machine because we can load up a little heavier.

10287
15:28:16,331 --> 15:28:18,774
So of course, as always, we start very light.

10288
15:28:19,114 --> 15:28:21,577
